{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:27:00.322Z","ordinal":68325,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac61e5318d887d08498a0ebc7762acf","status":"completed","call_id":"call_41ab9ef5270a49b0adbb35a249185907","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat packages/infrastructure/src/apps-stack.ts\\ncat apps/api/src/server.ts\\ncat node_modules/alchemy/src/Cloudflare/Workers/WorkerExecutionContext.ts 2>/dev/null\\nrg -n 'class WorkerExecutionContext|waitUntil:' node_modules/alchemy/src/Cloudflare/Workers/WorkerRuntime.ts\\ncat knip.production.json | head -135\\nsed -n '1,145p' packages/infrastructure/src/native-domains-provider.boundary.test.ts\",\"max_output_tokens\":5600}));\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit/packages/analytics/README.md\\n@@\\n-# `@taxkit/analytics`\\n-\\n-Effect service package with explicit contract, live, and deterministic test\\n-boundaries.\\n+---\\n+document_type: package-readme\\n+lifecycle: current\\n+authority: canonical\\n+owner: taxkit-analytics-owner\\n+last_reviewed: 2026-10-07\\n+review_trigger: analytics event, settings, service, export, transport or privacy change\\n+---\\n+\\n+# `@taxkit/analytics`\\n+\\n+Private compiled contracts for the accepted page visit and successful hosted\\n+calculator events. The current backend Layer sends only the catalogue ID and\\n+name, fixed application/stage labels, an event UUID and timestamp. It never\\n+accepts tax inputs, results, browser identity, request URLs or request headers.\\n+Tax rule packages and local SDK calculations do not depend on this package.\\n@@\\n - `./errors`: public typed failures.\\n+- `./config`: checked collection mode and capture settings. Off needs no token;\\n+  invalid enabled settings fail with `AnalyticsConfigurationError`.\\n@@\\n-## Documentation impact\\n-\\n-The package owns its semantic schemas and service contract. It does not own app\\n-runtime execution, transport adapters, or provider runbooks. Update the nearest\\n-repository architecture owner when a public schema or service operation changes;\\n-update its proof/critical-journey owner when observable behavior changes.\\n+The application supplies native `FetchHttpClient` and Effect `Crypto`. Each\\n+backend send owns one scope and one five-second limit covering identity,\\n+encoding, headers and the complete reply. Replies are limited to 64 KiB. A\\n+request has one attempt, omits credentials, disables trace propagation and\\n+refuses redirects. Disabled or denied collection makes no request and generates\\n+no UUID. `accepted` means a successful HTTP response; stored provider events\\n+require separate readback.\\n+\\n+The browser contract is shared so the Website adapter can keep its SDK private.\\n+That adapter, the Website relay and the single API application event owner are\\n+T008 work in progress. A test Layer is substitution proof, not SDK or browser\\n+privacy proof.\\n+\\n+## Documentation impact\\n+\\n+Change required: this README, the repository\\n+[package ownership](../../docs/architecture/package-ownership.md),\\n+[Effect boundary owner](../../docs/architecture/effect-services.md) and\\n+[active plan](../../docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md) route these\\n+contracts and pending application work. Preserve: tax Schemas, results, HTTP\\n+and SDK contracts, public accepted documentation and the five existing runbook\\n+procedures. This package is private and is not part of the published tax/SDK\\n+closure, so its addition alone needs no Changeset.\\n@@\\n-No operational runbook is required until this package acquires an external\\n-system or consequential operation.\\n+The [deployment runbook](../../docs/runbooks/docs-deployment.md) and\\n+[recovery runbook](../../docs/runbooks/recovery.md) own later analytics resource\\n+plans, authority, retained projects, recovery and readback. Tests use controlled\\n+transports and synthetic capture tokens; they perform no provider operation.\\n+Local and ordinary Preview collection must stay off. Production or a controlled\\n+Preview requires checked settings and separately qualified app composition.\\n@@\\n-These exports and tests do not prove app composition, transport behavior,\\n-provider state, deployment, or a packed publisher artifact.\\n+These package checks do not prove the real browser SDK, app composition,\\n+provider project ownership, ingestion, deployment, release publication or\\n+exactly-once storage. Shared Axiom metrics remain deferred by Cooper.\\n*** Update File: /Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit/docs/architecture/package-ownership.md\\n@@\\n - `packages/content`\\n+- `packages/analytics`\\n@@\\n `packages/content`\\n@@\\n   identity live in its Schema owner; RPC retains a distinct API identity.\\n+\\n+`packages/analytics`\\n+: Private compiled owner of checked page/calculator events, collection policy,\\n+  settings, safe errors and named browser/backend service contracts. Its native\\n+  backend capture Layer has one bounded HTTP attempt. The application owns\\n+  execution, best-effort delivery and successful-use placement; the Website\\n+  owns its private browser SDK and relay; infrastructure owns retained provider\\n+  projects. Calculators, rules and the local SDK have no analytics dependency.\\n+  T008 application and provider qualification remain in progress; package tests\\n+  alone do not prove browser privacy or ingestion.\\n*** Update File: /Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit/docs/architecture/effect-services.md\\n@@\\n ## Scope\\n@@\\n contracts live with their owning rule packages and should link back here.\\n+\\n+The private [analytics package](../../packages/analytics/README.md) owns the\\n+two accepted event contracts. Its native backend Layer encodes a fixed provider\\n+request and maps transport failures to safe errors. The exact encoder admission\\n+in `oxlint.config.ts` covers that provider egress and its safe error-byte test;\\n+it does not admit runtime execution, raw JSON or decoding in neighbouring code.\\n+The application owns when to capture and which checked collection policy applies.\\n+T008 browser/application composition and provider readback remain pending.\\n*** End Patch\"));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","create_time":1791368787.1216772}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:27:00.343Z","ordinal":68326,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","session_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","root_turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","response_id":"resp_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac61e3c22b487d0ab222cbf10d52451","usage":{"input_tokens":146122,"cached_input_tokens":140800,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1785,"reasoning_output_tokens":449,"total_tokens":147907},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":40062773,"cached_input_tokens":39227008,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":202732,"reasoning_output_tokens":78298,"total_tokens":40265505},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1276572975,"cached_input_tokens":1250250496,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":6340794,"reasoning_output_tokens":2828135,"total_tokens":1282913769}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:27:00.422Z","ordinal":68327,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-c86009f7-808b-4b76-adb8-b21a9afcefd6","process_id":"14101","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat packages/infrastructure/src/apps-stack.ts\ncat apps/api/src/server.ts\ncat node_modules/alchemy/src/Cloudflare/Workers/WorkerExecutionContext.ts 2>/dev/null\nrg -n 'class WorkerExecutionContext|waitUntil:' node_modules/alchemy/src/Cloudflare/Workers/WorkerRuntime.ts\ncat knip.production.json | head -135\nsed -n '1,145p' packages/infrastructure/src/native-domains-provider.boundary.test.ts"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"cat packages/infrastructure/src/apps-stack.ts\ncat apps/api/src/server.ts\ncat node_modules/alchemy/src/Cloudflare/Workers/WorkerExecutionContext.ts 2>/dev/null\nrg -n 'class WorkerExecutionContext|waitUntil:' node_modules/alchemy/src/Cloudflare/Workers/WorkerRuntime.ts\ncat knip.production.json | head -135\nsed -n '1,145p' packages/infrastructure/src/native-domains-provider.boundary.test.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"import { adopt } from \"alchemy/AdoptPolicy\";\nimport { ZoneDnsSettings } from \"alchemy/Cloudflare/DNS\";\nimport * as Website from \"alchemy/Cloudflare/Website\";\nimport { Worker } from \"alchemy/Cloudflare/Workers\";\nimport { Zone } from \"alchemy/Cloudflare/Zone\";\nimport * as Output from \"alchemy/Output\";\nimport { retain } from \"alchemy/RemovalPolicy\";\nimport { Stage } from \"alchemy/Stage\";\nimport type { CalculatorHostMode } from \"api/worker\";\nimport {\n  ApiWorkerNativeInit,\n  ApiWorkerObservability,\n  TaxKitApiWorker,\n} from \"api/worker\";\nimport { Context, Effect, Option } from \"effect\";\n\nimport { nativeAppsStage } from \"./apps-secrets.boundary.js\";\n\nexport const NativeAppsHostMode = Context.Reference<CalculatorHostMode>(\n  \"@taxkit/infrastructure/NativeAppsHostMode\",\n  { defaultValue: () => \"edge\" }\n);\n\nconst NativeProductionZone = Context.Reference<Option.Option<Zone>>(\n  \"@taxkit/infrastructure/NativeProductionZone\",\n  { defaultValue: Option.none }\n);\n\n// A forward API tag registers before its implementation Layer finishes. The\n// native planner retains both address Outputs, including the binding cycle.\nexport class TaxKitWebsite extends Website.Vite<TaxKitWebsite>()(\n  \"TaxKitWebsite\",\n  Effect.gen(function* () {\n    const api = yield* TaxKitApiWorker;\n    const apiOrigin = api.url.pipe(\n      Output.map((url) => Option.getOrNull(Option.fromNullishOr(url)))\n    );\n    return {\n      ...Option.match(yield* NativeProductionZone, {\n        onNone: () => ({}),\n        onSome: (zone) => ({\n          domain: {\n            name: \"taxkit.dev\",\n            redirects: [\"www.taxkit.dev\"],\n            zoneId: zone.zoneId,\n          },\n        }),\n      }),\n      compatibility: {\n        date: \"2026-10-04\",\n        flags: [\"nodejs_compat\"],\n      },\n      env: {\n        API_PUBLIC_ORIGIN: apiOrigin,\n        CALCULATOR_HOST_MODE: yield* NativeAppsHostMode,\n        TAXKIT_API: api,\n        WEBSITE_PUBLIC_ORIGIN: Worker.URL,\n      },\n      // The Website's platform records can include caller URLs independently\n      // of its fixed application reporter. Qualified exporters remain pending.\n      observability: {\n        enabled: false,\n        headSamplingRate: 0,\n        logs: {\n          enabled: false,\n          headSamplingRate: 0,\n          invocationLogs: false,\n          persist: false,\n        },\n        traces: { enabled: false, headSamplingRate: 0, persist: false },\n      },\n      rootDir: \"apps/web\",\n      workersDev: true,\n    };\n  })\n) {}\n\nconst NativeApiHostLive = TaxKitApiWorker.make(\n  Effect.gen(function* () {\n    const website = yield* TaxKitWebsite;\n    return {\n      ...Option.match(yield* NativeProductionZone, {\n        onNone: () => ({}),\n        onSome: (zone) => ({\n          domain: { name: \"api.taxkit.dev\", zoneId: zone.zoneId },\n        }),\n      }),\n      compatibility: {\n        date: \"2026-10-04\",\n        flags: [\"nodejs_compat\"],\n      },\n      env: {\n        API_PUBLIC_ORIGIN: Worker.URL,\n        CALCULATOR_HOST_MODE: yield* NativeAppsHostMode,\n        WEBSITE_PUBLIC_ORIGIN: website.url.pipe(\n          Output.map((url) => Option.getOrNull(Option.fromNullishOr(url)))\n        ),\n      },\n      // The app export owns its native entry; the graph crosses the workspace\n      // through that export rather than a relative filesystem import.\n      main: import.meta.resolve(\"api/worker\"),\n      observability: ApiWorkerObservability,\n      workersDev: true,\n    };\n  }),\n  ApiWorkerNativeInit\n);\n\nexport const declareNativeAppsStack = Effect.gen(function* () {\n  const stage = yield* nativeAppsStage(yield* Stage);\n  const zone =\n    stage === \"prod\"\n      ? Option.some(\n          yield* Zone(\"TaxKitProductionZone\", {\n            name: \"taxkit.dev\",\n            paused: false,\n            type: \"full\",\n          }).pipe(adopt(true), retain())\n        )\n      : Option.none<Zone>();\n  if (Option.isSome(zone)) {\n    // Preserve the DNS settings independently read on 7 October. This does\n    // not change DNSSEC, registrar, TLS, mail or verification records.\n    yield* ZoneDnsSettings(\"TaxKitProductionDnsSettings\", {\n      flattenAllCnames: false,\n      foundationDns: false,\n      multiProvider: false,\n      nameservers: { type: \"cloudflare.standard\" },\n      nsTtl: 86_400,\n      secondaryOverrides: false,\n      zoneId: zone.value.zoneId,\n      zoneMode: \"standard\",\n    }).pipe(retain());\n  }\n  return yield* Effect.gen(function* () {\n    const api = yield* TaxKitApiWorker;\n    const website = yield* TaxKitWebsite;\n    return