{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:49:58.827Z","ordinal":68663,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a43da49f-02a9-449b-8927-9d9bab6258f8","process_id":"97706","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat packages/analytics/package-structure.render.json; sed -n '1,130p' docs/README.md; sed -n '1,130p' .agents/skills/docs-maintainer/SKILL.md; sed -n '1,140p' .agents/skills/package-structure/scripts/validate_package.py"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat packages/analytics/package-structure.render.json","name":"package-structure.render.json","path":"packages/analytics/package-structure.render.json"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,130p' docs/README.md","name":"README.md","path":"docs/README.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,130p' .agents/skills/docs-maintainer/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":".agents/skills/docs-maintainer/SKILL.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,140p' .agents/skills/package-structure/scripts/validate_package.py","name":"validate_package.py","path":".agents/skills/package-structure/scripts/validate_package.py"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n  \"kind\": \"effect-service\",\n  \"packageName\": \"@taxkit/analytics\",\n  \"domainPackage\": null,\n  \"sourceCondition\": \"source\",\n  \"versionSnapshot\": {\n    \"resolvedAt\": \"2026-10-07\",\n    \"sha256\": \"263bd13f098099137c1ea2cd204e2920a41c5a8ddc22dba49724d9285aa80a12\"\n  },\n  \"officialSources\": {\n    \"effect\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/effect/4.0.0\",\n    \"vitest\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/vitest/5.0.3\",\n    \"typescript\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/typescript/7.0.2\"\n  },\n  \"selectedVersions\": {\n    \"effect\": \"4.0.0\",\n    \"@effect/vitest\": \"4.0.0\",\n    \"typescript\": \"7.0.2\",\n    \"vitest\": \"5.0.3\",\n    \"@effect/platform-bun\": \"4.0.0\"\n  },\n  \"compatibilityDecisions\": [\n    {\n      \"status\": \"qualified\",\n      \"decision\": \"Reuse TaxKit T002 stable Effect 4.0.0 dependency qualification and installed types; rendered source is a scaffold and needs real TaxKit type/lint/tests before acceptance\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"configDigests\": {\n    \"package.json\": \"1ee730f376aa3675eee314d99c24564d3dfaec5215387106cb46981dbafbf4ca\",\n    \"tsconfig.json\": \"71596163cd8ffea16eb4950049bc772ec8a8e2db408759c80bc8232aa40a6d99\",\n    \"tsconfig.build.json\": \"320b70b4115224df6a42038a8759a444d0feecabb0666c22a519904a1e9b9de9\",\n    \"vitest.config.ts\": \"8167d20931f3f88793a6253697dad0c2dc7a519ca7d4ec8aea6c2ffc9f1448b7\"\n  },\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"Structural rendering does not prove installed dependency, declaration, runtime, or packed-consumer behavior.\"\n  ],\n  \"nonClaims\": [\"Selected versions are not claimed to remain latest.\"]\n}\n---\ndocument_type: documentation-router\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: canonical\nowner: taxkit-documentation-owner\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-07\nreview_trigger: any maintainer/public docs class, root route, SPEC, plan, runbook, proof, evidence, or lifecycle change\n---\n\n# TaxKit documentation\n\nThis is the sole router for maintainer-document type, lifecycle, truth layers,\nand semantic ownership. Root `README.md` is the public repository entry point;\n`AGENTS.md` is the short task map; `docs/architecture/README.md` is the current\narchitecture route. Public documentation content is a separate product surface\nowned by the replacement `apps/web`, backend content contracts and docs\npackages. The old `apps/docs` workspace is retired. Its tombstone routes to the verified\nsource bundle and dated provider recovery records; no provider operation is\nauthorised by that retained history.\n\n## Truth layers\n\nUse the strongest applicable owner and link rather than copy:\n\n1. External systems own their current external state at readback time.\n2. Code, configuration, Schemas, package exports, workflows, and generated\n   sources own desired/executable state.\n3. Architecture and standards own durable boundaries and enforceable policy.\n4. Dated proof/evidence owns one artifact/environment/authority observation and\n   its limitations.\n5. Active SPEC/tasks and execution plans own current implementation intent.\n\nProvider/registry output cannot grant authority. Completed plans are history.\nLocal release checks do not prove npm publication or external consumers.\n\n## Metadata and lifecycle\n\nNew or materially revised maintainer docs separate `document_type`,\n`lifecycle`, `authority`, and `owner`. Current durable docs also record\n`last_reviewed` and `review_trigger`; superseded/tombstone docs record a\nsuccessor and reason.\n\nLifecycle values are `proposed`, `current`, `implemented`, `superseded`,\n`historical`, `evidence`, `reference`, `failed`, `inconclusive`, `tombstone`,\nand `archived`. Authority values are `canonical`, `supporting`, `generated`,\nand `external`. Legacy `status: canonical` is an authority marker, not a\nlifecycle; migrate it only when its owner is materially revised.\n\n## Routes\n\n| Need | Owner | Use |\n|---|---|---|\n| Architecture | [`architecture/README.md`](architecture/README.md) | Current architecture route. `architecture.md` is a tombstone only. |\n| Standards | [`standards/README.md`](standards/README.md) | Current durable engineering/documentation rules. |\n| Current intent | [`product-specs/index.md`](product-specs/index.md) and [`exec-plans/active/README.md`](exec-plans/active/README.md) | Only genuinely active work; implemented/history stays inventory. |\n| Completed history | [`exec-plans/completed/README.md`](exec-plans/completed/README.md) | Historical provenance, never default policy. |\n| Public docs product | [`../apps/web/README.md`](../apps/web/README.md), [`../packages/docs-content/README.md`](../packages/docs-content/README.md), and [`../packages/docs-fumadocs/README.md`](../packages/docs-fumadocs/README.md) | Consumer-facing content/runtime, not maintainer lifecycle policy. |\n| Repeatable release/deployment/recovery operations | [`runbooks/README.md`](runbooks/README.md) and [`operations/authority-model.md`](operations/authority-model.md) | Exactly five target-owned procedures; stop consequential operations when principal, candidate, target or receipt is unknown. |\n| CI controls and recurring automation | [`standards/controls.md`](standards/controls.md) and [`operations/automation-register.md`](operations/automation-register.md) | Quality workflow admission, release-graph controls, and report-only candidate boundaries; neither route grants external authority. |\n| Verification/critical journeys/proof | [`architecture/testing-and-quality.md`](architecture/testing-and-quality.md), [`verification/critical-journeys.json`](verification/critical-journeys.json), [`evidence/releases/HGI-203-critical-journeys.json`](evidence/releases/HGI-203-critical-journeys.json), [`evidence/releases/HGI-203-local.json`](evidence/releases/HGI-203-local.json), and [`documentation-audit/HGI-203-validation.json`](documentation-audit/HGI-203-validation.json) | The current inventory owns evolving journeys. Accepted HGI-203 retains the exact historical five-journey snapshot and bounded local proof that its immutable packet observed; HGI-204 validates both epochs without attributing current changes to the old attempt. Raw logs and secrets are never durable proof. |\n| Harness foundation and requalification | [`verification/repository-harness-profile.json`](verification/repository-harness-profile.json), [`documentation-audit/harness-foundation/accepted-findings.json`](documentation-audit/harness-foundation/accepted-findings.json), [`verification/harness-epochs.md`](verification/harness-epochs.md), and [`verification/effectiveness.md`](verification/effectiveness.md) | The TaxKit profile, accepted HE crosswalk, content-addressed skill receipt and focused gate own the implemented baseline. Last accepted epoch `HFI-004-2026-07-24` qualifies saved candidate `7c8a96e`; HGI-206 remains previous history. The active clean-slate plan owns pending qualification of today's graph. Neither saved epoch establishes current-checkout or external state. |\n| References | [`references/README.md`](references/README.md) | Revalidate mutable external guidance. |\n| Audit/accounting | [`documentation-audit/README.md`](documentation-audit/README.md) | Dated evidence, not policy. |\n\nFailed/inconclusive work retains provenance, last successful step, observed\nstate, escalation, resume trigger, recovery, and non-claims outside default\ncurrent routes. Do not delete or move historical/public/binary evidence without\nan approved retention manifest.\n\n## Maintenance\n\nEvery material slice decides `Change required`, `Preserve`, or `N/A` for docs,\nREADMEs, architecture, standards, public/generated references, runbooks,\nproof/evidence, skills, lint/config/CI, and active SPEC/tasks. Update the\nearliest durable owner and necessary pointers in the same slice. Counts prove\naccounting only; semantic and consumer claims need owner review and\nboundary-matched proof.\n\nUse the repository-local `$docs-maintainer` skill for this impact decision on\nboth PRD and ordinary changes. `$docs-writer` is limited to public-copy wording\nafter the maintenance route has selected the owner; it cannot close lifecycle,\ngenerated-content, package, proof, or validation work. Background freshness\nscans produce report-only candidates and cannot publish policy or documentation\nwithout separately attached implementation authority, review and publication\nidentity.\n\n`bun run check:docs` enforces the mechanical owner contract in\n[`../tools/documentation/owner-policy.json`](../tools/documentation/owner-policy.json).\nIt checks maintainer metadata, links, documented commands, workspace README\ncoverage, public/maintainer separation, accepted public-status representation,\nand generated-source edges with bounded diagnostics and a JSON detail receipt.\nThe command accepts `--json`; failed checks return a nonzero exit after the\nreport is saved. Effect CLI owns option parsing.\n`draft` means authored, locally renderable, visibly labelled candidate content;\n`published` means explicitly accepted current public documentation. Neither\nstatus proves runtime or external availability.\n\nAcceptance-record Schemas live in `@taxkit/content`. The docs tool explicitly\nselects source exports so it can run in a fresh checkout before package builds.\nVersion-two records include the reviewed source hash, which this check verifies;\nversion-one records retain their historical contract. The local accepted\ncatalogue builder, `bun run docs:catalogue`, requires version two, checks source\nbytes before and after compilation, and writes generated output only when\naccepted pages and matching navigation exist. It does not accept pages or\nestablish publication by running. See\n[`../packages/docs-content/README.md`](../packages/docs-content/README.md).\n\n`bun run check:runbooks` Schema-decodes the canonical runbook contract, the\ncurrent journey inventory and the exact historical HGI-203 journey snapshot,\nthen reconciles the immutable packet digest, four Markdown owners, commands,\nevidence paths, stop operations, index rows and authority rows. It writes only\nthe ignored bounded receipt `tmp/runbook-validation-report.json`, executes none\nof the documented procedures and establishes no consequential state.\n---\nname: docs-maintainer\ndescription: Audit and edit repository documentation so material code, configuration, API, infrastructure, CI, operational, skill, and SPEC changes update the correct semantic owners in the same implementation slice. Use for documentation maintenance, docs audits, stale or contradictory READMEs, documentation-impact assessment during implementation, and PRD writing/review/closeout. Preserve just-in-time context, distinguish skills from runbooks and durable docs from dated proof, and provide claim-matched verification. Do not use for public copywriting alone or to copy mutable provider state into repository docs.\n---\n\n# Documentation Maintainer\n\nKeep documentation aligned with repository behavior by updating the earliest\ndurable semantic owner and only the pointers that must lead to it.\n\n## Establish the local contract\n\n1. Read applicable `AGENTS.md`, inspect the worktree, and identify the exact\n   change, repository, environment, and write authority. Do not infer authority\n   to mutate providers, publish, release, or push from permission to edit docs.\n2. Read the repository-local `docs-maintainer` profile completely when one is\n   present at `references/repository-profile.md`. It owns repository paths,\n   commands, generated-document boundaries, mirrors, exceptions, and archive\n   policy. The global skill supplies method, never local truth.\n3. If no local profile exists, derive a temporary impact map from the root\n   `README*`, `docs/README*`, applicable package/app READMEs, active SPEC/tasks,\n   configuration, and changed implementation. Record missing ownership as a\n   gap; do not invent canonical paths or command names.\n4. Select an execution mode:\n   - **attached change:** when the user authorized implementation and repository\n     edits, edit affected documentation and task artifacts in the same slice;\n   - **audit or curator:** for scheduled/background freshness work, or when\n     mutation authority is absent, produce an isolated report-only candidate\n     with provenance and a proposed patch. Publication requires a separately\n     named responsible owner and publisher identity.\n\nNever let a curator publish its own uncorroborated findings or treat its prior\noutput as independent feedback. Pin any published context projection to an\nimmutable repository revision; refresh it only at a recorded phase boundary.\n\nKeep these truth layers distinct and apply the strongest applicable precedence:\nexternal system for current external state; shared store for shared source\nmaterial; immutable context projection for a recorded phase; repository code,\nconfig, and Schemas for desired state; durable docs for explanation and routing;\ndated evidence for observations; active SPEC/tasks for current intent and\nexecution. Link across layers instead of copying claims between them.\n\nFor a repository-wide documentation audit, substantial PRD, or cross-cutting\nharness change, read\n[repository-harness-contract.md](references/repository-harness-contract.md).\nIt routes to the complete local method and requires no external source lookup.\nLoad the applicable structured modules directly:\n\n- [contract map](references/harness/contract-map.md) for mode and lifecycle;\n- [invariant register](references/harness/invariant-register.md) for stable IDs;\n- [context and ownership](references/harness/context-and-ownership.md) for truth\n  layers, phased retrieval, and publication boundaries;\n- [proof and evaluation](references/harness/proof-and-evaluation.md) for\n  journeys, delivery, receipts, terminal states, and proportional evaluation;\n- [operations and authority](references/harness/operations-and-authority.md)\n  when runbooks, providers, controls, releases, or automation are in scope; and\n- [repository variation](references/harness/repository-variation.md) when\n  creating or changing the local profile.\n\nUse the Schemas and templates under `assets/harness/` for repository profiles,\ncritical journeys, bounded receipts, authority envelopes, and feedback or\nautomation controls. Do not replace those fixed field contracts with free-form\nprose.\nFor an ordinary localized documentation change, do not load that broader\ncontract unless an ownership, delivery, dependency, or proof question requires\nit. This skill owns the documentation track; use the sibling `repo-structure`\nskill for a complete repository audit.\n\n## Load context in phases\n\nUse just enough context to decide and then prove the change:\n\n1. **Ground:** read the change, directly affected docs/READMEs, the docs router,\n   the owning architecture or standard, and active task context.\n2. **Investigate:** inspect code, config, generated owners, history, provider\n   readback, or upstream material only to resolve an identified question.\n3. **Land:** inventory all affected docs, READMEs, skills, runbooks, references,\n   generated artifacts, indexes, and active/archive pointers. Reconcile every\n   contradiction on an affected route before closeout.\n\nDo not preload the whole repository for an ordinary localized change. A\nrepository-wide documentation audit or PRD review may require a full\n`docs/**` and `README*` accounting under its owning skill.\n\nFor a repository-wide audit, return documentation findings in the stable\nfinding format owned by the repository-audit procedure: consequence,\nevidence, semantic owner, root correction, duplicated guidance to retire,\naffected surfaces, proof, authority, limitations, and non-claims. Separate\nimportant corrections from optional improvements.\n\n## Build the impact ledger\n\nRead [document-classes.md](references/document-classes.md) to select semantic\nowners and [change-impact.md](references/change-impact.md) for the trigger\nmatrix. For each surface, record `Change required`, `Preserve`, or `N/A`, with:\n\n- changed behavior or claim;\n- semantic owner and required pointers;\n- exact affected path or narrowly bounded path set;\n- lifecycle transition, if any;\n- generated source and regeneration command, if applicable;\n- verification and observable postcondition;\n- proof location and explicit non-claims.\n\nCover docs, root/package/app READMEs, architecture/ADRs, standards, API and\ngenerated references, runbooks, critical journeys, proof/evidence, skills and\nagent instructions, lint/config/CI docs, migration/release notes, and active\nSPEC/tasks. Never accept a generic “update docs” item.\n\n## Edit the correct owner\n\n- Put durable design, invariants, and boundaries in architecture or standards.\n- Put exact repeatable operations in target-owned runbooks, including\n  preconditions, authority, sequential steps, receipts, rollback, and\n  escalation. Skills teach selection and judgment; they must route to rather\n  than copy runbooks.\n- Treat a procedure found in architecture or a README as an ownership defect,\n  not precedent to extend. Propose or create the target-owned runbook and leave\n  only durable rationale plus a pointer at the old location.\n- Put public setup and entry-point navigation in READMEs. Keep them short and\n  link to deeper owners.\n- Keep root `AGENTS.md` as a terse map of repository purpose/compatibility,\n  common operating loop, a small set of task classes or golden paths, and links\n  to their context, commands, and proof. Do not append completed-feature\n  histories or per-change atlas entries.\n- Put mutable external state and one-run observations in dated, addressable\n  evidence. Never present a provider response, deployment ID, secret age, or\n  current revision as durable repository truth.\n- Edit the source of generated documentation, run its real generator, and do\n  not hand-edit output unless repository policy explicitly says it is owned.\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Validate generated or existing package boundaries.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom render_package import validate_source_condition\n\n\nFORBIDDEN_SOURCE = {\n    \"generic SDK callback\": re.compile(r\"readonly\\s+(use|withClient)\\s*[:(]\"),\n    \"runtime class policy\": re.compile(r\"\\binstanceof\\b\"),\n    \"legacy Context tag\": re.compile(r\"Context\\.Tag\\b\"),\n    \"package-local runtime execution\": re.compile(r\"Effect\\.run(?:Promise|Sync)\\b\"),\n}\nPERSONAL_ROOT = \"/\" + \"Users\" + \"/\"\nRELATIVE_IMPORT = re.compile(r'''(?:\\bfrom\\s*|\\bimport\\s*\\(\\s*|\\bimport\\s*)[\"'](\\.[^\"']*)[\"']''')\n\n\ndef fail(message: str) -> None:\n    print(f\"ERROR: {message}\", file=sys.stderr)\n    raise SystemExit(1)\n\n\nroot = Path(sys.argv[1]).resolve(strict=True)\nfor path in root.rglob(\"*\"):\n    if not path.is_file():\n        continue\n    text = path.read_text(errors=\"ignore\")\n    if PERSONAL_ROOT in text:\n        fail(f\"{path.relative_to(root)} contains a personal absolute path\")\n    if re.search(r\"__[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*__|\\*\\*[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*\\*\\*\", text):\n        fail(f\"{path.relative_to(root)} contains an unresolved template token\")\nmanifest_path = root / \"package.json\"\nif not manifest_path.is_file():\n    fail(\"missing package.json\")\nmanifest = json.loads(manifest_path.read_text())\nrender_path = root / \"package-structure.render.json\"\nif not render_path.is_file():\n    fail(\"missing package-structure.render.json\")\nrender = json.loads(render_path.read_text())\ntry:\n    source_condition = validate_source_condition(render.get(\"sourceCondition\", \"\"))\nexcept (TypeError, ValueError) as error:\n    fail(str(error))\nkind = render.get(\"kind\")\nrequired_by_kind = {\n    \"effect-service\": {\n        \"src/schemas.ts\", \"src/errors.ts\", \"src/service.ts\", \"src/live.layer.ts\",\n        \"src/test.layer.ts\", \"src/__testing__/fixtures.ts\",\n        \"src/__testing__/observations.ts\", \"test/service.test.ts\", \"test/schemas.test.ts\",\n    },\n    \"rpc\": {\n        \"src/group.ts\", \"src/handlers.ts\", \"src/service.ts\", \"src/server.ts\",\n        \"src/live.layer.ts\", \"src/test.layer.ts\",\n    },\n    \"http-api\": {\n        \"src/api.ts\", \"src/group.ts\", \"src/handlers.ts\", \"src/server.ts\",\n        \"src/client/service.ts\", \"src/client/browser.layer.ts\",\n        \"src/client/live.layer.ts\",\n    },\n}\nif kind not in required_by_kind:\n    fail(f\"unknown rendered package kind: {kind}\")\nmissing = sorted(path for path in required_by_kind[kind] if not (root / path).is_file())\nif missing:\n    fail(f\"{kind} package missing required paths: {missing}\")\nif not render.get(\"officialSources\") or not render.get(\"compatibilityDecisions\"):\n    fail(\"render receipt lacks official sources or compatibility decisions\")\nif any(item.get(\"status\") != \"qualified\" for item in render[\"compatibilityDecisions\"]):\n    fail(\"render receipt contains an unqualified compatibility decision\")\nif not render.get(\"limitations\") or not render.get(\"nonClaims\"):\n    fail(\"render receipt lacks limitations or non-claims\")\nfor relative, expected in render.get(\"configDigests\", {}).items():\n    target = root / relative\n    observed = hashlib.sha256(target.read_bytes()).hexdigest() if target.is_file() else None\n    if observed != expected:\n        fail(f\"rendered config digest mismatch: {relative}\")\nexports = manifest.get(\"exports\")\nif not isinstance(exports, dict) or not exports:\n    fail(\"package exports must be explicit\")\nreadme = (root / \"README.md\").read_text()\nfor heading in (\"## Exports\", \"## Documentation impact\", \"## Runbook applicability\", \"## Non-claims\"):\n    if heading not in readme:\n        fail(f\"README missing required section: {heading}\")\nfor export_name in exports:\n    if f\"`{export_name}`\" not in readme:\n        fail(f\"README must document exact export {export_name}\")\nfor phrase in (\"repository\", \"runbook\", \"proof\"):\n    if phrase not in readme.lower():\n        fail(f\"README must route {phrase} ownership\")\npublish = manifest.get(\"publishConfig\", {}).get(\"exports\", {})\nsource_conditions: set[str] = set()\nfor name, value in exports.items():\n    if not isinstance(value, dict):\n        fail(f\"export {name} must be an object\")\n    keys = list(value)\n    if not keys or keys[0] != source_condition:\n        fail(f\"export {name} must place recorded source condition first: {source_condition}\")\n    source_target = value[source_condition]\n    if not isinstance(source_target, str) or not source_target.startswith(\"./src/\") or not (root / source_target).is_file():\n        fail(f\"export {name} recorded source condition must target an existing source file\")\n    conditions = [key for key in keys if key not in {\"types\", \"default\", \"import\"}]\n    source_conditions.update(conditions)\n    for condition in conditions:\n        target = value[condition]\n        if isinstance(target, str) and target.startswith(\"./src\"):\n            if keys.index(condition) > keys.index(\"types\"):\n                fail(f\"export {name} must place source before types\")\n            if not (root / target).is_file():\n                fail(f\"export {name} source target does not exist: {target}\")\n    if \"types\" in value and \"default\" in value and keys.index(\"types\") > keys.index(\"default\"):\n        fail(f\"export {name} must place types before default\")\nfor value in publish.values() if isinstance(publish, dict) else []:\n    if isinstance(value, dict) and source_conditions.intersection(value):\n        fail(\"publish exports must omit repository source conditions\")\nfor directory in (\"src\", \"test\"):\n    for path in (root / directory).rglob(\"*.ts\"):\n        for specifier in RELATIVE_IMPORT.findall(path.read_text()):\n            if not specifier.endswith(\".js\"):\n                fail(f\"{path.relative_to(root)} relative import must use an explicit .js suffix: {specifier}\")\nfor path in (root / \"src\").rglob(\"*.ts\"):\n    text = path.read_text()\n    for label, pattern in FORBIDDEN_SOURCE.items():\n        if pattern.search(text):\n            fail(f\"{path.relative_to(root)} contains {label}\")\n    if re.search(r\"\\bid\\s*[?:]?\\s*:\\s*string\\b\", text):\n        fail(f\"{path.relative_to(root)} contains a raw semantic id\")\n    if re.search(r'from\\s+[\"\\']effect/unstable/(?:rpc|httpapi)/(?!Rpc(?:ClientError|Group|Test)?[\"\\'])', text):\n        fail(f\"{path.relative_to(root)} contains a substituted upstream Effect import\")\nfor path in (root / \"src\").rglob(\"*\"):\n    if path.is_file() and path.stem.lower() in {\"helper\", \"helpers\", \"util\", \"utils\"}:\n        fail(f\"{path.relative_to(root)} is generic helper sprawl; name the owned capability\")\nservice = root / \"src/service.ts\"\nif service.is_file():\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n  \"kind\": \"effect-service\",\n  \"packageName\": \"@taxkit/analytics\",\n  \"domainPackage\": null,\n  \"sourceCondition\": \"source\",\n  \"versionSnapshot\": {\n    \"resolvedAt\": \"2026-10-07\",\n    \"sha256\": \"263bd13f098099137c1ea2cd204e2920a41c5a8ddc22dba49724d9285aa80a12\"\n  },\n  \"officialSources\": {\n    \"effect\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/effect/4.0.0\",\n    \"vitest\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/vitest/5.0.3\",\n    \"typescript\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/typescript/7.0.2\"\n  },\n  \"selectedVersions\": {\n    \"effect\": \"4.0.0\",\n    \"@effect/vitest\": \"4.0.0\",\n    \"typescript\": \"7.0.2\",\n    \"vitest\": \"5.0.3\",\n    \"@effect/platform-bun\": \"4.0.0\"\n  },\n  \"compatibilityDecisions\": [\n    {\n      \"status\": \"qualified\",\n      \"decision\": \"Reuse TaxKit T002 stable Effect 4.0.0 dependency qualification and installed types; rendered source is a scaffold and needs real TaxKit type/lint/tests before acceptance\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"configDigests\": {\n    \"package.json\": \"1ee730f376aa3675eee314d99c24564d3dfaec5215387106cb46981dbafbf4ca\",\n    \"tsconfig.json\": \"71596163cd8ffea16eb4950049bc772ec8a8e2db408759c80bc8232aa40a6d99\",\n    \"tsconfig.build.json\": \"320b70b4115224df6a42038a8759a444d0feecabb0666c22a519904a1e9b9de9\",\n    \"vitest.config.ts\": \"8167d20931f3f88793a6253697dad0c2dc7a519ca7d4ec8aea6c2ffc9f1448b7\"\n  },\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"Structural rendering does not prove installed dependency, declaration, runtime, or packed-consumer behavior.\"\n  ],\n  \"nonClaims\": [\"Selected versions are not claimed to remain latest.\"]\n}\n---\ndocument_type: documentation-router\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: canonical\nowner: taxkit-documentation-owner\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-07\nreview_trigger: any maintainer/public docs class, root route, SPEC, plan, runbook, proof, evidence, or lifecycle change\n---\n\n# TaxKit documentation\n\nThis is the sole router for maintainer-document type, lifecycle, truth layers,\nand semantic ownership. Root `README.md` is the public repository entry point;\n`AGENTS.md` is the short task map; `docs/architecture/README.md` is the current\narchitecture route. Public documentation content is a separate product surface\nowned by the replacement `apps/web`, backend content contracts and docs\npackages. The old `apps/docs` workspace is retired. Its tombstone routes to the verified\nsource bundle and dated provider recovery records; no provider operation is\nauthorised by that retained history.\n\n## Truth layers\n\nUse the strongest applicable owner and link rather than copy:\n\n1. External systems own their current external state at readback time.\n2. Code, configuration, Schemas, package exports, workflows, and generated\n   sources own desired/executable state.\n3. Architecture and standards own durable boundaries and enforceable policy.\n4. Dated proof/evidence owns one artifact/environment/authority observation and\n   its limitations.\n5. Active SPEC/tasks and execution plans own current implementation intent.\n\nProvider/registry output cannot grant authority. Completed plans are history.\nLocal release checks do not prove npm publication or external consumers.\n\n## Metadata and lifecycle\n\nNew or materially revised maintainer docs separate `document_type`,\n`lifecycle`, `authority`, and `owner`. Current durable docs also record\n`last_reviewed` and `review_trigger`; superseded/tombstone docs record a\nsuccessor and reason.\n\nLifecycle values are `proposed`, `current`, `implemented`, `superseded`,\n`historical`, `evidence`, `reference`, `failed`, `inconclusive`, `tombstone`,\nand `archived`. Authority values are `canonical`, `supporting`, `generated`,\nand `external`. Legacy `status: canonical` is an authority marker, not a\nlifecycle; migrate it only when its owner is materially revised.\n\n## Routes\n\n| Need | Owner | Use |\n|---|---|---|\n| Architecture | [`architecture/README.md`](architecture/README.md) | Current architecture route. `architecture.md` is a tombstone only. |\n| Standards | [`standards/README.md`](standards/README.md) | Current durable engineering/documentation rules. |\n| Current intent | [`product-specs/index.md`](product-specs/index.md) and [`exec-plans/active/README.md`](exec-plans/active/README.md) | Only genuinely active work; implemented/history stays inventory. |\n| Completed history | [`exec-plans/completed/README.md`](exec-plans/completed/README.md) | Historical provenance, never default policy. |\n| Public docs product | [`../apps/web/README.md`](../apps/web/README.md), [`../packages/docs-content/README.md`](../packages/docs-content/README.md), and [`../packages/docs-fumadocs/README.md`](../packages/docs-fumadocs/README.md) | Consumer-facing content/runtime, not maintainer lifecycle policy. |\n| Repeatable release/deployment/recovery operations | [`runbooks/README.md`](runbooks/README.md) and [`operations/authority-model.md`](operations/authority-model.md) | Exactly five target-owned procedures; stop consequential operations when principal, candidate, target or receipt is unknown. |\n| CI controls and recurring automation | [`standards/controls.md`](standards/controls.md) and [`operations/automation-register.md`](operations/automation-register.md) | Quality workflow admission, release-graph controls, and report-only candidate boundaries; neither route grants external authority. |\n| Verification/critical journeys/proof | [`architecture/testing-and-quality.md`](architecture/testing-and-quality.md), [`verification/critical-journeys.json`](verification/critical-journeys.json), [`evidence/releases/HGI-203-critical-journeys.json`](evidence/releases/HGI-203-critical-journeys.json), [`evidence/releases/HGI-203-local.json`](evidence/releases/HGI-203-local.json), and [`documentation-audit/HGI-203-validation.json`](documentation-audit/HGI-203-validation.json) | The current inventory owns evolving journeys. Accepted HGI-203 retains the exact historical five-journey snapshot and bounded local proof that its immutable packet observed; HGI-204 validates both epochs without attributing current changes to the old attempt. Raw logs and secrets are never durable proof. |\n| Harness foundation and requalification | [`verification/repository-harness-profile.json`](verification/repository-harness-profile.json), [`documentation-audit/harness-foundation/accepted-findings.json`](documentation-audit/harness-foundation/accepted-findings.json), [`verification/harness-epochs.md`](verification/harness-epochs.md), and [`verification/effectiveness.md`](verification/effectiveness.md) | The TaxKit profile, accepted HE crosswalk, content-addressed skill receipt and focused gate own the implemented baseline. Last accepted epoch `HFI-004-2026-07-24` qualifies saved candidate `7c8a96e`; HGI-206 remains previous history. The active clean-slate plan owns pending qualification of today's graph. Neither saved epoch establishes current-checkout or external state. |\n| References | [`references/README.md`](references/README.md) | Revalidate mutable external guidance. |\n| Audit/accounting | [`documentation-audit/README.md`](documentation-audit/README.md) | Dated evidence, not policy. |\n\nFailed/inconclusive work retains provenance, last successful step, observed\nstate, escalation, resume trigger, recovery, and non-claims outside default\ncurrent routes. Do not delete or move historical/public/binary evidence without\nan approved retention manifest.\n\n## Maintenance\n\nEvery material slice decides `Change required`, `Preserve`, or `N/A` for docs,\nREADMEs, architecture, standards, public/generated references, runbooks,\nproof/evidence, skills, lint/config/CI, and active SPEC/tasks. Update the\nearliest durable owner and necessary pointers in the same slice. Counts prove\naccounting only; semantic and consumer claims need owner review and\nboundary-matched proof.\n\nUse the repository-local `$docs-maintainer` skill for this impact decision on\nboth PRD and ordinary changes. `$docs-writer` is limited to public-copy wording\nafter the maintenance route has selected the owner; it cannot close lifecycle,\ngenerated-content, package, proof, or validation work. Background freshness\nscans produce report-only candidates and cannot publish policy or documentation\nwithout separately attached implementation authority, review and publication\nidentity.\n\n`bun run check:docs` enforces the mechanical owner contract in\n[`../tools/documentation/owner-policy.json`](../tools/documentation/owner-policy.json).\nIt checks maintainer metadata, links, documented commands, workspace README\ncoverage, public/maintainer separation, accepted public-status representation,\nand generated-source edges with bounded diagnostics and a JSON detail receipt.\nThe command accepts `--json`; failed checks return a nonzero exit after the\nreport is saved. Effect CLI owns option parsing.\n`draft` means authored, locally renderable, visibly labelled candidate content;\n`published` means explicitly accepted current public documentation. Neither\nstatus proves runtime or external availability.\n\nAcceptance-record Schemas live in `@taxkit/content`. The docs tool explicitly\nselects source exports so it can run in a fresh checkout before package builds.\nVersion-two records include the reviewed source hash, which this check verifies;\nversion-one records retain their historical contract. The local accepted\ncatalogue builder, `bun run docs:catalogue`, requires version two, checks source\nbytes before and after compilation, and writes generated output only when\naccepted pages and matching navigation exist. It does not accept pages or\nestablish publication by running. See\n[`../packages/docs-content/README.md`](../packages/docs-content/README.md).\n\n`bun run check:runbooks` Schema-decodes the canonical runbook contract, the\ncurrent journey inventory and the exact historical HGI-203 journey snapshot,\nthen reconciles the immutable packet digest, four Markdown owners, commands,\nevidence paths, stop operations, index rows and authority rows. It writes only\nthe ignored bounded receipt `tmp/runbook-validation-report.json`, executes none\nof the documented procedures and establishes no consequential state.\n---\nname: docs-maintainer\ndescription: Audit and edit repository documentation so material code, configuration, API, infrastructure, CI, operational, skill, and SPEC changes update the correct semantic owners in the same implementation slice. Use for documentation maintenance, docs audits, stale or contradictory READMEs, documentation-impact assessment during implementation, and PRD writing/review/closeout. Preserve just-in-time context, distinguish skills from runbooks and durable docs from dated proof, and provide claim-matched verification. Do not use for public copywriting alone or to copy mutable provider state into repository docs.\n---\n\n# Documentation Maintainer\n\nKeep documentation aligned with repository behavior by updating the earliest\ndurable semantic owner and only the pointers that must lead to it.\n\n## Establish the local contract\n\n1. Read applicable `AGENTS.md`, inspect the worktree, and identify the exact\n   change, repository, environment, and write authority. Do not infer authority\n   to mutate providers, publish, release, or push from permission to edit docs.\n2. Read the repository-local `docs-maintainer` profile completely when one is\n   present at `references/repository-profile.md`. It owns repository paths,\n   commands, generated-document boundaries, mirrors, exceptions, and archive\n   policy. The global skill supplies method, never local truth.\n3. If no local profile exists, derive a temporary impact map from the root\n   `README*`, `docs/README*`, applicable package/app READMEs, active SPEC/tasks,\n   configuration, and changed implementation. Record missing ownership as a\n   gap; do not invent canonical paths or command names.\n4. Select an execution mode:\n   - **attached change:** when the user authorized implementation and repository\n     edits, edit affected documentation and task artifacts in the same slice;\n   - **audit or curator:** for scheduled/background freshness work, or when\n     mutation authority is absent, produce an isolated report-only candidate\n     with provenance and a proposed patch. Publication requires a separately\n     named responsible owner and publisher identity.\n\nNever let a curator publish its own uncorroborated findings or treat its prior\noutput as independent feedback. Pin any published context projection to an\nimmutable repository revision; refresh it only at a recorded phase boundary.\n\nKeep these truth layers distinct and apply the strongest applicable precedence:\nexternal system for current external state; shared store for shared source\nmaterial; immutable context projection for a recorded phase; repository code,\nconfig, and Schemas for desired state; durable docs for explanation and routing;\ndated evidence for observations; active SPEC/tasks for current intent and\nexecution. Link across layers instead of copying claims between them.\n\nFor a repository-wide documentation audit, substantial PRD, or cross-cutting\nharness change, read\n[repository-harness-contract.md](references/repository-harness-contract.md).\nIt routes to the complete local method and requires no external source lookup.\nLoad the applicable structured modules directly:\n\n- [contract map](references/harness/contract-map.md) for mode and lifecycle;\n- [invariant register](references/harness/invariant-register.md) for stable IDs;\n- [context and ownership](references/harness/context-and-ownership.md) for truth\n  layers, phased retrieval, and publication boundaries;\n- [proof and evaluation](references/harness/proof-and-evaluation.md) for\n  journeys, delivery, receipts, terminal states, and proportional evaluation;\n- [operations and authority](references/harness/operations-and-authority.md)\n  when runbooks, providers, controls, releases, or automation are in scope; and\n- [repository variation](references/harness/repository-variation.md) when\n  creating or changing the local profile.\n\nUse the Schemas and templates under `assets/harness/` for repository profiles,\ncritical journeys, bounded receipts, authority envelopes, and feedback or\nautomation controls. Do not replace those fixed field contracts with free-form\nprose.\nFor an ordinary localized documentation change, do not load that broader\ncontract unless an ownership, delivery, dependency, or proof question requires\nit. This skill owns the documentation track; use the sibling `repo-structure`\nskill for a complete repository audit.\n\n## Load context in phases\n\nUse just enough context to decide and then prove the change:\n\n1. **Ground:** read the change, directly affected docs/READMEs, the docs router,\n   the owning architecture or standard, and active task context.\n2. **Investigate:** inspect code, config, generated owners, history, provider\n   readback, or upstream material only to resolve an identified question.\n3. **Land:** inventory all affected docs, READMEs, skills, runbooks, references,\n   generated artifacts, indexes, and active/archive pointers. Reconcile every\n   contradiction on an affected route before closeout.\n\nDo not preload the whole repository for an ordinary localized change. A\nrepository-wide documentation audit or PRD review may require a full\n`docs/**` and `README*` accounting under its owning skill.\n\nFor a repository-wide audit, return documentation findings in the stable\nfinding format owned by the repository-audit procedure: consequence,\nevidence, semantic owner, root correction, duplicated guidance to retire,\naffected surfaces, proof, authority, limitations, and non-claims. Separate\nimportant corrections from optional improvements.\n\n## Build the impact ledger\n\nRead [document-classes.md](references/document-classes.md) to select semantic\nowners and [change-impact.md](references/change-impact.md) for the trigger\nmatrix. For each surface, record `Change required`, `Preserve`, or `N/A`, with:\n\n- changed behavior or claim;\n- semantic owner and required pointers;\n- exact affected path or narrowly bounded path set;\n- lifecycle transition, if any;\n- generated source and regeneration command, if applicable;\n- verification and observable postcondition;\n- proof location and explicit non-claims.\n\nCover docs, root/package/app READMEs, architecture/ADRs, standards, API and\ngenerated references, runbooks, critical journeys, proof/evidence, skills and\nagent instructions, lint/config/CI docs, migration/release notes, and active\nSPEC/tasks. Never accept a generic “update docs” item.\n\n## Edit the correct owner\n\n- Put durable design, invariants, and boundaries in architecture or standards.\n- Put exact repeatable operations in target-owned runbooks, including\n  preconditions, authority, sequential steps, receipts, rollback, and\n  escalation. Skills teach selection and judgment; they must route to rather\n  than copy runbooks.\n- Treat a procedure found in architecture or a README as an ownership defect,\n  not precedent to extend. Propose or create the target-owned runbook and leave\n  only durable rationale plus a pointer at the old location.\n- Put public setup and entry-point navigation in READMEs. Keep them short and\n  link to deeper owners.\n- Keep root `AGENTS.md` as a terse map of repository purpose/compatibility,\n  common operating loop, a small set of task classes or golden paths, and links\n  to their context, commands, and proof. Do not append completed-feature\n  histories or per-change atlas entries.\n- Put mutable external state and one-run observations in dated, addressable\n  evidence. Never present a provider response, deployment ID, secret age, or\n  current revision as durable repository truth.\n- Edit the source of generated documentation, run its real generator, and do\n  not hand-edit output unless repository policy explicitly says it is owned.\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Validate generated or existing package boundaries.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom render_package import validate_source_condition\n\n\nFORBIDDEN_SOURCE = {\n    \"generic SDK callback\": re.compile(r\"readonly\\s+(use|withClient)\\s*[:(]\"),\n    \"runtime class policy\": re.compile(r\"\\binstanceof\\b\"),\n    \"legacy Context tag\": re.compile(r\"Context\\.Tag\\b\"),\n    \"package-local runtime execution\": re.compile(r\"Effect\\.run(?:Promise|Sync)\\b\"),\n}\nPERSONAL_ROOT = \"/\" + \"Users\" + \"/\"\nRELATIVE_IMPORT = re.compile(r'''(?:\\bfrom\\s*|\\bimport\\s*\\(\\s*|\\bimport\\s*)[\"'](\\.[^\"']*)[\"']''')\n\n\ndef fail(message: str) -> None:\n    print(f\"ERROR: {message}\", file=sys.stderr)\n    raise SystemExit(1)\n\n\nroot = Path(sys.argv[1]).resolve(strict=True)\nfor path in root.rglob(\"*\"):\n    if not path.is_file():\n        continue\n    text = path.read_text(errors=\"ignore\")\n    if PERSONAL_ROOT in text:\n        fail(f\"{path.relative_to(root)} contains a personal absolute path\")\n    if re.search(r\"__[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*__|\\*\\*[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*\\*\\*\", text):\n        fail(f\"{path.relative_to(root)} contains an unresolved template token\")\nmanifest_path = root / \"package.json\"\nif not manifest_path.is_file():\n    fail(\"missing package.json\")\nmanifest = json.loads(manifest_path.read_text())\nrender_path = root / \"package-structure.render.json\"\nif not render_path.is_file():\n    fail(\"missing package-structure.render.json\")\nrender = json.loads(render_path.read_text())\ntry:\n    source_condition = validate_source_condition(render.get(\"sourceCondition\", \"\"))\nexcept (TypeError, ValueError) as error:\n    fail(str(error))\nkind = render.get(\"kind\")\nrequired_by_kind = {\n    \"effect-service\": {\n        \"src/schemas.ts\", \"src/errors.ts\", \"src/service.ts\", \"src/live.layer.ts\",\n        \"src/test.layer.ts\", \"src/__testing__/fixtures.ts\",\n        \"src/__testing__/observations.ts\", \"test/service.test.ts\", \"test/schemas.test.ts\",\n    },\n    \"rpc\": {\n        \"src/group.ts\", \"src/handlers.ts\", \"src/service.ts\", \"src/server.ts\",\n        \"src/live.layer.ts\", \"src/test.layer.ts\",\n    },\n    \"http-api\": {\n        \"src/api.ts\", \"src/group.ts\", \"src/handlers.ts\", \"src/server.ts\",\n        \"src/client/service.ts\", \"src/client/browser.layer.ts\",\n        \"src/client/live.layer.ts\",\n    },\n}\nif kind not in required_by_kind:\n    fail(f\"unknown rendered package kind: {kind}\")\nmissing = sorted(path for path in required_by_kind[kind] if not (root / path).is_file())\nif missing:\n    fail(f\"{kind} package missing required paths: {missing}\")\nif not render.get(\"officialSources\") or not render.get(\"compatibilityDecisions\"):\n    fail(\"render receipt lacks official sources or compatibility decisions\")\nif any(item.get(\"status\") != \"qualified\" for item in render[\"compatibilityDecisions\"]):\n    fail(\"render receipt contains an unqualified compatibility decision\")\nif not render.get(\"limitations\") or not render.get(\"nonClaims\"):\n    fail(\"render receipt lacks limitations or non-claims\")\nfor relative, expected in render.get(\"configDigests\", {}).items():\n    target = root / relative\n    observed = hashlib.sha256(target.read_bytes()).hexdigest() if target.is_file() else None\n    if observed != expected:\n        fail(f\"rendered config digest mismatch: {relative}\")\nexports = manifest.get(\"exports\")\nif not isinstance(exports, dict) or not exports:\n    fail(\"package exports must be explicit\")\nreadme = (root / \"README.md\").read_text()\nfor heading in (\"## Exports\", \"## Documentation impact\", \"## Runbook applicability\", \"## Non-claims\"):\n    if heading not in readme:\n        fail(f\"README missing required section: {heading}\")\nfor export_name in exports:\n    if f\"`{export_name}`\" not in readme:\n        fail(f\"README must document exact export {export_name}\")\nfor phrase in (\"repository\", \"runbook\", \"proof\"):\n    if phrase not in readme.lower():\n        fail(f\"README must route {phrase} ownership\")\npublish = manifest.get(\"publishConfig\", {}).get(\"exports\", {})\nsource_conditions: set[str] = set()\nfor name, value in exports.items():\n    if not isinstance(value, dict):\n        fail(f\"export {name} must be an object\")\n    keys = list(value)\n    if not keys or keys[0] != source_condition:\n        fail(f\"export {name} must place recorded source condition first: {source_condition}\")\n    source_target = value[source_condition]\n    if not isinstance(source_target, str) or not source_target.startswith(\"./src/\") or not (root / source_target).is_file():\n        fail(f\"export {name} recorded source condition must target an existing source file\")\n    conditions = [key for key in keys if key not in {\"types\", \"default\", \"import\"}]\n    source_conditions.update(conditions)\n    for condition in conditions:\n        target = value[condition]\n        if isinstance(target, str) and target.startswith(\"./src\"):\n            if keys.index(condition) > keys.index(\"types\"):\n                fail(f\"export {name} must place source before types\")\n            if not (root / target).is_file():\n                fail(f\"export {name} source target does not exist: {target}\")\n    if \"types\" in value and \"default\" in value and keys.index(\"types\") > keys.index(\"default\"):\n        fail(f\"export {name} must place types before default\")\nfor value in publish.values() if isinstance(publish, dict) else []:\n    if isinstance(value, dict) and source_conditions.intersection(value):\n        fail(\"publish exports must omit repository source conditions\")\nfor directory in (\"src\", \"test\"):\n    for path in (root / directory).rglob(\"*.ts\"):\n        for specifier in RELATIVE_IMPORT.findall(path.read_text()):\n            if not specifier.endswith(\".js\"):\n                fail(f\"{path.relative_to(root)} relative import must use an explicit .js suffix: {specifier}\")\nfor path in (root / \"src\").rglob(\"*.ts\"):\n    text = path.read_text()\n    for label, pattern in FORBIDDEN_SOURCE.items():\n        if pattern.search(text):\n            fail(f\"{path.relative_to(root)} contains {label}\")\n    if re.search(r\"\\bid\\s*[?:]?\\s*:\\s*string\\b\", text):\n        fail(f\"{path.relative_to(root)} contains a raw semantic id\")\n    if re.search(r'from\\s+[\"\\']effect/unstable/(?:rpc|httpapi)/(?!Rpc(?:ClientError|Group|Test)?[\"\\'])', text):\n        fail(f\"{path.relative_to(root)} contains a substituted upstream Effect import\")\nfor path in (root / \"src\").rglob(\"*\"):\n    if path.is_file() and path.stem.lower() in {\"helper\", \"helpers\", \"util\", \"utils\"}:\n        fail(f\"{path.relative_to(root)} is generic helper sprawl; name the owned capability\")\nservice = root / \"src/service.ts\"\nif service.is_file():\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7292},"formatted_output":"{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n  \"kind\": \"effect-service\",\n  \"packageName\": \"@taxkit/analytics\",\n  \"domainPackage\": null,\n  \"sourceCondition\": \"source\",\n  \"versionSnapshot\": {\n    \"resolvedAt\": \"2026-10-07\",\n    \"sha256\": \"263bd13f098099137c1ea2cd204e2920a41c5a8ddc22dba49724d9285aa80a12\"\n  },\n  \"officialSources\": {\n    \"effect\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/effect/4.0.0\",\n    \"vitest\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/vitest/5.0.3\",\n    \"typescript\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/typescript/7.0.2\"\n  },\n  \"selectedVersions\": {\n    \"effect\": \"4.0.0\",\n    \"@effect/vitest\": \"4.0.0\",\n    \"typescript\": \"7.0.2\",\n    \"vitest\": \"5.0.3\",\n    \"@effect/platform-bun\": \"4.0.0\"\n  },\n  \"compatibilityDecisions\": [\n    {\n      \"status\": \"qualified\",\n      \"decision\": \"Reuse TaxKit T002 stable Effect 4.0.0 dependency qualification and installed types; rendered source is a scaffold and needs real TaxKit type/lint/tests before acceptance\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"configDigests\": {\n    \"package.json\": \"1ee730f376aa3675eee314d99c24564d3dfaec5215387106cb46981dbafbf4ca\",\n    \"tsconfig.json\": \"71596163cd8ffea16eb4950049bc772ec8a8e2db408759c80bc8232aa40a6d99\",\n    \"tsconfig.build.json\": \"320b70b4115224df6a42038a8759a444d0feecabb0666c22a519904a1e9b9de9\",\n    \"vitest.config.ts\": \"8167d20931f3f88793a6253697dad0c2dc7a519ca7d4ec8aea6c2ffc9f1448b7\"\n  },\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"Structural rendering does not prove installed dependency, declaration, runtime, or packed-consumer behavior.\"\n  ],\n  \"nonClaims\": [\"Selected versions are not claimed to remain latest.\"]\n}\n---\ndocument_type: documentation-router\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: canonical\nowner: taxkit-documentation-owner\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-07\nreview_trigger: any maintainer/public docs class, root route, SPEC, plan, runbook, proof, evidence, or lifecycle change\n---\n\n# TaxKit documentation\n\nThis is the sole router for maintainer-document type, lifecycle, truth layers,\nand semantic ownership. Root `README.md` is the public repository entry point;\n`AGENTS.md` is the short task map; `docs/architecture/README.md` is the current\narchitecture route. Public documentation content is a separate product surface\nowned by the replacement `apps/web`, backend content contracts and docs\npackages. The old `apps/docs` workspace is retired. Its tombstone routes to the verified\nsource bundle and dated provider recovery records; no provider operation is\nauthorised by that retained history.\n\n## Truth layers\n\nUse the strongest applicable owner and link rather than copy:\n\n1. External systems own their current external state at readback time.\n2. Code, configuration, Schemas, package exports, workflows, and generated\n   sources own desired/executable state.\n3. Architecture and standards own durable boundaries and enforceable policy.\n4. Dated proof/evidence owns one artifact/environment/authority observation and\n   its limitations.\n5. Active SPEC/tasks and execution plans own current implementation intent.\n\nProvider/registry output cannot grant authority. Completed plans are history.\nLocal release checks do not prove npm publication or external consumers.\n\n## Metadata and lifecycle\n\nNew or materially revised maintainer docs separate `document_type`,\n`lifecycle`, `authority`, and `owner`. Current durable docs also record\n`last_reviewed` and `review_trigger`; superseded/tombstone docs record a\nsuccessor and reason.\n\nLifecycle values are `proposed`, `current`, `implemented`, `superseded`,\n`historical`, `evidence`, `reference`, `failed`, `inconclusive`, `tombstone`,\nand `archived`. Authority values are `canonical`, `supporting`, `generated`,\nand `external`. Legacy `status: canonical` is an authority marker, not a\nlifecycle; migrate it only when its owner is materially revised.\n\n## Routes\n\n| Need | Owner | Use |\n|---|---|---|\n| Architecture | [`architecture/README.md`](architecture/README.md) | Current architecture route. `architecture.md` is a tombstone only. |\n| Standards | [`standards/README.md`](standards/README.md) | Current durable engineering/documentation rules. |\n| Current intent | [`product-specs/index.md`](product-specs/index.md) and [`exec-plans/active/README.md`](exec-plans/active/README.md) | Only genuinely active work; implemented/history stays inventory. |\n| Completed history | [`exec-plans/completed/README.md`](exec-plans/completed/README.md) | Historical provenance, never default policy. |\n| Public docs product | [`../apps/web/README.md`](../apps/web/README.md), [`../packages/docs-content/README.md`](../packages/docs-content/README.md), and [`../packages/docs-fumadocs/README.md`](../packages/docs-fumadocs/README.md) | Consumer-facing content/runtime, not maintainer lifecycle policy. |\n| Repeatable release/deployment/recovery operations | [`runbooks/README.md`](runbooks/README.md) and [`operations/authority-model.md`](operations/authority-model.md) | Exactly five target-owned procedures; stop consequential operations when principal, candidate, target or receipt is unknown. |\n| CI controls and recurring automation | [`standards/controls.md`](standards/controls.md) and [`operations/automation-register.md`](operations/automation-register.md) | Quality workflow admission, release-graph controls, and report-only candidate boundaries; neither route grants external authority. |\n| Verification/critical journeys/proof | [`architecture/testing-and-quality.md`](architecture/testing-and-quality.md), [`verification/critical-journeys.json`](verification/critical-journeys.json), [`evidence/releases/HGI-203-critical-journeys.json`](evidence/releases/HGI-203-critical-journeys.json), [`evidence/releases/HGI-203-local.json`](evidence/releases/HGI-203-local.json), and [`documentation-audit/HGI-203-validation.json`](documentation-audit/HGI-203-validation.json) | The current inventory owns evolving journeys. Accepted HGI-203 retains the exact historical five-journey snapshot and bounded local proof that its immutable packet observed; HGI-204 validates both epochs without attributing current changes to the old attempt. Raw logs and secrets are never durable proof. |\n| Harness foundation and requalification | [`verification/repository-harness-profile.json`](verification/repository-harness-profile.json), [`documentation-audit/harness-foundation/accepted-findings.json`](documentation-audit/harness-foundation/accepted-findings.json), [`verification/harness-epochs.md`](verification/harness-epochs.md), and [`verification/effectiveness.md`](verification/effectiveness.md) | The TaxKit profile, accepted HE crosswalk, content-addressed skill receipt and focused gate own the implemented baseline. Last accepted epoch `HFI-004-2026-07-24` qualifies saved candidate `7c8a96e`; HGI-206 remains previous history. The active clean-slate plan owns pending qualification of today's graph. Neither saved epoch establishes current-checkout or external state. |\n| References | [`references/README.md`](references/README.md) | Revalidate mutable external guidance. |\n| Audit/accounting | [`documentation-audit/README.md`](documentation-audit/README.md) | Dated evidence, not policy. |\n\nFailed/inconclusive work retains provenance, last successful step, observed\nstate, escalation, resume trigger, recovery, and non-claims outside default\ncurrent routes. Do not delete or move historical/public/binary evidence without\nan approved retention manifest.\n\n## Maintenance\n\nEvery material slice decides `Change required`, `Preserve`, or `N/A` for docs,\nREADMEs, architecture, standards, public/generated references, runbooks,\nproof/evidence, skills, lint/config/CI, and active SPEC/tasks. Update the\nearliest durable owner and necessary pointers in the same slice. Counts prove\naccounting only; semantic and consumer claims need owner review and\nboundary-matched proof.\n\nUse the repository-local `$docs-maintainer` skill for this impact decision on\nboth PRD and ordinary changes. `$docs-writer` is limited to public-copy wording\nafter the maintenance route has selected the owner; it cannot close lifecycle,\ngenerated-content, package, proof, or validation work. Background freshness\nscans produce report-only candidates and cannot publish policy or documentation\nwithout separately attached implementation authority, review and publication\nidentity.\n\n`bun run check:docs` enforces the mechanical owner contract in\n[`../tools/documentation/owner-policy.json`](../tools/documentation/owner-policy.json).\nIt checks maintainer metadata, links, documented commands, workspace README\ncoverage, public/maintainer separation, accepted public-status representation,\nand generated-source edges with bounded diagnostics and a JSON detail receipt.\nThe command accepts `--json`; failed checks return a nonzero exit after the\nreport is saved. Effect CLI owns option parsing.\n`draft` means authored, locally renderable, visibly labelled candidate content;\n`published` means explicitly accepted current public documentation. Neither\nstatus proves runtime or external availability.\n\nAcceptance-record Schemas live in `@taxkit/content`. The docs tool explicitly\nselects source exports so it can run in a fresh checkout before package builds.\nVersion-two records include the reviewed source hash, which this check verifies;\nversion-one records retain their historical contract. The local accepted\ncatalogue builder, `bun run docs:catalogue`, requires version two, checks source\nbytes before and after compilation, and writes generated output only when\naccepted pages and matching navigation exist. It does not accept pages or\nestablish publication by running. See\n[`../packages/docs-content/README.md`](../packages/docs-content/README.md).\n\n`bun run check:runbooks` Schema-decodes the canonical runbook contract, the\ncurrent journey inventory and the exact historical HGI-203 journey snapshot,\nthen reconciles the immutable packet digest, four Markdown owners, commands,\nevidence paths, stop operations, index rows and authority rows. It writes only\nthe ignored bounded receipt `tmp/runbook-validation-report.json`, executes none\nof the documented procedures and establishes no consequential state.\n---\nname: docs-maintainer\ndescription: Audit and edit repository documentation so material code, configuration, API, infrastructure, CI, operational, skill, and SPEC changes update the correct semantic owners in the same implementation slice. Use for documentation maintenance, docs audits, stale or contradictory READMEs, documentation-impact assessment during implementation, and PRD writing/review/closeout. Preserve just-in-time context, distinguish skills from runbooks and durable docs from dated proof, and provide claim-matched verification. Do not use for public copywriting alone or to copy mutable provider state into repository docs.\n---\n\n# Documentation Maintainer\n\nKeep documentation aligned with repository behavior by updating the earliest\ndurable semantic owner and only the pointers that must lead to it.\n\n## Establish the local contract\n\n1. Read applicable `AGENTS.md`, inspect the worktree, and identify the exact\n   change, repository, environment, and write authority. Do not infer authority\n   to mutate providers, publish, release, or push from permission to edit docs.\n2. Read the repository-local `docs-maintainer` profile completely when one is\n   present at `references/repository-profile.md`. It owns repository paths,\n   commands, generated-document boundaries, mirrors, exceptions, and archive\n   policy. The global skill supplies method, never local truth.\n3. If no local profile exists, derive a temporary impact map from the root\n   `README*`, `docs/README*`, applicable package/app READMEs, active SPEC/tasks,\n   configuration, and changed implementation. Record missing ownership as a\n   gap; do not invent canonical paths or command names.\n4. Select an execution mode:\n   - **attached change:** when the user authorized implementation and repository\n     edits, edit affected documentation and task artifacts in the same slice;\n   - **audit or curator:** for scheduled/background freshness work, or when\n     mutation authority is absent, produce an isolated report-only candidate\n     with provenance and a proposed patch. Publication requires a separately\n     named responsible owner and publisher identity.\n\nNever let a curator publish its own uncorroborated findings or treat its prior\noutput as independent feedback. Pin any published context projection to an\nimmutable repository revision; refresh it only at a recorded phase boundary.\n\nKeep these truth layers distinct and apply the strongest applicable precedence:\nexternal system for current external state; shared store for shared source\nmaterial; immutable context projection for a recorded phase; repository code,\nconfig, and Schemas for desired state; durable docs for explanation and routing;\ndated evidence for observations; active SPEC/tasks for current intent and\nexecution. Link across layers instead of copying claims between them.\n\nFor a repository-wide documentation audit, substantial PRD, or cross-cutting\nharness change, read\n[repository-harness-contract.md](references/repository-harness-contract.md).\nIt routes to the complete local method and requires no external source lookup.\nLoad the applicable structured modules directly:\n\n- [contract map](references/harness/contract-map.md) for mode and lifecycle;\n- [invariant register](references/harness/invariant-register.md) for stable IDs;\n- [context and ownership](references/harness/context-and-ownership.md) for truth\n  layers, phased retrieval, and publication boundaries;\n- [proof and evaluation](references/harness/proof-and-evaluation.md) for\n  journeys, delivery, receipts, terminal states, and proportional evaluation;\n- [operations and authority](references/harness/operations-and-authority.md)\n  when runbooks, providers, controls, releases, or automation are in scope; and\n- [repository variation](references/harness/repository-variation.md) when\n  creating or changing the local profile.\n\nUse the Schemas and templates under `assets/harness/` for repository profiles,\ncritical journeys, bounded receipts, authority envelopes, and feedback or\nautomation controls. Do not replace those fixed field contracts with free-form\nprose.\nFor an ordinary localized documentation change, do not load that broader\ncontract unless an ownership, delivery, dependency, or proof question requires\nit. This skill owns the documentation track; use the sibling `repo-structure`\nskill for a complete repository audit.\n\n## Load context in phases\n\nUse just enough context to decide and then prove the change:\n\n1. **Ground:** read the change, directly affected docs/READMEs, the docs router,\n   the owning architecture or standard, and active task context.\n2. **Investigate:** inspect code, config, generated owners, history, provider\n   readback, or upstream material only to resolve an identified question.\n3. **Land:** inventory all affected docs, READMEs, skills, runbooks, references,\n   generated artifacts, indexes, and active/archive pointers. Reconcile every\n   contradiction on an affected route before closeout.\n\nDo not preload the whole repository for an ordinary localized change. A\nrepository-wide documentation audit or PRD review may require a full\n`docs/**` and `README*` accounting under its owning skill.\n\nFor a repository-wide audit, return documentation findings in the stable\nfinding format owned by the repository-audit procedure: consequence,\nevidence, semantic owner, root correction, duplicated guidance to retire,\naffected surfaces, proof, authority, limitations, and non-claims. Separate\nimportant corrections from optional improvements.\n\n## Build the impact ledger\n\nRead [document-classes.md](references/document-classes.md) to select semantic\nowners and [change-impact.md](references/change-impact.md) for the trigger\nmatrix. For each surface, record `Change required`, `Preserve`, or `N/A`, with:\n\n- changed behavior or claim;\n- semantic owner and required pointers;\n- exact affected path or narrowly bounded path set;\n- lifecycle transition, if any;\n- generated source and regeneration command, if applicable;\n- verification and observable postcondition;\n- proof location and explicit non-claims.\n\nCover docs, root/package/app READMEs, architecture/ADRs, standards, API and\ngenerated references, runbooks, critical journeys, proof/evidence, skills and\nagent instructions, lint/config/CI docs, migration/release notes, and active\nSPEC/tasks. Never accept a generic “update docs” item.\n\n## Edit the correct owner\n\n- Put durable design, invariants, and boundaries in architecture or standards.\n- Put exact repeatable operations in target-owned runbooks, including\n  preconditions, authority, sequential steps, receipts, rollback, and\n  escalation. Skills teach selection and judgment; they must route to rather\n  than copy runbooks.\n- Treat a procedure found in architecture or a README as an ownership defect,\n  not precedent to extend. Propose or create the target-owned runbook and leave\n  only durable rationale plus a pointer at the old location.\n- Put public setup and entry-point navigation in READMEs. Keep them short and\n  link to deeper owners.\n- Keep root `AGENTS.md` as a terse map of repository purpose/compatibility,\n  common operating loop, a small set of task classes or golden paths, and links\n  to their context, commands, and proof. Do not append completed-feature\n  histories or per-change atlas entries.\n- Put mutable external state and one-run observations in dated, addressable\n  evidence. Never present a provider response, deployment ID, secret age, or\n  current revision as durable repository truth.\n- Edit the source of generated documentation, run its real generator, and do\n  not hand-edit output unless repository policy explicitly says it is owned.\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Validate generated or existing package boundaries.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom render_package import validate_source_condition\n\n\nFORBIDDEN_SOURCE = {\n    \"generic SDK callback\": re.compile(r\"readonly\\s+(use|withClient)\\s*[:(]\"),\n    \"runtime class policy\": re.compile(r\"\\binstanceof\\b\"),\n    \"legacy Context tag\": re.compile(r\"Context\\.Tag\\b\"),\n    \"package-local runtime execution\": re.compile(r\"Effect\\.run(?:Promise|Sync)\\b\"),\n}\nPERSONAL_ROOT = \"/\" + \"Users\" + \"/\"\nRELATIVE_IMPORT = re.compile(r'''(?:\\bfrom\\s*|\\bimport\\s*\\(\\s*|\\bimport\\s*)[\"'](\\.[^\"']*)[\"']''')\n\n\ndef fail(message: str) -> None:\n    print(f\"ERROR: {message}\", file=sys.stderr)\n    raise SystemExit(1)\n\n\nroot = Path(sys.argv[1]).resolve(strict=True)\nfor path in root.rglob(\"*\"):\n    if not path.is_file():\n        continue\n    text = path.read_text(errors=\"ignore\")\n    if PERSONAL_ROOT in text:\n        fail(f\"{path.relative_to(root)} contains a personal absolute path\")\n    if re.search(r\"__[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*__|\\*\\*[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*\\*\\*\", text):\n        fail(f\"{path.relative_to(root)} contains an unresolved template token\")\nmanifest_path = root / \"package.json\"\nif not manifest_path.is_file():\n    fail(\"missing package.json\")\nmanifest = json.loads(manifest_path.read_text())\nrender_path = root / \"package-structure.render.json\"\nif not render_path.is_file():\n    fail(\"missing package-structure.render.json\")\nrender = json.loads(render_path.read_text())\ntry:\n    source_condition = validate_source_condition(render.get(\"sourceCondition\", \"\"))\nexcept (TypeError, ValueError) as error:\n    fail(str(error))\nkind = render.get(\"kind\")\nrequired_by_kind = {\n    \"effect-service\": {\n        \"src/schemas.ts\", \"src/errors.ts\", \"src/service.ts\", \"src/live.layer.ts\",\n        \"src/test.layer.ts\", \"src/__testing__/fixtures.ts\",\n        \"src/__testing__/observations.ts\", \"test/service.test.ts\", \"test/schemas.test.ts\",\n    },\n    \"rpc\": {\n        \"src/group.ts\", \"src/handlers.ts\", \"src/service.ts\", \"src/server.ts\",\n        \"src/live.layer.ts\", \"src/test.layer.ts\",\n    },\n    \"http-api\": {\n        \"src/api.ts\", \"src/group.ts\", \"src/handlers.ts\", \"src/server.ts\",\n        \"src/client/service.ts\", \"src/client/browser.layer.ts\",\n        \"src/client/live.layer.ts\",\n    },\n}\nif kind not in required_by_kind:\n    fail(f\"unknown rendered package kind: {kind}\")\nmissing = sorted(path for path in required_by_kind[kind] if not (root / path).is_file())\nif missing:\n    fail(f\"{kind} package missing required paths: {missing}\")\nif not render.get(\"officialSources\") or not render.get(\"compatibilityDecisions\"):\n    fail(\"render receipt lacks official sources or compatibility decisions\")\nif any(item.get(\"status\") != \"qualified\" for item in render[\"compatibilityDecisions\"]):\n    fail(\"render receipt contains an unqualified compatibility decision\")\nif not render.get(\"limitations\") or not render.get(\"nonClaims\"):\n    fail(\"render receipt lacks limitations or non-claims\")\nfor relative, expected in render.get(\"configDigests\", {}).items():\n    target = root / relative\n    observed = hashlib.sha256(target.read_bytes()).hexdigest() if target.is_file() else None\n    if observed != expected:\n        fail(f\"rendered config digest mismatch: {relative}\")\nexports = manifest.get(\"exports\")\nif not isinstance(exports, dict) or not exports:\n    fail(\"package exports must be explicit\")\nreadme = (root / \"README.md\").read_text()\nfor heading in (\"## Exports\", \"## Documentation impact\", \"## Runbook applicability\", \"## Non-claims\"):\n    if heading not in readme:\n        fail(f\"README missing required section: {heading}\")\nfor export_name in exports:\n    if f\"`{export_name}`\" not in readme:\n        fail(f\"README must document exact export {export_name}\")\nfor phrase in (\"repository\", \"runbook\", \"proof\"):\n    if phrase not in readme.lower():\n        fail(f\"README must route {phrase} ownership\")\npublish = manifest.get(\"publishConfig\", {}).get(\"exports\", {})\nsource_conditions: set[str] = set()\nfor name, value in exports.items():\n    if not isinstance(value, dict):\n        fail(f\"export {name} must be an object\")\n    keys = list(value)\n    if not keys or keys[0] != source_condition:\n        fail(f\"export {name} must place recorded source condition first: {source_condition}\")\n    source_target = value[source_condition]\n    if not isinstance(source_target, str) or not source_target.startswith(\"./src/\") or not (root / source_target).is_file():\n        fail(f\"export {name} recorded source condition must target an existing source file\")\n    conditions = [key for key in keys if key not in {\"types\", \"default\", \"import\"}]\n    source_conditions.update(conditions)\n    for condition in conditions:\n        target = value[condition]\n        if isinstance(target, str) and target.startswith(\"./src\"):\n            if keys.index(condition) > keys.index(\"types\"):\n                fail(f\"export {name} must place source before types\")\n            if not (root / target).is_file():\n                fail(f\"export {name} source target does not exist: {target}\")\n    if \"types\" in value and \"default\" in value and keys.index(\"types\") > keys.index(\"default\"):\n        fail(f\"export {name} must place types before default\")\nfor value in publish.values() if isinstance(publish, dict) else []:\n    if isinstance(value, dict) and source_conditions.intersection(value):\n        fail(\"publish exports must omit repository source conditions\")\nfor directory in (\"src\", \"test\"):\n    for path in (root / directory).rglob(\"*.ts\"):\n        for specifier in RELATIVE_IMPORT.findall(path.read_text()):\n            if not specifier.endswith(\".js\"):\n                fail(f\"{path.relative_to(root)} relative import must use an explicit .js suffix: {specifier}\")\nfor path in (root / \"src\").rglob(\"*.ts\"):\n    text = path.read_text()\n    for label, pattern in FORBIDDEN_SOURCE.items():\n        if pattern.search(text):\n            fail(f\"{path.relative_to(root)} contains {label}\")\n    if re.search(r\"\\bid\\s*[?:]?\\s*:\\s*string\\b\", text):\n        fail(f\"{path.relative_to(root)} contains a raw semantic id\")\n    if re.search(r'from\\s+[\"\\']effect/unstable/(?:rpc|httpapi)/(?!Rpc(?:ClientError|Group|Test)?[\"\\'])', text):\n        fail(f\"{path.relative_to(root)} contains a substituted upstream Effect import\")\nfor path in (root / \"src\").rglob(\"*\"):\n    if path.is_file() and path.stem.lower() in {\"helper\", \"helpers\", \"util\", \"utils\"}:\n        fail(f\"{path.relative_to(root)} is generic helper sprawl; name the owned capability\")\nservice = root / \"src/service.ts\"\nif service.is_file():\n"},"started_at_ms":1791370198827,"completed_at_ms":1791370198827}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:49:58.879Z","ordinal":68664,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a115fb-ff5f-7bd3-aaef-6b1dac93a53c","call_id":"call_3JCACuHeW1VRYbS4i1rrLGur","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"c18301\",\"wall_time_seconds\":1.003297417,\"session_id\":69957,\"original_token_count\":0,\"output\":\"\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"5823f8\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007292,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":6081,\"output\":\"{\\n  \\\"schemaVersion\\\": 1,\\n  \\\"kind\\\": \\\"effect-service\\\",\\n  \\\"packageName\\\": \\\"@taxkit/analytics\\\",\\n  \\\"domainPackage\\\": null,\\n  \\\"sourceCondition\\\": \\\"source\\\",\\n  \\\"versionSnapshot\\\": {\\n    \\\"resolvedAt\\\": \\\"2026-10-07\\\",\\n    \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"263bd13f098099137c1ea2cd204e2920a41c5a8ddc22dba49724d9285aa80a12\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"officialSources\\\": {\\n    \\\"effect\\\": \\\"https://registry.npmjs.org/effect/4.0.0\\\",\\n    \\\"vitest\\\": \\\"https://registry.npmjs.org/vitest/5.0.3\\\",\\n    \\\"typescript\\\": \\\"https://registry.npmjs.org/typescript/7.0.2\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"selectedVersions\\\": {\\n    \\\"effect\\\": \\\"4.0.0\\\",\\n    \\\"@effect/vitest\\\": \\\"4.0.0\\\",\\n    \\\"typescript\\\": \\\"7.0.2\\\",\\n    \\\"vitest\\\": \\\"5.0.3\\\",\\n    \\\"@effect/platform-bun\\\": \\\"4.0.0\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"compatibilityDecisions\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"qualified\\\",\\n      \\\"decision\\\": \\\"Reuse TaxKit T002 stable Effect 4.0.0 dependency qualification and installed types; rendered source is a scaffold and needs real TaxKit type/lint/tests before acceptance\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"configDigests\\\": {\\n    \\\"package.json\\\": \\\"1ee730f376aa3675eee314d99c24564d3dfaec5215387106cb46981dbafbf4ca\\\",\\n    \\\"tsconfig.json\\\": \\\"71596163cd8ffea16eb4950049bc772ec8a8e2db408759c80bc8232aa40a6d99\\\",\\n    \\\"tsconfig.build.json\\\": \\\"320b70b4115224df6a42038a8759a444d0feecabb0666c22a519904a1e9b9de9\\\",\\n    \\\"vitest.config.ts\\\": \\\"8167d20931f3f88793a6253697dad0c2dc7a519ca7d4ec8aea6c2ffc9f1448b7\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"limitations\\\": [\\n    \\\"Structural rendering does not prove installed dependency, declaration, runtime, or packed-consumer behavior.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"nonClaims\\\": [\\\"Selected versions are not claimed to remain latest.\\\"]\\n}\\n---\\ndocument_type: documentation-router\\nlifecycle: current\\nauthority: canonical\\nowner: taxkit-documentation-owner\\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-07\\nreview_trigger: any maintainer/public docs class, root route, SPEC, plan, runbook, proof, evidence, or lifecycle change\\n---\\n\\n# TaxKit documentation\\n\\nThis is the sole router for maintainer-document type, lifecycle, truth layers,\\nand semantic ownership. Root `README.md` is the public repository entry point;\\n`AGENTS.md` is the short task map; `docs/architecture/README.md` is the current\\narchitecture route. Public documentation content is a separate product surface\\nowned by the replacement `apps/web`, backend content contracts and docs\\npackages. The old `apps/docs` workspace is retired. Its tombstone routes to the verified\\nsource bundle and dated provider recovery records; no provider operation is\\nauthorised by that retained history.\\n\\n## Truth layers\\n\\nUse the strongest applicable owner and link rather than copy:\\n\\n1. External systems own their current external state at readback time.\\n2. Code, configuration, Schemas, package exports, workflows, and generated\\n   sources own desired/executable state.\\n3. Architecture and standards own durable boundaries and enforceable policy.\\n4. Dated proof/evidence owns one artifact/environment/authority observation and\\n   its limitations.\\n5. Active SPEC/tasks and execution plans own current implementation intent.\\n\\nProvider/registry output cannot grant authority. Completed plans are history.\\nLocal release checks do not prove npm publication or external consumers.\\n\\n## Metadata and lifecycle\\n\\nNew or materially revised maintainer docs separate `document_type`,\\n`lifecycle`, `authority`, and `owner`. Current durable docs also record\\n`last_reviewed` and `review_trigger`; superseded/tombstone docs record a\\nsuccessor and reason.\\n\\nLifecycle values are `proposed`, `current`, `implemented`, `superseded`,\\n`historical`, `evidence`, `reference`, `failed`, `inconclusive`, `tombstone`,\\nand `archived`. Authority values are `canonical`, `supporting`, `generated`,\\nand `external`. Legacy `status: canonical` is an authority marker, not a\\nlifecycle; migrate it only when its owner is materially revised.\\n\\n## Routes\\n\\n| Need | Owner | Use |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Architecture | [`architecture/README.md`](architecture/README.md) | Current architecture route. `architecture.md` is a tombstone only. |\\n| Standards | [`standards/README.md`](standards/README.md) | Current durable engineering/documentation rules. |\\n| Current intent | [`product-specs/index.md`](product-specs/index.md) and [`exec-plans/active/README.md`](exec-plans/active/README.md) | Only genuinely active work; implemented/history stays inventory. |\\n| Completed history | [`exec-plans/completed/README.md`](exec-plans/completed/README.md) | Historical provenance, never default policy. |\\n| Public docs product | [`../apps/web/README.md`](../apps/web/README.md), [`../packages/docs-content/README.md`](../packages/docs-content/README.md), and [`../packages/docs-fumadocs/README.md`](../packages/docs-fumadocs/README.md) | Consumer-facing content/runtime, not maintainer lifecycle policy. |\\n| Repeatable release/deployment/recovery operations | [`runbooks/README.md`](runbooks/README.md) and [`operations/authority-model.md`](operations/authority-model.md) | Exactly five target-owned procedures; stop consequential operations when principal, candidate, target or receipt is unknown. |\\n| CI controls and recurring automation | [`standards/controls.md`](standards/controls.md) and [`operations/automation-register.md`](operations/automation-register.md) | Quality workflow admission, release-graph controls, and report-only candidate boundaries; neither route grants external authority. |\\n| Verification/critical journeys/proof | [`architecture/testing-and-quality.md`](architecture/testing-and-quality.md), [`verification/critical-journeys.json`](verification/critical-journeys.json), [`evidence/releases/HGI-203-critical-journeys.json`](evidence/releases/HGI-203-critical-journeys.json), [`evidence/releases/HGI-203-local.json`](evidence/releases/HGI-203-local.json), and [`documentation-audit/HGI-203-validation.json`](documentation-audit/HGI-203-validation.json) | The current inventory owns evolving journeys. Accepted HGI-203 retains the exact historical five-journey snapshot and bounded local proof that its immutable packet observed; HGI-204 validates both epochs without attributing current changes to the old attempt. Raw logs and secrets are never durable proof. |\\n| Harness foundation and requalification | [`verification/repository-harness-profile.json`](verification/repository-harness-profile.json), [`documentation-audit/harness-foundation/accepted-findings.json`](documentation-audit/harness-foundation/accepted-findings.json), [`verification/harness-epochs.md`](verification/harness-epochs.md), and [`verification/effectiveness.md`](verification/effectiveness.md) | The TaxKit profile, accepted HE crosswalk, content-addressed skill receipt and focused gate own the implemented baseline. Last accepted epoch `HFI-004-2026-07-24` qualifies saved candidate `7c8a96e`; HGI-206 remains previous history. The active clean-slate plan owns pending qualification of today's graph. Neither saved epoch establishes current-checkout or external state. |\\n| References | [`references/README.md`](references/README.md) | Revalidate mutable external guidance. |\\n| Audit/accounting | [`documentation-audit/README.md`](documentation-audit/README.md) | Dated evidence, not policy. |\\n\\nFailed/inconclusive work retains provenance, last successful step, observed\\nstate, escalation, resume trigger, recovery, and non-claims outside default\\ncurrent routes. Do not delete or move historical/public/binary evidence without\\nan approved retention manifest.\\n\\n## Maintenance\\n\\nEvery material slice decides `Change required`, `Preserve`, or `N/A` for docs,\\nREADMEs, architecture, standards, public/generated references, runbooks,\\nproof/evidence, skills, lint/config/CI, and active SPEC/tasks. Update the\\nearliest durable owner and necessary pointers in the same slice. Counts prove\\naccounting only; semantic and consumer claims need owner review and\\nboundary-matched proof.\\n\\nUse the repository-local `$docs-maintainer` skill for this impact decision on\\nboth PRD and ordinary changes. `$docs-writer` is limited to public-copy wording\\nafter the maintenance route has selected the owner; it cannot close lifecycle,\\ngenerated-content, package, proof, or validation work. Background freshness\\nscans produce report-only candidates and cannot publish policy or documentation\\nwithout separately attached implementation authority, review and publication\\nidentity.\\n\\n`bun run check:docs` enforces the mechanical owner contract in\\n[`../tools/documentation/owner-policy.json`](../tools/documentation/owner-policy.json).\\nIt checks maintainer metadata, links, documented commands, workspace README\\ncoverage, public/maintainer separation, accepted public-status representation,\\nand generated-source edges with bounded diagnostics and a JSON detail receipt.\\nThe command accepts `--json`; failed checks return a nonzero exit after the\\nreport is saved. Effect CLI owns option parsing.\\n`draft` means authored, locally renderable, visibly labelled candidate content;\\n`published` means explicitly accepted current public documentation. Neither\\nstatus proves runtime or external availability.\\n\\nAcceptance-record Schemas live in `@taxkit/content`. The docs tool explicitly\\nselects source exports so it can run in a fresh checkout before package builds.\\nVersion-two records include the reviewed source hash, which this check verifies;\\nversion-one records retain their historical contract. The local accepted\\ncatalogue builder, `bun run docs:catalogue`, requires version two, checks source\\nbytes before and after compilation, and writes generated output only when\\naccepted pages and matching navigation exist. It does not accept pages or\\nestablish publication by running. See\\n[`../packages/docs-content/README.md`](../packages/docs-content/README.md).\\n\\n`bun run check:runbooks` Schema-decodes the canonical runbook contract, the\\ncurrent journey inventory and the exact historical HGI-203 journey snapshot,\\nthen reconciles the immutable packet digest, four Markdown owners, commands,\\nevidence paths, stop operations, index rows and authority rows. It writes only\\nthe ignored bounded receipt `tmp/runbook-validation-report.json`, executes none\\nof the documented procedures and establishes no consequential state.\\n---\\nname: docs-maintainer\\ndescription: Audit and edit repository documentation so material code, configuration, API, infrastructure, CI, operational, skill, and SPEC changes update the correct semantic owners in the same implementation slice. Use for documentation maintenance, docs audits, stale or contradictory READMEs, documentation-impact assessment during implementation, and PRD writing/review/closeout. Preserve just-in-time context, distinguish skills from runbooks and durable docs from dated proof, and provide claim-matched verification. Do not use for public copywriting alone or to copy mutable provider state into repository docs.\\n---\\n\\n# Documentation Maintainer\\n\\nKeep documentation aligned with repository behavior by updating the earliest\\ndurable semantic owner and only the pointers that must lead to it.\\n\\n## Establish the local contract\\n\\n1. Read applicable `AGENTS.md`, inspect the worktree, and identify the exact\\n   change, repository, environment, and write authority. Do not infer authority\\n   to mutate providers, publish, release, or push from permission to edit docs.\\n2. Read the repository-local `docs-maintainer` profile completely when one is\\n   present at `references/repository-profile.md`. It owns repository paths,\\n   commands, generated-document boundaries, mirrors, exceptions, and archive\\n   policy. The global skill supplies method, never local truth.\\n3. If no local profile exists, derive a temporary impact map from the root\\n   `README*`, `docs/README*`, applicable package/app READMEs, active SPEC/tasks,\\n   configuration, and changed implementation. Record missing ownership as a\\n   gap; do not invent canonical paths or command names.\\n4. Select an execution mode:\\n   - **attached change:** when the user authorized implementation and repository\\n     edits, edit affected documentation and task artifacts in the same slice;\\n   - **audit or curator:** for scheduled/background freshness work, or when\\n     mutation authority is absent, produce an isolated report-only candidate\\n     with provenance and a proposed patch. Publication requires a separately\\n     named responsible owner and publisher identity.\\n\\nNever let a curator publish its own uncorroborated findings or treat its prior\\noutput as independent feedback. Pin any published context projection to an\\nimmutable repository revision; refresh it only at a recorded phase boundary.\\n\\nKeep these truth layers distinct and apply the strongest applicable precedence:\\nexternal system for current external state; shared store for shared source\\nmaterial; immutable context projection for a recorded phase; repository code,\\nconfig, and Schemas for desired state; durable docs for explanation and routing;\\ndated evidence for observations; active SPEC/tasks for current intent and\\nexecution. Link across layers instead of copying claims between them.\\n\\nFor a repository-wide documentation audit, substantial PRD, or cross-cutting\\nharness change, read\\n[repository-harness-contract.md](references/repository-harness-contract.md).\\nIt routes to the complete local method and requires no external source lookup.\\nLoad the applicable structured modules directly:\\n\\n- [contract map](references/harness/contract-map.md) for mode and lifecycle;\\n- [invariant register](references/harness/invariant-register.md) for stable IDs;\\n- [context and ownership](references/harness/context-and-ownership.md) for truth\\n  layers, phased retrieval, and publication boundaries;\\n- [proof and evaluation](references/harness/proof-and-evaluation.md) for\\n  journeys, delivery, receipts, terminal states, and proportional evaluation;\\n- [operations and authority](references/harness/operations-and-authority.md)\\n  when runbooks, providers, controls, releases, or automation are in scope; and\\n- [repository variation](references/harness/repository-variation.md) when\\n  creating or changing the local profile.\\n\\nUse the Schemas and templates under `assets/harness/` for repository profiles,\\ncritical journeys, bounded receipts, authority envelopes, and feedback or\\nautomation controls. Do not replace those fixed field contracts with free-form\\nprose.\\nFor an ordinary localized documentation change, do not load that broader\\ncontract unless an ownership, delivery, dependency, or proof question requires\\nit. This skill owns the documentation track; use the sibling `repo-structure`\\nskill for a complete repository audit.\\n\\n## Load context in phases\\n\\nUse just enough context to decide and then prove the change:\\n\\n1. **Ground:** read the change, directly affected docs/READMEs, the docs router,\\n   the owning architecture or standard, and active task context.\\n2. **Investigate:** inspect code, config, generated owners, history, provider\\n   readback, or upstream material only to resolve an identified question.\\n3. **Land:** inventory all affected docs, READMEs, skills, runbooks, references,\\n   generated artifacts, indexes, and active/archive pointers. Reconcile every\\n   contradiction on an affected route before closeout.\\n\\nDo not preload the whole repository for an ordinary localized change. A\\nrepository-wide documentation audit or PRD review may require a full\\n`docs/**` and `README*` accounting under its owning skill.\\n\\nFor a repository-wide audit, return documentation findings in the stable\\nfinding format owned by the repository-audit procedure: consequence,\\nevidence, semantic owner, root correction, duplicated guidance to retire,\\naffected surfaces, proof, authority, limitations, and non-claims. Separate\\nimportant corrections from optional improvements.\\n\\n## Build the impact ledger\\n\\nRead [document-classes.md](references/document-classes.md) to select semantic\\nowners and [change-impact.md](references/change-impact.md) for the trigger\\nmatrix. For each surface, record `Change required`, `Preserve`, or `N/A`, with:\\n\\n- changed behavior or claim;\\n- semantic owner and required pointers;\\n- exact affected path or narrowly bounded path set;\\n- lifecycle transition, if any;\\n- generated source and regeneration command, if applicable;\\n- verification and observable postcondition;\\n- proof location and explicit non-claims.\\n\\nCover docs, root/package/app READMEs, architecture/ADRs, standards, API and\\ngenerated references, runbooks, critical journeys, proof/evidence, skills and\\nagent instructions, lint/config/CI docs, migration/release notes, and active\\nSPEC/tasks. Never accept a generic “update docs” item.\\n\\n## Edit the correct owner\\n\\n- Put durable design, invariants, and boundaries in architecture or standards.\\n- Put exact repeatable operations in target-owned runbooks, including\\n  preconditions, authority, sequential steps, receipts, rollback, and\\n  escalation. Skills teach selection and judgment; they must route to rather\\n  than copy runbooks.\\n- Treat a procedure found in architecture or a README as an ownership defect,\\n  not precedent to extend. Propose or create the target-owned runbook and leave\\n  only durable rationale plus a pointer at the old location.\\n- Put public setup and entry-point navigation in READMEs. Keep them short and\\n  link to deeper owners.\\n- Keep root `AGENTS.md` as a terse map of repository purpose/compatibility,\\n  common operating loop, a small set of task classes or golden paths, and links\\n  to their context, commands, and proof. Do not append completed-feature\\n  histories or per-change atlas entries.\\n- Put mutable external state and one-run observations in dated, addressable\\n  evidence. Never present a provider response, deployment ID, secret age, or\\n  current revision as durable repository truth.\\n- Edit the source of generated documentation, run its real generator, and do\\n  not hand-edit output unless repository policy explicitly says it is owned.\\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Validate generated or existing package boundaries.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport hashlib\\nimport json\\nimport re\\nimport sys\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\n\\nfrom render_package import validate_source_condition\\n\\n\\nFORBIDDEN_SOURCE = {\\n    \\\"generic SDK callback\\\": re.compile(r\\\"readonly\\\\s+(use|withClient)\\\\s*[:(]\\\"),\\n    \\\"runtime class policy\\\": re.compile(r\\\"\\\\binstanceof\\\\b\\\"),\\n    \\\"legacy Context tag\\\": re.compile(r\\\"Context\\\\.Tag\\\\b\\\"),\\n    \\\"package-local runtime execution\\\": re.compile(r\\\"Effect\\\\.run(?:Promise|Sync)\\\\b\\\"),\\n}\\nPERSONAL_ROOT = \\\"/\\\" + \\\"Users\\\" + \\\"/\\\"\\nRELATIVE_IMPORT = re.compile(r'''(?:\\\\bfrom\\\\s*|\\\\bimport\\\\s*\\\\(\\\\s*|\\\\bimport\\\\s*)[\\\"'](\\\\.[^\\\"']*)[\\\"']''')\\n\\n\\ndef fail(message: str) -> None:\\n    print(f\\\"ERROR: {message}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n    raise SystemExit(1)\\n\\n\\nroot = Path(sys.argv[1]).resolve(strict=True)\\nfor path in root.rglob(\\\"*\\\"):\\n    if not path.is_file():\\n        continue\\n    text = path.read_text(errors=\\\"ignore\\\")\\n    if PERSONAL_ROOT in text:\\n        fail(f\\\"{path.relative_to(root)} contains a personal absolute path\\\")\\n    if re.search(r\\\"__[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*__|\\\\*\\\\*[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*\\\\*\\\\*\\\", text):\\n        fail(f\\\"{path.relative_to(root)} contains an unresolved template token\\\")\\nmanifest_path = root / \\\"package.json\\\"\\nif not manifest_path.is_file():\\n    fail(\\\"missing package.json\\\")\\nmanifest = json.loads(manifest_path.read_text())\\nrender_path = root / \\\"package-structure.render.json\\\"\\nif not render_path.is_file():\\n    fail(\\\"missing package-structure.render.json\\\")\\nrender = json.loads(render_path.read_text())\\ntry:\\n    source_condition = validate_source_condition(render.get(\\\"sourceCondition\\\", \\\"\\\"))\\nexcept (TypeError, ValueError) as error:\\n    fail(str(error))\\nkind = render.get(\\\"kind\\\")\\nrequired_by_kind = {\\n    \\\"effect-service\\\": {\\n        \\\"src/schemas.ts\\\", \\\"src/errors.ts\\\", \\\"src/service.ts\\\", \\\"src/live.layer.ts\\\",\\n        \\\"src/test.layer.ts\\\", \\\"src/__testing__/fixtures.ts\\\",\\n        \\\"src/__testing__/observations.ts\\\", \\\"test/service.test.ts\\\", \\\"test/schemas.test.ts\\\",\\n    },\\n    \\\"rpc\\\": {\\n        \\\"src/group.ts\\\", \\\"src/handlers.ts\\\", \\\"src/service.ts\\\", \\\"src/server.ts\\\",\\n        \\\"src/live.layer.ts\\\", \\\"src/test.layer.ts\\\",\\n    },\\n    \\\"http-api\\\": {\\n        \\\"src/api.ts\\\", \\\"src/group.ts\\\", \\\"src/handlers.ts\\\", \\\"src/server.ts\\\",\\n        \\\"src/client/service.ts\\\", \\\"src/client/browser.layer.ts\\\",\\n        \\\"src/client/live.layer.ts\\\",\\n    },\\n}\\nif kind not in required_by_kind:\\n    fail(f\\\"unknown rendered package kind: {kind}\\\")\\nmissing = sorted(path for path in required_by_kind[kind] if not (root / path).is_file())\\nif missing:\\n    fail(f\\\"{kind} package missing required paths: {missing}\\\")\\nif not render.get(\\\"officialSources\\\") or not render.get(\\\"compatibilityDecisions\\\"):\\n    fail(\\\"render receipt lacks official sources or compatibility decisions\\\")\\nif any(item.get(\\\"status\\\") != \\\"qualified\\\" for item in render[\\\"compatibilityDecisions\\\"]):\\n    fail(\\\"render receipt contains an unqualified compatibility decision\\\")\\nif not render.get(\\\"limitations\\\") or not render.get(\\\"nonClaims\\\"):\\n    fail(\\\"render receipt lacks limitations or non-claims\\\")\\nfor relative, expected in render.get(\\\"configDigests\\\", {}).items():\\n    target = root / relative\\n    observed = hashlib.sha256(target.read_bytes()).hexdigest() if target.is_file() else None\\n    if observed != expected:\\n        fail(f\\\"rendered config digest mismatch: {relative}\\\")\\nexports = manifest.get(\\\"exports\\\")\\nif not isinstance(exports, dict) or not exports:\\n    fail(\\\"package exports must be explicit\\\")\\nreadme = (root / \\\"README.md\\\").read_text()\\nfor heading in (\\\"## Exports\\\", \\\"## Documentation impact\\\", \\\"## Runbook applicability\\\", \\\"## Non-claims\\\"):\\n    if heading not in readme:\\n        fail(f\\\"README missing required section: {heading}\\\")\\nfor export_name in exports:\\n    if f\\\"`{export_name}`\\\" not in readme:\\n        fail(f\\\"README must document exact export {export_name}\\\")\\nfor phrase in (\\\"repository\\\", \\\"runbook\\\", \\\"proof\\\"):\\n    if phrase not in readme.lower():\\n        fail(f\\\"README must route {phrase} ownership\\\")\\npublish = manifest.get(\\\"publishConfig\\\", {}).get(\\\"exports\\\", {})\\nsource_conditions: set[str] = set()\\nfor name, value in exports.items():\\n    if not isinstance(value, dict):\\n        fail(f\\\"export {name} must be an object\\\")\\n    keys = list(value)\\n    if not keys or keys[0] != source_condition:\\n        fail(f\\\"export {name} must place recorded source condition first: {source_condition}\\\")\\n    source_target = value[source_condition]\\n    if not isinstance(source_target, str) or not source_target.startswith(\\\"./src/\\\") or not (root / source_target).is_file():\\n        fail(f\\\"export {name} recorded source condition must target an existing source file\\\")\\n    conditions = [key for key in keys if key not in {\\\"types\\\", \\\"default\\\", \\\"import\\\"}]\\n    source_conditions.update(conditions)\\n    for condition in conditions:\\n        target = value[condition]\\n        if isinstance(target, str) and target.startswith(\\\"./src\\\"):\\n            if keys.index(condition) > keys.index(\\\"types\\\"):\\n                fail(f\\\"export {name} must place source before types\\\")\\n            if not (root / target).is_file():\\n                fail(f\\\"export {name} source target does not exist: {target}\\\")\\n    if \\\"types\\\" in value and \\\"default\\\" in value and keys.index(\\\"types\\\") > keys.index(\\\"default\\\"):\\n        fail(f\\\"export {name} must place types before default\\\")\\nfor value in publish.values() if isinstance(publish, dict) else []:\\n    if isinstance(value, dict) and source_conditions.intersection(value):\\n        fail(\\\"publish exports must omit repository source conditions\\\")\\nfor directory in (\\\"src\\\", \\\"test\\\"):\\n    for path in (root / directory).rglob(\\\"*.ts\\\"):\\n        for specifier in RELATIVE_IMPORT.findall(path.read_text()):\\n            if not specifier.endswith(\\\".js\\\"):\\n                fail(f\\\"{path.relative_to(root)} relative import must use an explicit .js suffix: {specifier}\\\")\\nfor path in (root / \\\"src\\\").rglob(\\\"*.ts\\\"):\\n    text = path.read_text()\\n    for label, pattern in FORBIDDEN_SOURCE.items():\\n        if pattern.search(text):\\n            fail(f\\\"{path.relative_to(root)} contains {label}\\\")\\n    if re.search(r\\\"\\\\bid\\\\s*[?:]?\\\\s*:\\\\s*string\\\\b\\\", text):\\n        fail(f\\\"{path.relative_to(root)} contains a raw semantic id\\\")\\n    if re.search(r'from\\\\s+[\\\"\\\\']effect/unstable/(?:rpc|httpapi)/(?!Rpc(?:ClientError|Group|Test)?[\\\"\\\\'])', text):\\n        fail(f\\\"{path.relative_to(root)} contains a substituted upstream Effect import\\\")\\nfor path in (root / \\\"src\\\").rglob(\\\"*\\\"):\\n    if path.is_file() and path.stem.lower() in {\\\"helper\\\", \\\"helpers\\\", \\\"util\\\", \\\"utils\\\"}:\\n        fail(f\\\"{path.relative_to(root)} is generic helper sprawl; name the owned capability\\\")\\nservice = root / \\\"src/service.ts\\\"\\nif service.is_file():\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","create_time":1791370198.879098}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
