{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:54:17.680Z","ordinal":68777,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac624d853a487d08354af8cd12e3a86","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The new tests use the built app with a controlled analytics server, so they send nothing to PostHog. They check that tax results still return promptly when the server fails, redirects or leaves its reply unfinished.\n"}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1791370456353,"completed_at_ms":1791370457680}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:54:17.684Z","ordinal":68778,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac624d853a487d08354af8cd12e3a86","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The new tests use the built app with a controlled analytics server, so they send nothing to PostHog. They check that tax results still return promptly when the server fails, redirects or leaves its reply unfinished.\n"}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","create_time":1791370452.04732,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac624d853a487d08354af8cd12e3a86","turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a115ff-f253-7c71-b4c8-9829c4b37475","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":1447}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:54:20.866Z","ordinal":68779,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac624d99b5887d0a063db89d5f8b191","status":"completed","call_id":"call_6WrnehqfDZDKLiZGGs4bR79s","name":"exec","input":"const result=await tools.mcp__codex_apps__linear_get_issue({id:\"DEV-79\",includeRelations:true});\nstore(\"dev79-latest-issue\",result);\ntext(result);\ntext(await tools.write_stdin({session_id:73791,chars:\"\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:1000}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '101,125p' .agents/skills/package-structure/SKILL.md; rg -n '^##|PostHog|Analytics' docs/architecture/frontend.md apps/web/README.md; cat packages/analytics/tsconfig.json; cat packages/analytics/tsconfig.build.json; cat packages/analytics/vitest.config.ts\",\"max_output_tokens\":1500}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","create_time":1791370452.04732}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:54:20.908Z","ordinal":68780,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","session_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","root_turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","response_id":"resp_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac624d399f487d086d58d71e96dfdd9","usage":{"input_tokens":129261,"cached_input_tokens":128384,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":273,"reasoning_output_tokens":56,"total_tokens":129534},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":49686628,"cached_input_tokens":48651136,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":250123,"reasoning_output_tokens":95060,"total_tokens":49936751},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1286196830,"cached_input_tokens":1259674624,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":6388185,"reasoning_output_tokens":2844897,"total_tokens":1292585015}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:54:21.487Z","ordinal":68781,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","item":{"type":"McpToolCall","id":"exec-17d4741d-396d-4106-8adc-c06bf5599dfa","server":"codex_apps","tool":"linear.get_issue","arguments":{"id":"DEV-79","includeRelations":true},"connectorId":"asdk_app_69a089a326dc8191b32a3f2553f5be2c","linkId":"link_6ac0779f5b188191860fcae4d4b097aa","appName":"Linear","actionName":"get_issue","readOnlyHint":true,"status":"completed","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"DEV-79\",\"uuid\":\"85150329-9061-4690-8f80-bfbc7af57ebe\",\"title\":\"CSF-T008 — Track visits and calculator choice with minimal PostHog events\",\"description\":\"This issue tracks `CSF-T008` in the clean-slate rebuild plan.\\n\\nCooper wants traffic and calculator-use counts without sending the figures people enter or adding consent dialogs.\\n\\nWork to do:\\n\\n* Manage TaxKit Production and shared Preview PostHog projects through Alchemy with checked ownership and region.\\n* Send explicit pageviews from the website and one calculator_used event from the backend after a successful hosted calculation. Record which calculator was used, never its inputs or answer.\\n* Use a checked final field allowlist, memory-only browser identity and Do Not Track support. Disable automatic clicks, profiles, recordings and other unwanted capture; keep ordinary local/Preview capture off.\\n* Use the bounded same-origin event relay and owned Effect HTTP operations. Check the actual SDK transport, enrichment, retry identity and disposal so adapters do not count one action twice.\\n\\nAccept when:\\n\\n* Actual outbound payloads contain only approved page/usage fields, with no tax figures, free text or persistent browser identity.\\n* A successful calculation has one event owner; pure tax packages and local SDK use send no analytics.\\n* No consent dialog is introduced. Any provider event readback is proved separately in an approved Preview.\\n\\nRequired commands are recorded in the owning task: `bun run test`, `bun run test:oxlint`, `bun run check-types`, `bun run build`, `bun run check:docs`, `bun run check:runbooks`, `bun run verification`.\\n\\nDepends on `CSF-T004`, `CSF-T005`, `CSF-T006`. These will also be saved as native issue blockers.\\n\\nImplementation has started under Cooper’s approved continuation; the old whole-design hold is superseded. The prerequisite slices are locally accepted and delivered as reviewable drafts, including the deployed agent guide in <pull-request id=\\\"ebc88fb2-91a4-4b08-b8a7-503c330a40e5\\\" href=\\\"https://linear.app/coopers-personal/review/dev-77-document-agent-setup-and-tested-cancellation-limits-4a0a6d3df773\\\">crcorbett/taxkit#162</pull-request> and checked deployment handover in <pull-request id=\\\"cf1c9900-6ac0-49aa-84a5-26d6fd1cff23\\\" href=\\\"https://linear.app/coopers-personal/review/dev-78-align-native-deployment-handover-with-tested-local-operations-9525610e0f85\\\">crcorbett/taxkit#163</pull-request>. Current PostHog browser SDK 1.438.2 and Distilled 1.0.0-rc.13 have been read from their official registry archives; installed Effect/Alchemy compatibility and actual transport still need local qualification. Read-only preparation finds the Cooper US organisation but no TaxKit project among its six accessible projects, and no PostHog configuration in taxkit/prd or taxkit/stg_preview. Prepare the private event rules, one backend successful-use owner, browser lifetime and bounded relay locally. Local/ordinary Preview capture stays disabled. New project setup, management credential and exact stored-event proof remain separate concrete provider operations; no provider or credential has been changed. Metrics remain deferred.\\n\\nOwning [task and checks](<https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/blob/8ed03f0e1a96d2cc258b68935b9f9be443666e1b/docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json#L607>), [design](<https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/blob/8ed03f0e1a96d2cc258b68935b9f9be443666e1b/docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md>) and [planning commit](<https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/commit/8ed03f0e1a96d2cc258b68935b9f9be443666e1b>).\",\"priority\":{\"value\":0,\"name\":\"No priority\"},\"url\":\"https://linear.app/coopers-personal/issue/DEV-79/csf-t008-track-visits-and-calculator-choice-with-minimal-posthog\",\"gitBranchName\":\"coopercorbett/dev-79-csf-t008-track-visits-and-calculator-choice-with-minimal\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-04T00:14:08.681Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-07T10:10:06.422Z\",\"archivedAt\":null,\"completedAt\":null,\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-07T10:10:06.397Z\",\"canceledAt\":null,\"dueDate\":null,\"slaStartedAt\":null,\"slaMediumRiskAt\":null,\"slaHighRiskAt\":null,\"slaBreachesAt\":null,\"status\":\"In Progress\",\"statusType\":\"started\",\"labels\":[\"web\",\"analytics\"],\"attachments\":[],\"documents\":[],\"stateHistory\":[{\"state\":{\"id\":\"64be05ca-3288-4616-9b5b-4d0c8d805b56\",\"name\":\"Backlog\",\"type\":\"backlog\"},\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-04T00:14:08.681Z\",\"endedAt\":\"2026-10-07T10:10:06.422Z\"},{\"state\":{\"id\":\"b878aab7-e95e-4f74-aac1-e8693ffd9fd1\",\"name\":\"In Progress\",\"type\":\"started\"},\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-07T10:10:06.422Z\",\"endedAt\":null}],\"createdBy\":\"Cooper Corbett\",\"createdById\":\"d8b7eeef-6a21-42af-8081-66dca85ec9df\",\"project\":\"Taxkit\",\"projectId\":\"4e0eb6ef-1871-46d4-8f47-9c8f52a9c069\",\"team\":\"Development\",\"teamId\":\"ed6b68f2-2ec2-4db2-983f-bdc5951dc79a\",\"relations\":{\"blocks\":[{\"id\":\"DEV-81\",\"title\":\"CSF-T010 — Finish rebuild checks, package versioning and controlled delivery\"}],\"blockedBy\":[{\"id\":\"DEV-75\",\"title\":\"CSF-T004 — Build all calculator pages and the fresh package interface\"},{\"id\":\"DEV-77\",\"title\":\"CSF-T006 — Add remote MCP and visible browser calculator tools\"},{\"id\":\"DEV-76\",\"title\":\"CSF-T005 — Rebuild docs, search discovery, public Markdown and share images\"}],\"relatedTo\":[],\"duplicateOf\":null}}"}],"isError":false,"_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"Linear MCP","title":"Linear","version":"1.0.0","websiteUrl":"https://linear.app","icons":[{"src":"https://static.linear.app/integrations/mcp/icon.svg","mimeType":"image/svg+xml"}]}}},"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":598700875}},"started_at_ms":1791370460888,"completed_at_ms":1791370461487}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T10:54:21.676Z","ordinal":68782,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-4981dec8-f409-46b3-8c96-4188a67e87d1","process_id":"50803","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '101,125p' .agents/skills/package-structure/SKILL.md; rg -n '^##|PostHog|Analytics' docs/architecture/frontend.md apps/web/README.md; cat packages/analytics/tsconfig.json; cat packages/analytics/tsconfig.build.json; cat packages/analytics/vitest.config.ts"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '101,125p' .agents/skills/package-structure/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":".agents/skills/package-structure/SKILL.md"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n '^##|PostHog|Analytics' docs/architecture/frontend.md apps/web/README.md","query":"^##|PostHog|Analytics","path":"frontend.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat packages/analytics/tsconfig.json","name":"tsconfig.json","path":"packages/analytics/tsconfig.json"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat packages/analytics/tsconfig.build.json","name":"tsconfig.build.json","path":"packages/analytics/tsconfig.build.json"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat packages/analytics/vitest.config.ts","name":"vitest.config.ts","path":"packages/analytics/vitest.config.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"## Validate and hand off\n\nRun the repository's real format, lint, typecheck, focused tests, integration\ntests, build, packed-artifact, and downstream commands that apply. Also run:\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/validate_package.py /absolute/package\npython3 scripts/validate_ecosystem.py /absolute/skill-or-repository-root\n```\n\nFor publishable packages, inspect the tarball produced by the repository's\nactual publisher; `publishConfig.exports` alone is not proof that npm or Bun\nremoved the development source condition.\n\nFor new or changed skill folders, run the global skill validator separately.\nRun the local docs-maintainer checks and attach the applicable impact rows and\nnon-claims. Report the selected variant, ownership decision, exports,\ndocumentation/proof impact, tests, commands, and any repository-specific exception. Render receipts\nretain official sources, qualified compatibility decisions, config digests,\nlimitations, and non-claims. Read [maintenance](references/maintenance.md)\nwhen updating templates, validators, or Effect APIs.\n\n## Strict data ownership in every package\n\nUse one Schema owner for each identity, constrained value and data record; infer\napps/web/README.md:18:## What runs where\napps/web/README.md:61:## Settings and generated owners\napps/web/README.md:75:## Checks\napps/web/README.md:142:## Related owners\napps/web/README.md:215:## Calculator routes\napps/web/README.md:297:## Native calculation rate admission\napps/web/README.md:309:## Documentation pages\napps/web/README.md:350:## Documentation search\napps/web/README.md:387:## Documentation discovery\napps/web/README.md:415:## Documentation Markdown\napps/web/README.md:444:## Public documentation share images\napps/web/README.md:478:## Release documentation check\napps/web/README.md:503:## Visible calculator browser tools\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:17:## Scope\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:22:## Main areas\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:40:## Runtime shape\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:109:## Decoding and composition boundaries\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:137:## Visible composition and leaf ownership\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:183:## Guardrails\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:215:## Related Docs\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:307:## Page-owned browser tools\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:339:## Native calculation rate admission\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:350:## Replacement Website documentation composition\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:399:### Replacement Website search\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:423:### Replacement Website discovery files\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:444:### Replacement Website Markdown\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:467:### Replacement Website share metadata\n{\n  \"extends\": \"../../tsconfig.base.json\",\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"lib\": [\"ES2024\", \"DOM\", \"DOM.Iterable\"]\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"src/**/*.ts\", \"test/**/*.ts\", \"vitest.config.ts\"]\n}\n{\n  \"extends\": \"./tsconfig.json\",\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"rootDir\": \"src\",\n    \"outDir\": \"dist\"\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"src/**/*.ts\"],\n  \"exclude\": [\"test\", \"vitest.config.ts\"]\n}\nimport { defaultServerConditions } from \"vite\";\nimport { defineConfig } from \"vitest/config\";\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  resolve: { conditions: [\"source\", ...defaultServerConditions] },\n  test: { fileParallelism: false, include: [\"test/**/*.test.ts\"] },\n});\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"## Validate and hand off\n\nRun the repository's real format, lint, typecheck, focused tests, integration\ntests, build, packed-artifact, and downstream commands that apply. Also run:\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/validate_package.py /absolute/package\npython3 scripts/validate_ecosystem.py /absolute/skill-or-repository-root\n```\n\nFor publishable packages, inspect the tarball produced by the repository's\nactual publisher; `publishConfig.exports` alone is not proof that npm or Bun\nremoved the development source condition.\n\nFor new or changed skill folders, run the global skill validator separately.\nRun the local docs-maintainer checks and attach the applicable impact rows and\nnon-claims. Report the selected variant, ownership decision, exports,\ndocumentation/proof impact, tests, commands, and any repository-specific exception. Render receipts\nretain official sources, qualified compatibility decisions, config digests,\nlimitations, and non-claims. Read [maintenance](references/maintenance.md)\nwhen updating templates, validators, or Effec