ondition must be a custom name such as `@scope/source`, not an\nempty, malformed or standard condition such as `types`, `default` or `node`.\nEvery compiled export keeps that recorded condition first and points it at an\nexisting source file. Repository and package receipts must agree on the name.\n\nThe version snapshot must contain an ISO date and an exact `effect` version.\nTemplates target DAW's qualified Effect `4.0.0-rc.117` API, including\n`Schema.TaggedError`. The renderer accepts current v4 RC/stable snapshots and\nhas no legacy API switch. A different selected release needs qualification of\nthe canonical templates before adoption.\nNetwork resolution belongs to repository snapshot maintenance, never rendering.\nThe render manifest records the snapshot date and content digest, never the\nabsolute installation or source path.\n\nUse an isolated temporary directory for smoke tests. Do not point the renderer\nat a dirty live package; audit and patch that package deliberately instead.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7375},"formatted_output":"docs/architecture/package-ownership.md:28:- `packages/analytics`\ndocs/architecture/package-ownership.md:136:  the three calculator pages and bounded T003 connection are locally qualified.\ndocs/architecture/package-ownership.md:141:  qualified. Current release documentation checking selects this app.\ndocs/architecture/package-ownership.md:189:`packages/analytics`\ndocs/architecture/package-ownership.md:195:  projects. Calculators, rules and the local SDK have no analytics dependency.\ndocs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md:12:The active T008 candidate adds minimal analytics only in the native API app.\ndocs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md:16:analytics. The [API README](../../apps/api/README.md#analytics-candidate) owns\ndocs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md:350:adapter. Full native trace/export proof remains pending. The native Worker\ndocs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md:406:lazy ManagedRuntime per client, and `dispose(): Pr