    // through the normal failure callback for both synchronous and async compression.\\n623:        options.compression === types_1.Compression.GZipJS &&\\n634:                safeTransportMethod(__assign(__assign({}, options), { compression: undefined, url: buildRequestURL(_options.url, _options.method, undefined, _options.timestampMode) }));\\n640:            // If async compression fails for another reason, fall back to the synchronous fflate path\\nbans while allowing only the non-throwing callback decoder. Test a misplaced\\nPromise bridge under the consumer path too.\\n\\n## Respect the selected privacy controls\\n\\nHonour Do Not Track when it is part of the agreed policy, both at startup and\\nbefore each capture. Consent controls are separate. Do not add or remove them\\nbecause this reference's source application made a different choice, and do not\\nstate a legal exemption based on geography.\\n\\nIf collection needs consent withdrawal, discard pending SDK batches before\\nclosing the instance. In the qualified SDK, opt-out/reset did not empty send\\nqueues and shutdown could flush a waiting batch. Test Allow followed immediately\\nby withdrawal within the batch delay. Do not present opt-out followed by shutdown\\nas proof that waiting events are gone. If the supported SDK cannot meet the\\nrequired policy, surface that mismatch rather than bypassing its queue contract.\\n\\nFor a consent-free migration, change only the application's owned old-choice\\nkeys under the user's instruction. Test both saved choices and no saved choice;\\ndo not clear unrelated browser storage. The qualified SDK needed an explicit\\nqueue-resume operation without an opt-in event. Inspect the target version before\\nreusing that workaround; ordinary SDK initialisation may behave differently.\\n\\n## Check the real client\\n\\nTest through deterministic Layers: disabled state, malformed configuration,\\nwrong origin, Do Not Track, allowed events/properties, acknowledgement failure,\\nduplicate suppression, timeout, interruption and scoped cleanup. Include late\\nimport/acknowledgement, partial init failure, concurrent capture/close and repeated\\nLayer mount/unmount. Prove one acquisition and one release per mounted lifetime,\\nno capture after close, and bounded safe diagnostics. Do not replace\\nthe imported SDK with a fake and then claim the real SDK works.\\n\\nIn a deliberate enabled Preview, observe a fresh browser: SDK chunk loads,\\nselected Home/About events, real batching, request status and stored exact UUIDs.\\nCheck Do Not Track beyond the batching window, restore any temporary override,\\nand test required migrations with both old saved choices. Keep startup coverage\\nseparate if the browser tool cannot set the value before SDK initialisation.\\nClosing a tab can lose waiting events; a shutdown call is not durable delivery.\\n\\nRead [PostHog browser configuration](https://posthog.com/docs/libraries/js/config),\\n[collection controls](https://posthog.com/docs/privacy/data-collection) and the\\n[SDK source](https://github.com/PostHog/posthog-js), then reconcile those sources\\n   Start at  22:19:08\\n   Duration  604ms (tests 67%, import 26%, transform 6%, worker 1%)\\n\\n$ turbo run //#test:quality-workflow:task\\n\\n   • turbo 2.11.7\\n   • Packages in scope: //\\n   • Running //#test:quality-workflow:task in 1 package\\n   • Remote caching disabled, using shared worktree cache\\n\\n//:test:quality-workflow:task: cache miss, executing a21d1d9667587d76\\n//:test:quality-workflow:task: $ bun --bun vitest run --config tools/vitest.config.ts tools/quality-workflow\\n//:test:quality-workflow:task: \\n//:test:quality-workflow:task:  RUN  v5.0.3 /Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit\\n//:test:quality-workflow:task: \\n{\\n  \\\"document_type\\\": \\\"bounded-proof-receipt\\\",\\n  \\\"lifecycle\\\": \\\"evidence\\\",\\n  \\\"authority\\\": \\\"supporting\\\",\\n  \\\"owner\\\": \\\"taxkit-analytics-owner\\\",\\n  \\\"last_reviewed\\\": \\\"2026-10-07\\\",\\n  \\\"review_trigger\\\": \\\"T008 source, native host, privacy, provider or qualification change\\\",\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"T008 backend and request policy candidate; whole-source verification pending; T008 remains in progress\\\",\\n  \\\"observedAt\\\": \\\"2026-10-07T11:14:45.383610+00:00\\\",\\n  \\\"baseHead\\\": \\\"d9cadb664291b327cf3e3cb624d40c511d78a384\\\",\\n  \\\"executionAuthority\\\": {\\n    \\\"principal\\\": \\\"Cooper\\\",\\n    \\\"operation\\\": \\\"Approved repository implementation, local checks, commits/pushes/draft PR and routine Linear tracking\\\",\\n    \\\"resource\\\": \\\"crcorbett/taxkit; CSF-T008 / DEV-79\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Local Mac; disposable native workerd and controlled upstream only\\\",\\n    \\\"boundary\\\": \\\"No PostHog provider, credential, deployment, merge or publication mutation in this candidate\\\",\\n    \\\"rollback\\\": \\\"Revert this candidate; collection defaults to off and requires no capture settings\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"outcomes\\\": [\\n    \\\"Private compiled analytics package with catalogue-owned calculator identity, checked event/settings/policy Schemas, safe errors and separate named live/test services\\\",\\n    \\\"Backend capture sends only calculator catalogue ID/name plus required operational and event identity, never inputs, answers, visitor identity, URLs or request headers\\\",\\n    \\\"Off needs no token; invalid enabled settings have a separate checked configuration failure\\\",\\n    \\\"One API decorator records a successful hosted calculation; request-local deny, malformed policy or DNT refuses collection without changing calculation admission\\\",\\n    \\\"Application captures delivery during initialisation and provides it to returned requests; native Worker/session waitUntil owns a one-attempt send, own HTTP scope and complete five-second deadline; the collector is capped at 64 successes\\\",\\n    \\\"Actual native HTTP/RPC and both official client protocols use the same successful-use owner; denied requests and metadata do not add another event\\\",\\n    \\\"Pure tax packages and local SDK calculations have no analytics dependency\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"qualification\\\": {\\n    \\\"focusedPackageTests\\\": 31,\\n    \\\"focusedApiTests\\\": 112,\\n    \\\"actualPathLintCases\\\": 16,\\n    \\\"nativeAnalyticsCases\\\": 3,\\n    \\\"wholeSource\\\": \\\"pending\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"referenceVersions\\\": {\\n    \\\"installedEffect\\\": \\\"4.0.0\\\",\\n    \\\"installedAlchemy\\\": \\\"2.0.0-beta.80\\\",\\n    \\\"officialRegistryPostHogBrowserCandidate\\\": \\\"1.438.2\\\",\\n    \\\"officialRegistryDistilledPostHogCandidate\\\": \\\"1.0.0-rc.13\\\",\\n    \\\"browserAndManagementSdkInstalled\\\": false,\\n    \\\"nativeMcpClient\\\": \\\"2.3.1\\\",\\n    \\\"nativeProtocols\\\": [\\n      \\\"2026-07-28\\\",\\n      \\\"2025-11-25\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"CommonplaceGuidance\\\": \\\"development-workflows 0.6.9; repository canonical skill baseline 0.6.1 unchanged\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"packageValidation\\\": {\\n    \\\"renderer\\\": \\\"Repository canonical package-structure renderer, effect-service variant\\\",\\n    \\\"adaptation\\\": \\\"Private compiled package using TaxKit stable dependency graph, root tsconfig and source export condition; original scaffold/config identities retained in package-structure.render.json\\\",\\n    \\\"structuralScope\\\": \\\"Byte-matched copy of all 16 owned package files, excluding installed node_modules, dist, caches and tsbuildinfo\\\",\\n    \\\"result\\\": \\\"validate_package.py and validate_ecosystem.py pass; focused types/build/tests qualify the adapted package only\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"docImpact\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"decision\\\": \\\"Change required\\\",\\n      \\\"paths\\\": [\\n        \\\"packages/analytics/README.md\\\",\\n        \\\"packages/analytics/package-structure.render.json\\\",\\n        \\\"apps/api/README.md\\\",\\n        \\\"apps/we