{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T11:29:14.500Z","ordinal":69393,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-0e36c8bf-2d73-42bb-9d13-bfb4e94bc021","process_id":"48358","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","tail -n 25 /private/tmp/dev79-backend-whole-a-verification.log; cat .agents/skills/effect-client-wrapper/SKILL.md; cat apps/web/src/lib/calculator.atoms.ts; cat packages/analytics/src/config.ts"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"tail -n 25 /private/tmp/dev79-backend-whole-a-verification.log","name":"dev79-backend-whole-a-verification.log","path":"/private/tmp/dev79-backend-whole-a-verification.log"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat .agents/skills/effect-client-wrapper/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":".agents/skills/effect-client-wrapper/SKILL.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat apps/web/src/lib/calculator.atoms.ts","name":"calculator.atoms.ts","path":"apps/web/src/lib/calculator.atoms.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat packages/analytics/src/config.ts","name":"config.ts","path":"packages/analytics/src/config.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"web build:native-pair: [22:28:09.088] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] (!) Your Vite config uses features that are unsupported by `configLoader: 'native'`, which is planned to become the default in a future major version of Vite:\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.088] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:8:8). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.088] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"./docs-images.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:9:39). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.088] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.schemas.ts:3:38). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.088] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] Set `VITE_CONFIG_NATIVE_IGNORE_WARNING=true` to suppress this warning.\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.755] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] (!) Your Vite config uses features that are unsupported by `configLoader: 'native'`, which is planned to become the default in a future major version of Vite:\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.756] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:8:8). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.756] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"./docs-images.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:9:39). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.756] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.schemas.ts:3:38). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.756] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] Set `VITE_CONFIG_NATIVE_IGNORE_WARNING=true` to suppress this warning.\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.272] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] (!) Your Vite config uses features that are unsupported by `configLoader: 'native'`, which is planned to become the default in a future major version of Vite:\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.272] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:8:8). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.272] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"./docs-images.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:9:39). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.272] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.schemas.ts:3:38). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.272] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] Set `VITE_CONFIG_NATIVE_IGNORE_WARNING=true` to suppress this warning.\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.766] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] vite v8.3.2 building client environment for production...\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.772] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] [MDX] generated files in 0.8558750000001965ms\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:13.046] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] ✓ built in 2.28s\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:13.046] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] vite v8.3.2 building ssr environment for production...\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:13.050] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] [MDX] generated files in 0.315415999999459ms\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:13.717] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] ✓ built in 671ms\nweb build:native-pair: Exited with code 0\nweb test:native-pair: \nweb test:native-pair:  RUN  v5.0.3 /Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit/apps/web\nweb test:native-pair: \n---\nname: effect-client-wrapper\ndescription: Design, implement, or review a typed Effect service around a third-party SDK, API client, callback library, or Promise-based provider. Use for provider adapters, service Layers, external-client configuration, request and response Schemas, typed provider errors, retries, and test Layers. Enforce named operations, branded identifiers, Schema-backed Config, immediate output decoding, flat Effects, and the explicit rejection of generic use callbacks, raw clients, primitive config, instanceof, and unchecked SDK outputs.\n---\n\n# Effect Client Wrapper\n\nCreate a semantic adapter owned by the application, not a generic Effect-shaped escape hatch around an SDK.\n\n## Establish the boundary\n\n1. Read applicable repository instructions, architecture docs, lint rules, installed Effect and SDK versions, and representative services and Layers.\n2. Identify the owner of every request, response, identifier, configuration value, error, retry policy, and runtime boundary.\n3. Research the cloned Effect v4 source, record its revision/version, then reconcile the chosen APIs with installed source/types. Use matching primary SDK source for its contract; DeepWiki through Executor MCP is secondary explanation for the upstream Effect/SDK repository.\n4. Prefer extending an existing semantic adapter over creating a parallel client abstraction.\n\n## Define the public service\n\n- Expose named domain/provider operations such as `getCustomer`, `sendMessage`, or `renderImage`.\n- Accept owning Schema-derived inputs and branded identifiers. Never substitute raw `id: string`.\n- Return only decoded application-owned or explicitly provider-owned Schema types.\n- Keep the raw SDK instance private to the live Layer or adapter module.\n- Provide a live Layer and a mock/test Layer at the same service contract.\n\nDo not expose a generic `use`, `run`, `withClient`, callback, unconstrained generic result, or raw-client accessor. Those APIs erase operation ownership, output provenance, retry policy, and testability.\n\n## Implement each operation linearly\n\nUse the locally installed Effect APIs. A named operation should read as one flat program:\n\n1. encode the checked request at its actual outbound contract, without re-decoding internal typed data;\n2. call exactly one SDK operation through `Effect.tryPromise`, callback adaptation, or the repository's boundary primitive;\n3. map rejection immediately into an owner-named typed Schema error with safe diagnostics;\n4. decode the unknown SDK result immediately with the owning output Schema;\n5. apply operation-specific retry, a complete-operation deadline, tracing, metrics, and redaction policy;\n6. return the decoded value without another wrapper layer.\n\nUse `Effect.gen`, meaningful `Effect.fn`, or local equivalents for readable sequential work. Keep one-use request mapping, rejection mapping, and decoding beside the operation. Extract only demonstrated reuse, stable domain policy, or a real I/O boundary.\n\nFor native Effect HTTP/RPC clients, reuse the domain service contract instead\nof exposing the generated client or inventing a second public service. Keep\nSchema-selected response checks and named transport/decode failures with their\nsemantic owner. Promise adaptation is unnecessary when the client already\nreturns Effect.\n\nA deadline includes headers and decoded body. Test both stalled phases, one\ntotal budget after late headers, underlying cleanup and earlier interruption.\nDo not reset the clock at each phase or add an automatic retry by default.\n\n## Configure safely\n\n- Model semantic configuration with Schema and `Config`/`ConfigProvider`, using the repository's supported API.\n- Give configuration an owner-named structure rather than passing independent primitive strings and numbers through the codebase.\n- Keep secrets redacted and unwrap them only for immediate SDK construction.\n- Construct the SDK once in the live Layer unless its documented lifecycle requires scoped acquisition and release.\n- Override configuration in tests through a test `ConfigProvider` or the repository's established Layer mechanism.\n\n## Model failures explicitly\n\n- Use owner-named Schema-tagged errors for expected configuration, transport, rate-limit, authentication, provider, and decode failures when those distinctions affect callers.\n- Preserve safe provider codes, operation names, retryability, and diagnostic context; do not place unchecked `unknown` payloads in public tagged errors.\n- Use tagged catches or pattern matching. Never use `instanceof` for provider-error policy.\n- Treat truly unexpected failures as defects only when callers cannot reasonably recover.\n\n## Adapt browser hosts and callbacks\n\nKeep the original host object when a method depends on `this`; do not detach\nthe method or decode it into a copied data object. Validate the required\ncapability with the owning Schema. Detect absence inside Effect and distinguish\nit from a supported host refusing an operation. Keep safe refusal details.\n\nScope callback execution and registration together. Release unregisters or\naborts registration and interrupts unfinished callbacks. Accommodate synchronous\nand Promise return forms only where a supported host requires them. Confine the\nbridge and justified lint exceptions to the named adapter. For a browser tool\ninterface, follow the sibling\n[MCP/WebMCP pattern](../strict-effect-ts/references/applications/mcp-and-webmcp.md).\n\nFor a PostHog browser SDK in a React-owned Effect Atom runtime, read the\n[PostHog browser adapter guide](references/posthog-browser.md). It covers scoped\nSDK ownership, explicit event operations, the synchronous capture callback,\nprivacy controls and real-client delivery proof. Native Distilled management\nand backend Effect HTTP capture do not need Promise bridges.\n\n## Test and enforce\n\nTest service operations through mock/test Layers and test the live adapter boundary narrowly. Cover success, request encoding, provider rejection mapping, output decode failure, redaction, timeout/retry policy, and non-idempotent retry exclusion.\n\nUpdate affected architecture docs, READMEs, lint/custom rules and fixtures, CI commands, SPEC/tasks, and repository-owned skills. Add the narrowest reliable static or stale-pattern check the repository supports.\n\nAcceptance requires zero examples or public APIs containing:\n\n- a generic SDK `use` callback or raw-client accessor;\n- a raw `id: string` where an owning branded ID exists;\n- primitive/manual semantic configuration in place of Schema-backed `Config`;\n- `instanceof` provider-error branching;\n- an SDK result escaping without immediate Schema decoding;\n- a one-use wrapper/helper that merely forwards, maps, reads one property, or hides the SDK call.\n\nRun the repository's actual format, lint, typecheck, test, build, boundary, skill-validation, and stale-pattern checks appropriate to the change. Do not invent commands or claim the wrapper is safe when any prohibited pattern remains.\n\n## Keep checked values checked\n\nThe live adapter owns actual untrusted replies. Decode there once and return the\nowning inferred type. A caller does not re-decode a typed service reply; a test\nLayer follows that same contract. Reuse the domain's branded fields and shared\nwhole-record checks in a provider codec, including checks lost when fields are\nspread. Keep expected identity, completeness and range checks as domain policy.\n\nNew branded values use the installed fallible constructor; map its issue to the\noperation's named error. Plain mappings from checked values stay immutable with\nEffect Array/Record functions. Optional provider/source fields decode to Option;\nhistorical missing/null distinctions belong in the source codec. Internal caches\nuse checked readonly keys directly, with equality, full-address and cancellation\ntests. Neither SDK typings nor another internal decoder replaces boundary proof.\nimport type { CalculatorRpcClientError } from \"@taxkit/api-rpc/errors\";\nimport { TaxKitRpcClientLive } from \"@taxkit/api-rpc/live\";\nimport type {\n  CalculatorCatalogResponse,\n  CalculatorRunResponse,\n  CalculatorRunServiceRequest,\n} from \"@taxkit/api-rpc/schemas\";\nimport { TaxKitRpcClient } from \"@taxkit/api-rpc/service\";\nimport { AnnualTaxReport } from \"@taxkit/rules-au-income-tax/schemas\";\nimport {\n  AuPayCalculatorId,\n  PayWithholdingsLedger,\n  TakeHomePayReport,\n} from \"@taxkit/rules-au-pay/schemas\";\nimport { Cause, Effect, Layer, Match, Option, Result, Schema } from \"effect\";\nimport { FetchHttpClient } from \"effect/http\";\nimport * as AsyncResult from \"effect/reactivity/AsyncResult\";\nimport * as Atom from \"effect/reactivity/Atom\";\n\nimport { calculationFailureMessage } from \"./calculation-failure\";\nimport { TaxKitWebConfigError } from \"./config\";\nimport {\n  takeHomeRequestFromForm,\n  annualTaxRequestFromForm,\n  initialTakeHomeForm,\n  AnnualTaxForm,\n  WebsiteInputError,\n  TakeHomeForm,\n} from \"./form.boundary\";\nimport type { WebsiteCalculatorForm } from \"./form.boundary\";\nimport type {\n  WebsiteCalculatorViewState,\n  WebsitePublicSettings,\n} from \"./schemas\";\n\n// These are descriptions of work. React's registry owns client acquisition,\n// execution and release; no module creates or runs a browser ManagedRuntime.\n// The loader seeds these settings for the React registry's whole lifetime.\n// They must survive an idle form before its first calculation.\nexport const publicSettingsAtom = Atom.make(\n  Option.none<WebsitePublicSettings>()\n).pipe(Atom.keepAlive);\nexport const websiteCatalogueAtom = Atom.make(\n  Option.none<CalculatorCatalogResponse>()\n).pipe(Atom.keepAlive);\nexport const calculatorRuntime = Atom.runtime((get) =>\n  Option.match(get(publicSettingsAtom), {\n    onNone: () =>\n      Layer.effect(\n        TaxKitRpcClient,\n        Effect.fail(\n          new TaxKitWebConfigError({\n            message: \"TaxKit web settings are missing or invalid.\",\n            operation: \"settings\",\n            runtime: \"client\",\n          })\n        )\n      ),\n    onSome: (settings) =>\n      TaxKitRpcClientLive(settings.apiOrigin).pipe(\n        Layer.provide(FetchHttpClient.layer)\n      ),\n  })\n);\n// The registry owns separate temporary state for each checked calculator ID.\n// The family memoises descriptions, never a client or a computed answer.\nexport const calculatorPageAtoms = Atom.family(\n  (calculatorId: CalculatorRunServiceRequest[\"calculatorId\"]) => {\n    const form = Atom.make<WebsiteCalculatorForm>(\n      Match.value(calculatorId).pipe(\n        Match.when(\"au.income-tax.annual\", () =>\n          AnnualTaxForm.make({ taxableDollars: \"67000\" })\n        ),\n        Match.when(\"au.pay.take-home\", () => initialTakeHomeForm),\n        Match.orElse(() => ({\n          grossDollars: \"9500\",\n          period: \"monthly\",\n          taxFreeThresholdClaimed: false,\n        }))\n      )\n    );\n    const calculation = calculatorRuntime.fn<CalculatorRunServiceRequest>()(\n      (request) =>\n        TaxKitRpcClient.pipe(\n          Effect.flatMap((client) => client.calculate(request))\n        )\n    );\n    const showSaved = Atom.make(true);\n    const showCalculation = Atom.make(false);\n    const formError = Atom.make(Option.none<string>());\n    const savedReport = Atom.make(\n      Option.none<CalculatorRunResponse[\"report\"]>()\n    );\n    const savedMessage = Atom.make(Option.none<string>());\n    // Checked request identity belongs to one visible attempt. An edit or a\n    // newer manual/tool submission invalidates a waiter for the older attempt.\n    const attempt = Atom.make(Option.none<CalculatorRunServiceRequest>());\n    const cancel = Atom.fnSync<\"cancel\">()((_, get) => {\n      get.set(attempt, Option.none());\n      get.set(calculation, Atom.Interrupt);\n      get.set(showCalculation, false);\n    });\n    const edit = Atom.fnSync<WebsiteCalculatorForm>()((value, get) => {\n      get.set(attempt, Option.none());\n      get.set(calculation, Atom.Interrupt);\n      get.set(showCalculation, false);\n      get.set(showSaved, false);\n      get.set(formError, Option.none());\n      get.set(form, value);\n    });\n    const submit = Atom.fnSync<\"calculate\">()((_, get) => {\n      const current = get(form);\n      const request = Result.gen(function* () {\n        if (calculatorId === \"au.income-tax.annual\") {\n          return yield* \"taxableDollars\" in current\n            ? annualTaxRequestFromForm(current)\n            : Result.fail(\n                new WebsiteInputError({\n                  message: \"Enter a valid annual taxable income.\",\n                })\n              );\n        }\n        return yield* \"grossDollars\" in current\n          ? takeHomeRequestFromForm(\n              current,\n              AuPayCalculatorId.make(calculatorId)\n            )\n          : Result.fail(\n              new WebsiteInputError({\n                message: \"Enter a valid pay amount and pay period.\",\n              })\n            );\n      });\n      get.set(showCalculation, true);\n      get.set(showSaved, false);\n      if (Result.isFailure(request)) {\n        get.set(attempt, Option.none());\n        get.set(calculation, Atom.Interrupt);\n        get.set(formError, Option.some(request.failure.message));\n        return;\n      }\n      get.set(formError, Option.none());\n      get.set(attempt, Option.some(request.success));\n      get.set(calculation, request.success);\n    });\n    const group = {\n      attempt,\n      calculation,\n      cancel,\n      edit,\n      form,\n      formError,\n      savedMessage,\n      savedReport,\n      showCalculation,\n      showSaved,\n      submit,\n      // The registry retains this in-memory page snapshot across an uncommitted\n      // React render. Otherwise idle cleanup can erase once-seeded SSR values\n      // before hydration subscribes. Page cleanup still interrupts live work.\n      // The retained view also holds its whole weak-family description group.\n      // Otherwise browser GC can replace that group on a return visit while the\n      // old values remain in the registry. The callback runs after group creation.\n      // Disposing the root registry releases the snapshot and its client.\n      view: Atom.make((get): WebsiteCalculatorViewState => {\n        const current = get(calculation);\n        const submitted = get(showCalculation);\n        const saved = get(showSaved);\n        const inputError = get(formError);\n        const report = AsyncResult.value(current).pipe(\n          Option.filter(\n            (value) => value.calculator.calculatorId === calculatorId\n          ),\n          Option.map((value) => value.report),\n          Option.orElse(() => get(savedReport)),\n          Option.filter((value) =>\n            Match.value(calculatorId).pipe(\n              Match.when(\"au.income-tax.annual\", () =>\n                Schema.is(AnnualTaxReport)(value)\n              ),\n              Match.when(\"au.pay.take-home\", () =>\n                Schema.is(TakeHomePayReport)(value)\n              ),\n              Match.orElse(() => Schema.is(PayWithholdingsLedger)(value))\n            )\n          )\n        );\n        const message = Option.match(inputError, {\n          onNone: () => {\n            if (\n              submitted &&\n              !current.waiting &&\n              (AsyncResult.isFailure(current) ||\n                (AsyncResult.isSuccess(current) && Option.isNone(report)))\n            ) {\n              if (AsyncResult.isFailure(current)) {\n                return current.cause.pipe(\n                  Cause.findErrorOption,\n                  Option.map(calculationFailureMessage)\n                );\n              }\n              return Option.some(\n                \"The calculation could not finish. Please try again.\"\n              );\n            }\n            return saved ? get(savedMessage) : Option.none<string>();\n          },\n          onSome: Option.some,\n        });\n        return {\n          busy: submitted && current.waiting,\n          calculatorId,\n          form: get(group.form),\n          message,\n          report,\n          stale:\n            Option.isSome(report) &&\n            !saved &&\n            (!submitted ||\n              current.waiting ||\n              !AsyncResult.isSuccess(current) ||\n              Option.isSome(inputError)),\n        };\n      }).pipe(Atom.keepAlive),\n    } as const;\n    return group;\n  }\n);\n\n// Home uses the same page commands and state owner as the other calculators.\n// These existing names retain their narrow React/test call sites.\nconst home = calculatorPageAtoms(AuPayCalculatorId.make(\"au.pay.take-home\"));\nexport const calculateAtom: Atom.AtomResultFn<\n  CalculatorRunServiceRequest,\n  CalculatorRunResponse,\n  CalculatorRpcClientError | TaxKitWebConfigError\n> = home.calculation;\nexport const takeHomeFormAtom = Atom.writable(\n  (get) => {\n    const form = get(home.form);\n    return Schema.is(TakeHomeForm)(form) ? form : initialTakeHomeForm;\n  },\n  (get, form: TakeHomeForm) => get.set(home.form, form)\n);\nexport const submitTakeHomeAtom = home.submit;\nexport const editTakeHomeAtom = Atom.fnSync<TakeHomeForm>()((value, get) =>\n  get.set(home.edit, value)\n);\nimport { Config, Effect, Match, Schema } from \"effect\";\n\nimport { AnalyticsConfigurationError } from \"./errors.js\";\nimport type { AnalyticsSettings } from \"./schemas.js\";\nimport { AnalyticsDisabled, AnalyticsEnabled } from \"./schemas.js\";\n\n// Off is a deliberate mode. Missing or malformed enabled settings have a\n// separate failure; no token is acquired by the disabled branch.\nexport const AnalyticsSettingsConfig: Effect.Effect<\n  AnalyticsSettings,\n  AnalyticsConfigurationError\n> = Config.schema(\n  Schema.Literals([\"off\", \"production\", \"controlled-preview\"]),\n  \"POSTHOG_COLLECTION_MODE\"\n).pipe(\n  Config.withDefault(\"off\"),\n  Effect.flatMap((mode) =>\n    Match.value(mode).pipe(\n      Match.when(\"off\", () => Effect.succeed(AnalyticsDisabled.make({}))),\n      Match.orElse((environment) =>\n        Effect.all({\n          projectId: Config.schema(\n            AnalyticsEnabled.fields.projectId,\n            \"POSTHOG_PROJECT_ID\"\n          ),\n          region: Config.schema(\n            AnalyticsEnabled.fields.region,\n            \"POSTHOG_REGION\"\n          ),\n          stage: Config.schema(AnalyticsEnabled.fields.stage, \"POSTHOG_STAGE\"),\n          token: Config.schema(\n            AnalyticsEnabled.fields.token,\n            \"POSTHOG_CAPTURE_TOKEN\"\n          ),\n        }).pipe(\n          Effect.flatMap((settings) =>\n            AnalyticsEnabled.makeEffect({\n              environment,\n              ...settings,\n            })\n          )\n        )\n      )\n    )\n  ),\n  Effect.mapError(\n    () => new AnalyticsConfigurationError({ operation: \"configure\" })\n  )\n);\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"web build:native-pair: [22:28:09.088] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] (!) Your Vite config uses features that are unsupported by `configLoader: 'native'`, which is planned to become the default in a future major version of Vite:\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.088] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:8:8). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.088] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"./docs-images.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:9:39). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.088] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.schemas.ts:3:38). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.088] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] Set `VITE_CONFIG_NATIVE_IGNORE_WARNING=true` to suppress this warning.\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.755] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] (!) Your Vite config uses features that are unsupported by `configLoader: 'native'`, which is planned to become the default in a future major version of Vite:\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.756] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:8:8). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.756] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"./docs-images.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:9:39). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.756] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.schemas.ts:3:38). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.756] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] Set `VITE_CONFIG_NATIVE_IGNORE_WARNING=true` to suppress this warning.\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.272] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] (!) Your Vite config uses features that are unsupported by `configLoader: 'native'`, which is planned to become the default in a future major version of Vite:\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.272] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:8:8). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.272] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"./docs-images.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:9:39). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.272] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.schemas.ts:3:38). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.272] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] Set `VITE_CONFIG_NATIVE_IGNORE_WARNING=true` to suppress this warning.\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.766] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] vite v8.3.2 building client environment for production...\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.772] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] [MDX] generated files in 0.8558750000001965ms\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:13.046] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] ✓ built in 2.28s\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:13.046] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] vite v8.3.2 building ssr environment for production...\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:13.050] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] [MDX] generated files in 0.315415999999459ms\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:13.717] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] ✓ built in 671ms\nweb build:native-pair: Exited with code 0\nweb test:native-pair: \nweb test:native-pair:  RUN  v5.0.3 /Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit/apps/web\nweb test:native-pair: \n---\nname: effect-client-wrapper\ndescription: Design, implement, or review a typed Effect service around a third-party SDK, API client, callback library, or Promise-based provider. Use for provider adapters, service Layers, external-client configuration, request and response Schemas, typed provider errors, retries, and test Layers. Enforce named operations, branded identifiers, Schema-backed Config, immediate output decoding, flat Effects, and the explicit rejection of generic use callbacks, raw clients, primitive config, instanceof, and unchecked SDK outputs.\n---\n\n# Effect Client Wrapper\n\nCreate a semantic adapter owned by the application, not a generic Effect-shaped escape hatch around an SDK.\n\n## Establish the boundary\n\n1. Read applicable repository instructions, architecture docs, lint rules, installed Effect and SDK versions, and representative services and Layers.\n2. Identify the owner of every request, response, identifier, configuration value, error, retry policy, and runtime boundary.\n3. Research the cloned Effect v4 source, record its revision/version, then reconcile the chosen APIs with installed source/types. Use matching primary SDK source for its contract; DeepWiki through Executor MCP is secondary explanation for the upstream Effect/SDK repository.\n4. Prefer extending an existing semantic adapter over creating a parallel client abstraction.\n\n## Define the public service\n\n- Expose named domain/provider operations such as `getCustomer`, `sendMessage`, or `renderImage`.\n- Accept owning Schema-derived inputs and branded identifiers. Never substitute raw `id: string`.\n- Return only decoded application-owned or explicitly provider-owned Schema types.\n- Keep the raw SDK instance private to the live Layer or adapter module.\n- Provide a live Layer and a mock/test Layer at the same service contract.\n\nDo not expose a generic `use`, `run`, `withClient`, callback, unconstrained generic result, or raw-client accessor. Those APIs erase operation ownership, output provenance, retry policy, and testability.\n\n## Implement each operation linearly\n\nUse the locally installed Effect APIs. A named operation should read as one flat program:\n\n1. encode the checked request at its actual outbound contract, without re-decoding internal typed data;\n2. call exactly one SDK operation through `Effect.tryPromise`, callback adaptation, or the repository's boundary primitive;\n3. map rejection immediately into an owner-named typed Schema error with safe diagnostics;\n4. decode the unknown SDK result immediately with the owning output Schema;\n5. apply operation-specific retry, a complete-operation deadline, tracing, metrics, and redaction policy;\n6. return the decoded value without another wrapper layer.\n\nUse `Effect.gen`, meaningful `Effect.fn`, or local equivalents for readable sequential work. Keep one-use request mapping, rejection mapping, and decoding beside the operation. Extract only demonstrated reuse, stable domain policy, or a real I/O boundary.\n\nFor native Effect HTTP/RPC clients, reuse the domain service contract instead\nof exposing the generated client or inventing a second public service. Keep\nSchema-selected response checks and named transport/decode failures with their\nsemantic owner. Promise adaptation is unnecessary when the client already\nreturns Effect.\n\nA deadline includes headers and decoded body. Test both stalled phases, one\ntotal budget after late headers, underlying cleanup and earlier interruption.\nDo not reset the clock at each phase or add an automatic retry by default.\n\n## Configure safely\n\n- Model semantic configuration with Schema and `Config`/`ConfigProvider`, using the repository's supported API.\n- Give configuration an owner-named structure rather than passing independent primitive strings and numbers through the codebase.\n- Keep secrets redacted and unwrap them only for immediate SDK construction.\n- Construct the SDK once in the live Layer unless its documented lifecycle requires scoped acquisition and release.\n- Override configuration in tests through a test `ConfigProvider` or the repository's established Layer mechanism.\n\n## Model failures explicitly\n\n- Use owner-named Schema-tagged errors for expected configuration, transport, rate-limit, authentication, provider, and decode failures when those distinctions affect callers.\n- Preserve safe provider codes, operation names, retryability, and diagnostic context; do not place unchecked `unknown` payloads in public tagged errors.\n- Use tagged catches or pattern matching. Never use `instanceof` for provider-error policy.\n- Treat truly unexpected failures as defects only when callers cannot reasonably recover.\n\n## Adapt browser hosts and callbacks\n\nKeep the original host object when a method depends on `this`; do not detach\nthe method or decode it into a copied data object. Validate the required\ncapability with the owning Schema. Detect absence inside Effect and distinguish\nit from a supported host refusing an operation. Keep safe refusal details.\n\nScope callback execution and registration together. Release unregisters or\naborts registration and interrupts unfinished callbacks. Accommodate synchronous\nand Promise return forms only where a supported host requires them. Confine the\nbridge and justified lint exceptions to the named adapter. For a browser tool\ninterface, follow the sibling\n[MCP/WebMCP pattern](../strict-effect-ts/references/applications/mcp-and-webmcp.md).\n\nFor a PostHog browser SDK in a React-owned Effect Atom runtime, read the\n[PostHog browser adapter guide](references/posthog-browser.md). It covers scoped\nSDK ownership, explicit event operations, the synchronous capture callback,\nprivacy controls and real-client delivery proof. Native Distilled management\nand backend Effect HTTP capture do not need Promise bridges.\n\n## Test and enforce\n\nTest service operations through mock/test Layers and test the live adapter boundary narrowly. Cover success, request encoding, provider rejection mapping, output decode failure, redaction, timeout/retry policy, and non-idempotent retry exclusion.\n\nUpdate affected architecture docs, READMEs, lint/custom rules and fixtures, CI commands, SPEC/tasks, and repository-owned skills. Add the narrowest reliable static or stale-pattern check the repository supports.\n\nAcceptance requires zero examples or public APIs containing:\n\n- a generic SDK `use` callback or raw-client accessor;\n- a raw `id: string` where an owning branded ID exists;\n- primitive/manual semantic configuration in place of Schema-backed `Config`;\n- `instanceof` provider-error branching;\n- an SDK result escaping without immediate Schema decoding;\n- a one-use wrapper/helper that merely forwards, maps, reads one property, or hides the SDK call.\n\nRun the repository's actual format, lint, typecheck, test, build, boundary, skill-validation, and stale-pattern checks appropriate to the change. Do not invent commands or claim the wrapper is safe when any prohibited pattern remains.\n\n## Keep checked values checked\n\nThe live adapter owns actual untrusted replies. Decode there once and return the\nowning inferred type. A caller does not re-decode a typed service reply; a test\nLayer follows that same contract. Reuse the domain's branded fields and shared\nwhole-record checks in a provider codec, including checks lost when fields are\nspread. Keep expected identity, completeness and range checks as domain policy.\n\nNew branded values use the installed fallible constructor; map its issue to the\noperation's named error. Plain mappings from checked values stay immutable with\nEffect Array/Record functions. Optional provider/source fields decode to Option;\nhistorical missing/null distinctions belong in the source codec. Internal caches\nuse checked readonly keys directly, with equality, full-address and cancellation\ntests. Neither SDK typings nor another internal decoder replaces boundary proof.\nimport type { CalculatorRpcClientError } from \"@taxkit/api-rpc/errors\";\nimport { TaxKitRpcClientLive } from \"@taxkit/api-rpc/live\";\nimport type {\n  CalculatorCatalogResponse,\n  CalculatorRunResponse,\n  CalculatorRunServiceRequest,\n} from \"@taxkit/api-rpc/schemas\";\nimport { TaxKitRpcClient } from \"@taxkit/api-rpc/service\";\nimport { AnnualTaxReport } from \"@taxkit/rules-au-income-tax/schemas\";\nimport {\n  AuPayCalculatorId,\n  PayWithholdingsLedger,\n  TakeHomePayReport,\n} from \"@taxkit/rules-au-pay/schemas\";\nimport { Cause, Effect, Layer, Match, Option, Result, Schema } from \"effect\";\nimport { FetchHttpClient } from \"effect/http\";\nimport * as AsyncResult from \"effect/reactivity/AsyncResult\";\nimport * as Atom from \"effect/reactivity/Atom\";\n\nimport { calculationFailureMessage } from \"./calculation-failure\";\nimport { TaxKitWebConfigError } from \"./config\";\nimport {\n  takeHomeRequestFromForm,\n  annualTaxRequestFromForm,\n  initialTakeHomeForm,\n  AnnualTaxForm,\n  WebsiteInputError,\n  TakeHomeForm,\n} from \"./form.boundary\";\nimport type { WebsiteCalculatorForm } from \"./form.boundary\";\nimport type {\n  WebsiteCalculatorViewState,\n  WebsitePublicSettings,\n} from \"./schemas\";\n\n// These are descriptions of work. React's registry owns client acquisition,\n// execution and release; no module creates or runs a browser ManagedRuntime.\n// The loader seeds these settings for the React registry's whole lifetime.\n// They must survive an idle form before its first calculation.\nexport const publicSettingsAtom = Atom.make(\n  Option.none<WebsitePublicSettings>()\n).pipe(Atom.keepAlive);\nexport const websiteCatalogueAtom = Atom.make(\n  Option.none<CalculatorCatalogResponse>()\n).pipe(Atom.keepAlive);\nexport const calculatorRuntime = Atom.runtime((get) =>\n  Option.match(get(publicSettingsAtom), {\n    onNone: () =>\n      Layer.effect(\n        TaxKitRpcClient,\n        Effect.fail(\n          new TaxKitWebConfigError({\n            message: \"TaxKit web settings are missing or invalid.\",\n            operation: \"settings\",\n            runtime: \"client\",\n          })\n        )\n      ),\n    onSome: (settings) =>\n      TaxKitRpcClientLive(settings.apiOrigin).pipe(\n        Layer.provide(FetchHttpClient.layer)\n      ),\n  })\n);\n// The registry owns separate temporary state for each checked calculator ID.\n// The family memoises descriptions, never a client or a computed answer.\nexport const calculatorPageAtoms = Atom.family(\n  (calculatorId: CalculatorRunServiceRequest[\"calculatorId\"]) => {\n    const form = Atom.make<WebsiteCalculatorForm>(\n      Match.value(calculatorId).pipe(\n        Match.when(\"au.income-tax.annual\", () =>\n          AnnualTaxForm.make({ taxableDollars: \"67000\" })\n        ),\n        Match.when(\"au.pay.take-home\", () => initialTakeHomeForm),\n        Match.orElse(() => ({\n          grossDollars: \"9500\",\n          period: \"monthly\",\n          taxFreeThresholdClaimed: false,\n        }))\n      )\n    );\n    const calculation = calculatorRuntime.fn<CalculatorRunServiceRequest>()(\n      (request) =>\n        TaxKitRpcClient.pipe(\n          Effect.flatMap((client) => client.calculate(request))\n        )\n    );\n    const showSaved = Atom.make(true);\n    const showCalculation = Atom.make(false);\n    const formError = Atom.make(Option.none<string>());\n    const savedReport = Atom.make(\n      Option.none<CalculatorRunResponse[\"report\"]>()\n    );\n    const savedMessage = Atom.make(Option.none<string>());\n    // Checked request identity belongs to one visible attempt. An edit or a\n    // newer manual/tool submission invalidates a waiter for the older attempt.\n    const attempt = Atom.make(Option.none<CalculatorRunServiceRequest>());\n    const cancel = Atom.fnSync<\"cancel\">()((_, get) => {\n      get.set(attempt, Option.none());\n      get.set(calculation, Atom.Interrupt);\n      get.set(showCalculation, false);\n    });\n    const edit = Atom.fnSync<WebsiteCalculatorForm>()((value, get) => {\n      get.set(attempt, Option.none());\n      get.set(calculation, Atom.Interrupt);\n      get.set(showCalculation, false);\n      get.set(showSaved, false);\n      get.set(formError, Option.none());\n      get.set(form, value);\n    });\n    const submit = Atom.fnSync<\"calculate\">()((_, get) => {\n      const current = get(form);\n      const request = Result.gen(function* () {\n        if (calculatorId === \"au.income-tax.annual\") {\n          return yield* \"taxableDollars\" in current\n            ? annualTaxRequestFromForm(current)\n            : Result.fail(\n                new WebsiteInputError({\n                  message: \"Enter a valid annual taxable income.\",\n                })\n              );\n        }\n        return yield* \"grossDollars\" in current\n          ? takeHomeRequestFromForm(\n              current,\n              AuPayCalculatorId.make(calculatorId)\n            )\n          : Result.fail(\n              new WebsiteInputError({\n                message: \"Enter a valid pay amount and pay period.\",\n              })\n            );\n      });\n      get.set(showCalculation, true);\n      get.set(showSaved, false);\n      if (Result.isFailure(request)) {\n        get.set(attempt, Option.none());\n        get.set(calculation, Atom.Interrupt);\n        get.set(formError, Option.some(request.failure.message));\n        return;\n      }\n      get.set(formError, Option.none());\n      get.set(attempt, Option.some(request.success));\n      get.set(calculation, request.success);\n    });\n    const group = {\n      attempt,\n      calculation,\n      cancel,\n      edit,\n      form,\n      formError,\n      savedMessage,\n      savedReport,\n      showCalculation,\n      showSaved,\n      submit,\n      // The registry retains this in-memory page snapshot across an uncommitted\n      // React render. Otherwise idle cleanup can erase once-seeded SSR values\n      // before hydration subscribes. Page cleanup still interrupts live work.\n      // The retained view also holds its whole weak-family description group.\n      // Otherwise browser GC can replace that group on a return visit while the\n      // old values remain in the registry. The callback runs after group creation.\n      // Disposing the root registry releases the snapshot and its client.\n      view: Atom.make((get): WebsiteCalculatorViewState => {\n        const current = get(calculation);\n        const submitted = get(showCalculation);\n        const saved = get(showSaved);\n        const inputError = get(formError);\n        const report = AsyncResult.value(current).pipe(\n          Option.filter(\n            (value) => value.calculator.calculatorId === calculatorId\n          ),\n          Option.map((value) => value.report),\n          Option.orElse(() => get(savedReport)),\n          Option.filter((value) =>\n            Match.value(calculatorId).pipe(\n              Match.when(\"au.income-tax.annual\", () =>\n                Schema.is(AnnualTaxReport)(value)\n              ),\n              Match.when(\"au.pay.take-home\", () =>\n                Schema.is(TakeHomePayReport)(value)\n              ),\n              Match.orElse(() => Schema.is(PayWithholdingsLedger)(value))\n            )\n          )\n        );\n        const message = Option.match(inputError, {\n          onNone: () => {\n            if (\n              submitted &&\n              !current.waiting &&\n              (AsyncResult.isFailure(current) ||\n                (AsyncResult.isSuccess(current) && Option.isNone(report)))\n            ) {\n              if (AsyncResult.isFailure(current)) {\n                return current.cause.pipe(\n                  Cause.findErrorOption,\n                  Option.map(calculationFailureMessage)\n                );\n              }\n              return Option.some(\n                \"The calculation could not finish. Please try again.\"\n              );\n            }\n            return saved ? get(savedMessage) : Option.none<string>();\n          },\n          onSome: Option.some,\n        });\n        return {\n          busy: submitted && current.waiting,\n          calculatorId,\n          form: get(group.form),\n          message,\n          report,\n          stale:\n            Option.isSome(report) &&\n            !saved &&\n            (!submitted ||\n              current.waiting ||\n              !AsyncResult.isSuccess(current) ||\n              Option.isSome(inputError)),\n        };\n      }).pipe(Atom.keepAlive),\n    } as const;\n    return group;\n  }\n);\n\n// Home uses the same page commands and state owner as the other calculators.\n// These existing names retain their narrow React/test call sites.\nconst home = calculatorPageAtoms(AuPayCalculatorId.make(\"au.pay.take-home\"));\nexport const calculateAtom: Atom.AtomResultFn<\n  CalculatorRunServiceRequest,\n  CalculatorRunResponse,\n  CalculatorRpcClientError | TaxKitWebConfigError\n> = home.calculation;\nexport const takeHomeFormAtom = Atom.writable(\n  (get) => {\n    const form = get(home.form);\n    return Schema.is(TakeHomeForm)(form) ? form : initialTakeHomeForm;\n  },\n  (get, form: TakeHomeForm) => get.set(home.form, form)\n);\nexport const submitTakeHomeAtom = home.submit;\nexport const editTakeHomeAtom = Atom.fnSync<TakeHomeForm>()((value, get) =>\n  get.set(home.edit, value)\n);\nimport { Config, Effect, Match, Schema } from \"effect\";\n\nimport { AnalyticsConfigurationError } from \"./errors.js\";\nimport type { AnalyticsSettings } from \"./schemas.js\";\nimport { AnalyticsDisabled, AnalyticsEnabled } from \"./schemas.js\";\n\n// Off is a deliberate mode. Missing or malformed enabled settings have a\n// separate failure; no token is acquired by the disabled branch.\nexport const AnalyticsSettingsConfig: Effect.Effect<\n  AnalyticsSettings,\n  AnalyticsConfigurationError\n> = Config.schema(\n  Schema.Literals([\"off\", \"production\", \"controlled-preview\"]),\n  \"POSTHOG_COLLECTION_MODE\"\n).pipe(\n  Config.withDefault(\"off\"),\n  Effect.flatMap((mode) =>\n    Match.value(mode).pipe(\n      Match.when(\"off\", () => Effect.succeed(AnalyticsDisabled.make({}))),\n      Match.orElse((environment) =>\n        Effect.all({\n          projectId: Config.schema(\n            AnalyticsEnabled.fields.projectId,\n            \"POSTHOG_PROJECT_ID\"\n          ),\n          region: Config.schema(\n            AnalyticsEnabled.fields.region,\n            \"POSTHOG_REGION\"\n          ),\n          stage: Config.schema(AnalyticsEnabled.fields.stage, \"POSTHOG_STAGE\"),\n          token: Config.schema(\n            AnalyticsEnabled.fields.token,\n            \"POSTHOG_CAPTURE_TOKEN\"\n          ),\n        }).pipe(\n          Effect.flatMap((settings) =>\n            AnalyticsEnabled.makeEffect({\n              environment,\n              ...settings,\n            })\n          )\n        )\n      )\n    )\n  ),\n  Effect.mapError(\n    () => new AnalyticsConfigurationError({ operation: \"configure\" })\n  )\n);\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":8917},"formatted_output":"web build:native-pair: [22:28:09.088] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] (!) Your Vite config uses features that are unsupported by `configLoader: 'native'`, which is planned to become the default in a future major version of Vite:\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.088] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:8:8). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.088] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"./docs-images.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:9:39). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.088] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.schemas.ts:3:38). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.088] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] Set `VITE_CONFIG_NATIVE_IGNORE_WARNING=true` to suppress this warning.\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.755] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] (!) Your Vite config uses features that are unsupported by `configLoader: 'native'`, which is planned to become the default in a future major version of Vite:\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.756] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:8:8). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.756] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"./docs-images.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:9:39). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.756] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.schemas.ts:3:38). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.756] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] Set `VITE_CONFIG_NATIVE_IGNORE_WARNING=true` to suppress this warning.\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.272] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] (!) Your Vite config uses features that are unsupported by `configLoader: 'native'`, which is planned to become the default in a future major version of Vite:\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.272] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:8:8). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.272] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"./docs-images.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:9:39). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.272] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.schemas.ts:3:38). Add the file extension\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.272] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] Set `VITE_CONFIG_NATIVE_IGNORE_WARNING=true` to suppress this warning.\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.766] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] vite v8.3.2 building client environment for production...\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.772] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] [MDX] generated files in 0.8558750000001965ms\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:13.046] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] ✓ built in 2.28s\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:13.046] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] vite v8.3.2 building ssr environment for production...\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:13.050] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] [MDX] generated files in 0.315415999999459ms\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:13.717] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] ✓ built in 671ms\nweb build:native-pair: Exited with code 0\nweb test:native-pair: \nweb test:native-pair:  RUN  v5.0.3 /Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit/apps/web\nweb test:native-pair: \n---\nname: effect-client-wrapper\ndescription: Design, implement, or review a typed Effect service around a third-party SDK, API client, callback library, or Promise-based provider. Use for provider adapters, service Layers, external-client configuration, request and response Schemas, typed provider errors, retries, and test Layers. Enforce named operations, branded identifiers, Schema-backed Config, immediate output decoding, flat Effects, and the explicit rejection of generic use callbacks, raw clients, primitive config, instanceof, and unchecked SDK outputs.\n---\n\n# Effect Client Wrapper\n\nCreate a semantic adapter owned by the application, not a generic Effect-shaped escape hatch around an SDK.\n\n## Establish the boundary\n\n1. Read applicable repository instructions, architecture docs, lint rules, installed Effect and SDK versions, and representative services and Layers.\n2. Identify the owner of every request, response, identifier, configuration value, error, retry policy, and runtime boundary.\n3. Research the cloned Effect v4 source, record its revision/version, then reconcile the chosen APIs with installed source/types. Use matching primary SDK source for its contract; DeepWiki through Executor MCP is secondary explanation for the upstream Effect/SDK repository.\n4. Prefer extending an existing semantic adapter over creating a parallel client abstraction.\n\n## Define the public service\n\n- Expose named domain/provider operations such as `getCustomer`, `sendMessage`, or `renderImage`.\n- Accept owning Schema-derived inputs and branded identifiers. Never substitute raw `id: string`.\n- Return only decoded application-owned or explicitly provider-owned Schema types.\n- Keep the raw SDK instance private to the live Layer or adapter module.\n- Provide a live Layer and a mock/test Layer at the same service contract.\n\nDo not expose a generic `use`, `run`, `withClient`, callback, unconstrained generic result, or raw-client accessor. Those APIs erase operation ownership, output provenance, retry policy, and testability.\n\n## Implement each operation linearly\n\nUse the locally installed Effect APIs. A named operation should read as one flat program:\n\n1. encode the checked request at its actual outbound contract, without re-decoding internal typed data;\n2. call exactly one SDK operation through `Effect.tryPromise`, callback adaptation, or the repository's boundary primitive;\n3. map rejection immediately into an owner-named typed Schema error with safe diagnostics;\n4. decode the unknown SDK result immediately with the owning output Schema;\n5. apply operation-specific retry, a complete-operation deadline, tracing, metrics, and redaction policy;\n6. return the decoded value without another wrapper layer.\n\nUse `Effect.gen`, meaningful `Effect.fn`, or local equivalents for readable sequential work. Keep one-use request mapping, rejection mapping, and decoding beside the operation. Extract only demonstrated reuse, stable domain policy, or a real I/O boundary.\n\nFor native Effect HTTP/RPC clients, reuse the domain service contract instead\nof exposing the generated client or inventing a second public service. Keep\nSchema-selected response checks and named transport/decode failures with their\nsemantic owner. Promise adaptation is unnecessary when the client already\nreturns Effect.\n\nA deadline includes headers and decoded body. Test both stalled phases, one\ntotal budget after late headers, underlying cleanup and earlier interruption.\nDo not reset the clock at each phase or add an automatic retry by default.\n\n## Configure safely\n\n- Model semantic configuration with Schema and `Config`/`ConfigProvider`, using the repository's supported API.\n- Give configuration an owner-named structure rather than passing independent primitive strings and numbers through the codebase.\n- Keep secrets redacted and unwrap them only for immediate SDK construction.\n- Construct the SDK once in the live Layer unless its documented lifecycle requires scoped acquisition and release.\n- Override configuration in tests through a test `ConfigProvider` or the repository's established Layer mechanism.\n\n## Model failures explicitly\n\n- Use owner-named Schema-tagged errors for expected configuration, transport, rate-limit, authentication, provider, and decode failures when those distinctions affect callers.\n- Preserve safe provider codes, operation names, retryability, and diagnostic context; do not place unchecked `unknown` payloads in public tagged errors.\n- Use tagged catches or pattern matching. Never use `instanceof` for provider-error policy.\n- Treat truly unexpected failures as defects only when callers cannot reasonably recover.\n\n## Adapt browser hosts and callbacks\n\nKeep the original host object when a method depends on `this`; do not detach\nthe method or decode it into a copied data object. Validate the required\ncapability with the owning Schema. Detect absence inside Effect and distinguish\nit from a supported host refusing an operation. Keep safe refusal details.\n\nScope callback execution and registration together. Release unregisters or\naborts registration and interrupts unfinished callbacks. Accommodate synchronous\nand Promise return forms only where a supported host requires them. Confine the\nbridge and justified lint exceptions to the named adapter. For a browser tool\ninterface, follow the sibling\n[MCP/WebMCP pattern](../strict-effect-ts/references/applications/mcp-and-webmcp.md).\n\nFor a PostHog browser SDK in a React-owned Effect Atom runtime, read the\n[PostHog browser adapter guide](references/posthog-browser.md). It covers scoped\nSDK ownership, explicit event operations, the synchronous capture callback,\nprivacy controls and real-client delivery proof. Native Distilled management\nand backend Effect HTTP capture do not need Promise bridges.\n\n## Test and enforce\n\nTest service operations through mock/test Layers and test the live adapter boundary narrowly. Cover success, request encoding, provider rejection mapping, output decode failure, redaction, timeout/retry policy, and non-idempotent retry exclusion.\n\nUpdate affected architecture docs, READMEs, lint/custom rules and fixtures, CI commands, SPEC/tasks, and repository-owned skills. Add the narrowest reliable static or stale-pattern check the repository supports.\n\nAcceptance requires zero examples or public APIs containing:\n\n- a generic SDK `use` callback or raw-client accessor;\n- a raw `id: string` where an owning branded ID exists;\n- primitive/manual semantic configuration in place of Schema-backed `Config`;\n- `instanceof` provider-error branching;\n- an SDK result escaping without immediate Schema decoding;\n- a one-use wrapper/helper that merely forwards, maps, reads one property, or hides the SDK call.\n\nRun the repository's actual format, lint, typecheck, test, build, boundary, skill-validation, and stale-pattern checks appropriate to the change. Do not invent commands or claim the wrapper is safe when any prohibited pattern remains.\n\n## Keep checked values checked\n\nThe live adapter owns actual untrusted replies. Decode there once and return the\nowning inferred type. A caller does not re-decode a typed service reply; a test\nLayer follows that same contract. Reuse the domain's branded fields and shared\nwhole-record checks in a provider codec, including checks lost when fields are\nspread. Keep expected identity, completeness and range checks as domain policy.\n\nNew branded values use the installed fallible constructor; map its issue to the\noperation's named error. Plain mappings from checked values stay immutable with\nEffect Array/Record functions. Optional provider/source fields decode to Option;\nhistorical missing/null distinctions belong in the source codec. Internal caches\nuse checked readonly keys directly, with equality, full-address and cancellation\ntests. Neither SDK typings nor another internal decoder replaces boundary proof.\nimport type { CalculatorRpcClientError } from \"@taxkit/api-rpc/errors\";\nimport { TaxKitRpcClientLive } from \"@taxkit/api-rpc/live\";\nimport type {\n  CalculatorCatalogResponse,\n  CalculatorRunResponse,\n  CalculatorRunServiceRequest,\n} from \"@taxkit/api-rpc/schemas\";\nimport { TaxKitRpcClient } from \"@taxkit/api-rpc/service\";\nimport { AnnualTaxReport } from \"@taxkit/rules-au-income-tax/schemas\";\nimport {\n  AuPayCalculatorId,\n  PayWithholdingsLedger,\n  TakeHomePayReport,\n} from \"@taxkit/rules-au-pay/schemas\";\nimport { Cause, Effect, Layer, Match, Option, Result, Schema } from \"effect\";\nimport { FetchHttpClient } from \"effect/http\";\nimport * as AsyncResult from \"effect/reactivity/AsyncResult\";\nimport * as Atom from \"effect/reactivity/Atom\";\n\nimport { calculationFailureMessage } from \"./calculation-failure\";\nimport { TaxKitWebConfigError } from \"./config\";\nimport {\n  takeHomeRequestFromForm,\n  annualTaxRequestFromForm,\n  initialTakeHomeForm,\n  AnnualTaxForm,\n  WebsiteInputError,\n  TakeHomeForm,\n} from \"./form.boundary\";\nimport type { WebsiteCalculatorForm } from \"./form.boundary\";\nimport type {\n  WebsiteCalculatorViewState,\n  WebsitePublicSettings,\n} from \"./schemas\";\n\n// These are descriptions of work. React's registry owns client acquisition,\n// execution and release; no module creates or runs a browser ManagedRuntime.\n// The loader seeds these settings for the React registry's whole lifetime.\n// They must survive an idle form before its first calculation.\nexport const publicSettingsAtom = Atom.make(\n  Option.none<WebsitePublicSettings>()\n).pipe(Atom.keepAlive);\nexport const websiteCatalogueAtom = Atom.make(\n  Option.none<CalculatorCatalogResponse>()\n).pipe(Atom.keepAlive);\nexport const calculatorRuntime = Atom.runtime((get) =>\n  Option.match(get(publicSettingsAtom), {\n    onNone: () =>\n      Layer.effect(\n        TaxKitRpcClient,\n        Effect.fail(\n          new TaxKitWebConfigError({\n            message: \"TaxKit web settings are missing or invalid.\",\n            operation: \"settings\",\n            runtime: \"client\",\n          })\n        )\n      ),\n    onSome: (settings) =>\n      TaxKitRpcClientLive(settings.apiOrigin).pipe(\n        Layer.provide(FetchHttpClient.layer)\n      ),\n  })\n);\n// The registry owns separate temporary state for each checked calculator ID.\n// The family memoises descriptions, never a client or a computed answer.\nexport const calculatorPageAtoms = Atom.family(\n  (calculatorId: CalculatorRunServiceRequest[\"calculatorId\"]) => {\n    const form = Atom.make<WebsiteCalculatorForm>(\n      Match.value(calculatorId).pipe(\n        Match.when(\"au.income-tax.annual\", () =>\n          AnnualTaxForm.make({ taxableDollars: \"67000\" })\n        ),\n        Match.when(\"au.pay.take-home\", () => initialTakeHomeForm),\n        Match.orElse(() => ({\n          grossDollars: \"9500\",\n          period: \"monthly\",\n          taxFreeThresholdClaimed: false,\n        }))\n      )\n    );\n    const calculation = calculatorRuntime.fn<CalculatorRunServiceRequest>()(\n      (request) =>\n        TaxKitRpcClient.pipe(\n          Effect.flatMap((client) => client.calculate(request))\n        )\n    );\n    const showSaved = Atom.make(true);\n    const showCalculation = Atom.make(false);\n    const formError = Atom.make(Option.none<string>());\n    const savedReport = Atom.make(\n      Option.none<CalculatorRunResponse[\"report\"]>()\n    );\n    const savedMessage = Atom.make(Option.none<string>());\n    // Checked request identity belongs to one visible attempt. An edit or a\n    // newer manual/tool submission invalidates a waiter for the older attempt.\n    const attempt = Atom.make(Option.none<CalculatorRunServiceRequest>());\n    const cancel = Atom.fnSync<\"cancel\">()((_, get) => {\n      get.set(attempt, Option.none());\n      get.set(calculation, Atom.Interrupt);\n      get.set(showCalculation, false);\n    });\n    const edit = Atom.fnSync<WebsiteCalculatorForm>()((value, get) => {\n      get.set(attempt, Option.none());\n      get.set(calculation, Atom.Interrupt);\n      get.set(showCalculation, false);\n      get.set(showSaved, false);\n      get.set(formError, Option.none());\n      get.set(form, value);\n    });\n    const submit = Atom.fnSync<\"calculate\">()((_, get) => {\n      const current = get(form);\n      const request = Result.gen(function* () {\n        if (calculatorId === \"au.income-tax.annual\") {\n          return yield* \"taxableDollars\" in current\n            ? annualTaxRequestFromForm(current)\n            : Result.fail(\n                new WebsiteInputError({\n                  message: \"Enter a valid annual taxable income.\",\n                })\n              );\n        }\n        return yield* \"grossDollars\" in current\n          ? takeHomeRequestFromForm(\n              current,\n              AuPayCalculatorId.make(calculatorId)\n            )\n          : Result.fail(\n              new WebsiteInputError({\n                message: \"Enter a valid pay amount and pay period.\",\n              })\n            );\n      });\n      get.set(showCalculation, true);\n      get.set(showSaved, false);\n      if (Result.isFailure(request)) {\n        get.set(attempt, Option.none());\n        get.set(calculation, Atom.Interrupt);\n        get.set(formError, Option.some(request.failure.message));\n        return;\n      }\n      get.set(formError, Option.none());\n      get.set(attempt, Option.some(request.success));\n      get.set(calculation, request.success);\n    });\n    const group = {\n      attempt,\n      calculation,\n      cancel,\n      edit,\n      form,\n      formError,\n      savedMessage,\n      savedReport,\n      showCalculation,\n      showSaved,\n      submit,\n      // The registry retains this in-memory page snapshot across an uncommitted\n      // React render. Otherwise idle cleanup can erase once-seeded SSR values\n      // before hydration subscribes. Page cleanup still interrupts live work.\n      // The retained view also holds its whole weak-family description group.\n      // Otherwise browser GC can replace that group on a return visit while the\n      // old values remain in the registry. The callback runs after group creation.\n      // Disposing the root registry releases the snapshot and its client.\n      view: Atom.make((get): WebsiteCalculatorViewState => {\n        const current = get(calculation);\n        const submitted = get(showCalculation);\n        const saved = get(showSaved);\n        const inputError = get(formError);\n        const report = AsyncResult.value(current).pipe(\n          Option.filter(\n            (value) => value.calculator.calculatorId === calculatorId\n          ),\n          Option.map((value) => value.report),\n          Option.orElse(() => get(savedReport)),\n          Option.filter((value) =>\n            Match.value(calculatorId).pipe(\n              Match.when(\"au.income-tax.annual\", () =>\n                Schema.is(AnnualTaxReport)(value)\n              ),\n              Match.when(\"au.pay.take-home\", () =>\n                Schema.is(TakeHomePayReport)(value)\n              ),\n              Match.orElse(() => Schema.is(PayWithholdingsLedger)(value))\n            )\n          )\n        );\n        const message = Option.match(inputError, {\n          onNone: () => {\n            if (\n              submitted &&\n              !current.waiting &&\n              (AsyncResult.isFailure(current) ||\n                (AsyncResult.isSuccess(current) && Option.isNone(report)))\n            ) {\n              if (AsyncResult.isFailure(current)) {\n                return current.cause.pipe(\n                  Cause.findErrorOption,\n                  Option.map(calculationFailureMessage)\n                );\n              }\n              return Option.some(\n                \"The calculation could not finish. Please try again.\"\n              );\n            }\n            return saved ? get(savedMessage) : Option.none<string>();\n          },\n          onSome: Option.some,\n        });\n        return {\n          busy: submitted && current.waiting,\n          calculatorId,\n          form: get(group.form),\n          message,\n          report,\n          stale:\n            Option.isSome(report) &&\n            !saved &&\n            (!submitted ||\n              current.waiting ||\n              !AsyncResult.isSuccess(current) ||\n              Option.isSome(inputError)),\n        };\n      }).pipe(Atom.keepAlive),\n    } as const;\n    return group;\n  }\n);\n\n// Home uses the same page commands and state owner as the other calculators.\n// These existing names retain their narrow React/test call sites.\nconst home = calculatorPageAtoms(AuPayCalculatorId.make(\"au.pay.take-home\"));\nexport const calculateAtom: Atom.AtomResultFn<\n  CalculatorRunServiceRequest,\n  CalculatorRunResponse,\n  CalculatorRpcClientError | TaxKitWebConfigError\n> = home.calculation;\nexport const takeHomeFormAtom = Atom.writable(\n  (get) => {\n    const form = get(home.form);\n    return Schema.is(TakeHomeForm)(form) ? form : initialTakeHomeForm;\n  },\n  (get, form: TakeHomeForm) => get.set(home.form, form)\n);\nexport const submitTakeHomeAtom = home.submit;\nexport const editTakeHomeAtom = Atom.fnSync<TakeHomeForm>()((value, get) =>\n  get.set(home.edit, value)\n);\nimport { Config, Effect, Match, Schema } from \"effect\";\n\nimport { AnalyticsConfigurationError } from \"./errors.js\";\nimport type { AnalyticsSettings } from \"./schemas.js\";\nimport { AnalyticsDisabled, AnalyticsEnabled } from \"./schemas.js\";\n\n// Off is a deliberate mode. Missing or malformed enabled settings have a\n// separate failure; no token is acquired by the disabled branch.\nexport const AnalyticsSettingsConfig: Effect.Effect<\n  AnalyticsSettings,\n  AnalyticsConfigurationError\n> = Config.schema(\n  Schema.Literals([\"off\", \"production\", \"controlled-preview\"]),\n  \"POSTHOG_COLLECTION_MODE\"\n).pipe(\n  Config.withDefault(\"off\"),\n  Effect.flatMap((mode) =>\n    Match.value(mode).pipe(\n      Match.when(\"off\", () => Effect.succeed(AnalyticsDisabled.make({}))),\n      Match.orElse((environment) =>\n        Effect.all({\n          projectId: Config.schema(\n            AnalyticsEnabled.fields.projectId,\n            \"POSTHOG_PROJECT_ID\"\n          ),\n          region: Config.schema(\n            AnalyticsEnabled.fields.region,\n            \"POSTHOG_REGION\"\n          ),\n          stage: Config.schema(AnalyticsEnabled.fields.stage, \"POSTHOG_STAGE\"),\n          token: Config.schema(\n            AnalyticsEnabled.fields.token,\n            \"POSTHOG_CAPTURE_TOKEN\"\n          ),\n        }).pipe(\n          Effect.flatMap((settings) =>\n            AnalyticsEnabled.makeEffect({\n              environment,\n              ...settings,\n            })\n          )\n        )\n      )\n    )\n  ),\n  Effect.mapError(\n    () => new AnalyticsConfigurationError({ operation: \"configure\" })\n  )\n);\n"},"started_at_ms":1791372554500,"completed_at_ms":1791372554500}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T11:29:14.508Z","ordinal":69394,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","session_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","root_turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","response_id":"resp_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac62d0159e887d0bc878a615598ddff","usage":{"input_tokens":128102,"cached_input_tokens":126720,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":234,"reasoning_output_tokens":83,"total_tokens":128336},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":62164953,"cached_input_tokens":60909312,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":305418,"reasoning_output_tokens":117058,"total_tokens":62470371},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1298675155,"cached_input_tokens":1271932800,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":6443480,"reasoning_output_tokens":2866895,"total_tokens":1305118635}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T11:29:14.593Z","ordinal":69395,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1161f-f161-7b92-8ab9-753482263196","call_id":"call_brgjfiG2h3wP0IhKRNJ5ZIzi","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"5e31ff\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000008917,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":5558,\"output\":\"web build:native-pair: [22:28:09.088] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] (!) Your Vite config uses features that are unsupported by `configLoader: 'native'`, which is planned to become the default in a future major version of Vite:\\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.088] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \\\"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\\\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:8:8). Add the file extension\\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.088] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \\\"./docs-images.schemas\\\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:9:39). Add the file extension\\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.088] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \\\"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\\\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.schemas.ts:3:38). Add the file extension\\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.088] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] Set `VITE_CONFIG_NATIVE_IGNORE_WARNING=true` to suppress this warning.\\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.755] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] (!) Your Vite config uses features that are unsupported by `configLoader: 'native'`, which is planned to become the default in a future major version of Vite:\\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.756] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \\\"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\\\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:8:8). Add the file extension\\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.756] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \\\"./docs-images.schemas\\\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:9:39). Add the file extension\\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.756] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \\\"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\\\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.schemas.ts:3:38). Add the file extension\\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:09.756] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] Set `VITE_CONFIG_NATIVE_IGNORE_WARNING=true` to suppress this warning.\\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.272] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] (!) Your Vite config uses features that are unsupported by `configLoader: 'native'`, which is planned to become the default in a future major version of Vite:\\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.272] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \\\"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\\\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:8:8). Add the file extension\\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.272] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \\\"./docs-images.schemas\\\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.build.ts:9:39). Add the file extension\\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.272] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite]   - import \\\"../src/lib/docs/social.schemas\\\" without a file extension (scripts/docs-images.schemas.ts:3:38). Add the file extension\\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.272] INFO (#745): [TaxKitWebsite] Set `VITE_CONFIG_NATIVE_IGNORE_WARNING=true` to suppress this warning.\\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.766] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] vite v8.3.2 building client environment for production...\\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:10.772] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] [MDX] generated files in 0.8558750000001965ms\\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:13.046] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] ✓ built in 2.28s\\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:13.046] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] vite v8.3.2 building ssr environment for production...\\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:13.050] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] [MDX] generated files in 0.315415999999459ms\\nweb build:native-pair: [22:28:13.717] INFO (#744): [TaxKitWebsite] ✓ built in 671ms\\nweb build:native-pair: Exited with code 0\\nweb test:native-pair: \\nweb test:native-pair:  RUN  v5.0.3 /Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit/apps/web\\nweb test:native-pair: \\n---\\nname: effect-client-wrapper\\ndescription: Design, implement, or review a typed Effect service around a third-party SDK, API client, callback library, or Promise-based provider. Use for provider adapters, service Layers, external-client configuration, request and response Schemas, typed provider errors, retries, and test Layers. Enforce named operations, branded identifiers, Schema-backed Config, immediate output decoding, flat Effects, and the explicit rejection of generic use callbacks, raw clients, primitive config, instanceof, and unchecked SDK outputs.\\n---\\n\\n# Effect Client Wrapper\\n\\nCreate a semantic adapter owned by the application, not a generic Effect-shaped escape hatch around an SDK.\\n\\n## Establish the boundary\\n\\n1. Read applicable repository instructions, architecture docs, lint rules, installed Effect and SDK versions, and representative services and Layers.\\n2. Identify the owner of every request, response, identifier, configuration value, error, retry policy, and runtime boundary.\\n3. Research the cloned Effect v4 source, record its revision/version, then reconcile the chosen APIs with installed source/types. Use matching primary SDK source for its contract; DeepWiki through Executor MCP is secondary explanation for the upstream Effect/SDK repository.\\n4. Prefer extending an existing semantic adapter over creating a parallel client abstraction.\\n\\n## Define the public service\\n\\n- Expose named domain/provider operations such as `getCustomer`, `sendMessage`, or `renderImage`.\\n- Accept owning Schema-derived inputs and branded identifiers. Never substitute raw `id: string`.\\n- Return only decoded application-owned or explicitly provider-owned Schema types.\\n- Keep the raw SDK instance private to the live Layer or adapter module.\\n- Provide a live Layer and a mock/test Layer at the same service contract.\\n\\nDo not expose a generic `use`, `run`, `withClient`, callback, unconstrained generic result, or raw-client accessor. Those APIs erase operation ownership, output provenance, retry policy, and testability.\\n\\n## Implement each operation linearly\\n\\nUse the locally installed Effect APIs. A named operation should read as one flat program:\\n\\n1. encode the checked request at its actual outbound contract, without re-decoding internal typed data;\\n2. call exactly one SDK operation through `Effect.tryPromise`, callback adaptation, or the repository's boundary primitive;\\n3. map rejection immediately into an owner-named typed Schema error with safe diagnostics;\\n4. decode the unknown SDK result immediately with the owning output Schema;\\n5. apply operation-specific retry, a complete-operation deadline, tracing, metrics, and redaction policy;\\n6. return the decoded value without another wrapper layer.\\n\\nUse `Effect.gen`, meaningful `Effect.fn`, or local equivalents for readable sequential work. Keep one-use request mapping, rejection mapping, and decoding beside the operation. Extract only demonstrated reuse, stable domain policy, or a real I/O boundary.\\n\\nFor native Effect HTTP/RPC clients, reuse the domain service contract instead\\nof exposing the generated client or inventing a second public service. Keep\\nSchema-selected response checks and named transport/decode failures with their\\nsemantic owner. Promise adaptation is unnecessary when the client already\\nreturns Effect.\\n\\nA deadline includes headers and decoded body. Test both stalled phases, one\\ntotal budget after late headers, underlying cleanup and earlier interruption.\\nDo not reset the clock at each phase or add an automatic retry by default.\\n\\n## Configure safely\\n\\n- Model semantic configuration with Schema and `Config`/`ConfigProvider`, using the repository's supported API.\\n- Give configuration an owner-named structure rather than passing independent primitive strings and numbers through the codebase.\\n- Keep secrets redacted and unwrap them only for immediate SDK construction.\\n- Construct the SDK once in the live Layer unless its documented lifecycle requires scoped acquisition and release.\\n- Override configuration in tests through a test `ConfigProvider` or the repository's established Layer mechanism.\\n\\n## Model failures explicitly\\n\\n- Use owner-named Schema-tagged errors for expected configuration, transport, rate-limit, authentication, provider, and decode failures when those distinctions affect callers.\\n- Preserve safe provider codes, operation names, retryability, and diagnostic context; do not place unchecked `unknown` payloads in public tagged errors.\\n- Use tagged catches or pattern matching. Never use `instanceof` for provider-error policy.\\n- Treat truly unexpected failures as defects only when callers cannot reasonably recover.\\n\\n## Adapt browser hosts and callbacks\\n\\nKeep the original host object when a method depends on `this`; do not detach\\nthe method or decode it into a copied data object. Validate the required\\ncapability with the owning Schema. Detect absence inside Effect and distinguish\\nit from a supported host refusing an operation. Keep safe refusal details.\\n\\nScope callback execution and registration together. Release unregisters or\\naborts registration and interrupts unfinished callbacks. Accommodate synchronous\\nand Promise return forms only where a supported host requires them. Confine the\\nbridge and justified lint exceptions to the named adapter. For a browser tool\\ninterface, follow the sibling\\n[MCP/WebMCP pattern](../strict-effect-ts/references/applications/mcp-and-webmcp.md).\\n\\nFor a PostHog browser SDK in a React-owned Effect Atom runtime, read the\\n[PostHog browser adapter guide](references/posthog-browser.md). It covers scoped\\nSDK ownership, explicit event operations, the synchronous capture callback,\\nprivacy controls and real-client delivery proof. Native Distilled management\\nand backend Effect HTTP capture do not need Promise bridges.\\n\\n## Test and enforce\\n\\nTest service operations through mock/test Layers and test the live adapter boundary narrowly. Cover success, request encoding, provider rejection mapping, output decode failure, redaction, timeout/retry policy, and non-idempotent retry exclusion.\\n\\nUpdate affected architecture docs, READMEs, lint/custom rules and fixtures, CI commands, SPEC/tasks, and repository-owned skills. Add the narrowest reliable static or stale-pattern check the repository supports.\\n\\nAcceptance requires zero examples or public APIs containing:\\n\\n- a generic SDK `use` callback or raw-client accessor;\\n- a raw `id: string` where an owning branded ID exists;\\n- primitive/manual semantic configuration in place of Schema-backed `Config`;\\n- `instanceof` provider-error branching;\\n- an SDK result escaping without immediate Schema decoding;\\n- a one-use wrapper/helper that merely forwards, maps, reads one property, or hides the SDK call.\\n\\nRun the repository's actual format, lint, typecheck, test, build, boundary, skill-validation, and stale-pattern checks appropriate to the change. Do not invent commands or claim the wrapper is safe when any prohibited pattern remains.\\n\\n## Keep checked values checked\\n\\nThe live adapter owns actual untrusted replies. Decode there once and return the\\nowning inferred type. A caller does not re-decode a typed service reply; a test\\nLayer follows that same contract. Reuse the domain's branded fields and shared\\nwhole-record checks in a provider codec, including checks lost when fields are\\nspread. Keep expected identity, completeness and range checks as domain policy.\\n\\nNew branded values use the installed fallible constructor; map its issue to the\\noperation's named error. Plain mappings from checked values stay immutable with\\nEffect Array/Record functions. Optional provider/source fields decode to Option;\\nhistorical missing/null distinctions belong in the source codec. Internal caches\\nuse checked readonly keys directly, with equality, full-address and cancellation\\ntests. Neither SDK typings nor another internal decoder replaces boundary proof.\\nimport type { CalculatorRpcClientError } from \\\"@taxkit/api-rpc/errors\\\";\\nimport { TaxKitRpcClientLive } from \\\"@taxkit/api-rpc/live\\\";\\nimport type {\\n  CalculatorCatalogResponse,\\n  CalculatorRunResponse,\\n  CalculatorRunServiceRequest,\\n} from \\\"@taxkit/api-rpc/schemas\\\";\\nimport { TaxKitRpcClient } from \\\"@taxkit/api-rpc/service\\\";\\nimport { AnnualTaxReport } from \\\"@taxkit/rules-au-income-tax/schemas\\\";\\nimport {\\n  AuPayCalculatorId,\\n  PayWithholdingsLedger,\\n  TakeHomePayReport,\\n} from \\\"@taxkit/rules-au-pay/schemas\\\";\\nimport { Cause, Effect, Layer, Match, Option, Result, Schema } from \\\"effect\\\";\\nimport { FetchHttpClient } from \\\"effect/http\\\";\\nimport * as AsyncResult from \\\"effect/reactivity/AsyncResult\\\";\\nimport * as Atom from \\\"effect/reactivity/Atom\\\";\\n\\nimport { calculationFailureMessage } from \\\"./calculation-failure\\\";\\nimport { TaxKitWebConfigError } from \\\"./config\\\";\\nimport {\\n  takeHomeRequestFromForm,\\n  annualTaxRequestFromForm,\\n  initialTakeHomeForm,\\n  AnnualTaxForm,\\n  WebsiteInputError,\\n  TakeHomeForm,\\n} from \\\"./form.boundary\\\";\\nimport type { WebsiteCalculatorForm } from \\\"./form.boundary\\\";\\nimport type {\\n  WebsiteCalculatorViewState,\\n  WebsitePublicSettings,\\n} from \\\"./schemas\\\";\\n\\n// These are descriptions of work. React's registry owns client acquisition,\\n// execution and release; no module creates or runs a browser ManagedRuntime.\\n// The loader seeds these settings for the React registry's whole lifetime.\\n// They must survive an idle form before its first calculation.\\nexport const publicSettingsAtom = Atom.make(\\n  Option.none<WebsitePublicSettings>()\\n).pipe(Atom.keepAlive);\\nexport const websiteCatalogueAtom = Atom.make(\\n  Option.none<CalculatorCatalogResponse>()\\n).pipe(Atom.keepAlive);\\nexport const calculatorRuntime = Atom.runtime((get) =>\\n  Option.match(get(publicSettingsAtom), {\\n    onNone: () =>\\n      Layer.effect(\\n        TaxKitRpcClient,\\n        Effect.fail(\\n          new TaxKitWebConfigError({\\n            message: \\\"TaxKit web settings are missing or invalid.\\\",\\n            operation: \\\"settings\\\",\\n            runtime: \\\"client\\\",\\n          })\\n        )\\n      ),\\n    onSome: (settings) =>\\n      TaxKitRpcClientLive(settings.apiOrigin).pipe(\\n        Layer.provide(FetchHttpClient.layer)\\n      ),\\n  })\\n);\\n// The registry owns separate temporary state for each checked calculator ID.\\n// The family memoises descriptions, never a client or a computed answer.\\nexport const calculatorPageAtoms = Atom.family(\\n  (calculatorId: CalculatorRunServiceRequest[\\\"calculatorId\\\"]) => {\\n    const form = Atom.make<WebsiteCalculatorForm>(\\n      Match.value(calculatorId).pipe(\\n        Match.when(\\\"au.income-tax.annual\\\", () =>\\n          AnnualTaxForm.make({ taxableDollars: \\\"67000\\\" })\\n        ),\\n        Match.when(\\\"au.pay.take-home\\\", () => initialTakeHomeForm),\\n        Match.orElse(() => ({\\n          grossDollars: \\\"9500\\\",\\n          period: \\\"monthly\\\",\\n          taxFreeThresholdClaimed: false,\\n        }))\\n      )\\n    );\\n    const calculation = calculatorRuntime.fn<CalculatorRunServiceRequest>()(\\n      (request) =>\\n        TaxKitRpcClient.pipe(\\n          Effect.flatMap((client) => client.calculate(request))\\n        )\\n    );\\n    const showSaved = Atom.make(true);\\n    const showCalculation = Atom.make(false);\\n    const formError = Atom.make(Option.none<string>());\\n    const savedReport = Atom.make(\\n      Option.none<CalculatorRunResponse[\\\"report\\\"]>()\\n    );\\n    const savedMessage = Atom.make(Option.none<string>());\\n    // Checked request identity belongs to one visible attempt. An edit or a\\n    // newer manual/tool submission invalidates a waiter for the older attempt.\\n    const attempt = Atom.make(Option.none<CalculatorRunServiceRequest>());\\n    const cancel = Atom.fnSync<\\\"cancel\\\">()((_, get) => {\\n      get.set(attempt, Option.none());\\n      get.set(calculation, Atom.Interrupt);\\n      get.set(showCalculation, false);\\n    });\\n    const edit = Atom.fnSync<WebsiteCalculatorForm>()((value, get) => {\\n      get.set(attempt, Option.none());\\n      get.set(calculation, Atom.Interrupt);\\n      get.set(showCalculation, false);\\n      get.set(showSaved, false);\\n      get.set(formError, Option.none());\\n      get.set(form, value);\\n    });\\n    const submit = Atom.fnSync<\\\"calculate\\\">()((_, get) => {\\n      const current = get(form);\\n      const request = Result.gen(function* () {\\n        if (calculatorId === \\\"au.income-tax.annual\\\") {\\n          return yield* \\\"taxableDollars\\\" in current\\n            ? annualTaxRequestFromForm(current)\\n            : Result.fail(\\n                new WebsiteInputError({\\n                  message: \\\"Enter a valid annual taxable income.\\\",\\n                })\\n              );\\n        }\\n        return yield* \\\"grossDollars\\\" in current\\n          ? takeHomeRequestFromForm(\\n              current,\\n              AuPayCalculatorId.make(calculatorId)\\n            )\\n          : Result.fail(\\n              new WebsiteInputError({\\n                message: \\\"Enter a valid pay amount and pay period.\\\",\\n              })\\n            );\\n      });\\n      get.set(showCalculation, true);\\n      get.set(showSaved, false);\\n      if (Result.isFailure(request)) {\\n        get.set(attempt, Option.none());\\n        get.set(calculation, Atom.Interrupt);\\n        get.set(formError, Option.some(request.failure.message));\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      get.set(formError, Option.none());\\n      get.set(attempt, Option.some(request.success));\\n      get.set(calculation, request.success);\\n    });\\n    const group = {\\n      attempt,\\n      calculation,\\n      cancel,\\n      edit,\\n      form,\\n      formError,\\n      savedMessage,\\n      savedReport,\\n      showCalculation,\\n      showSaved,\\n      submit,\\n      // The registry retains this in-memory page snapshot across an uncommitted\\n      // React render. Otherwise idle cleanup can erase once-seeded SSR values\\n      // before hydration subscribes. Page cleanup still interrupts live work.\\n      // The retained view also holds its whole weak-family description group.\\n      // Otherwise browser GC can replace that group on a return visit while the\\n      // old values remain in the registry. The callback runs after group creation.\\n      // Disposing the root registry releases the snapshot and its client.\\n      view: Atom.make((get): WebsiteCalculatorViewState => {\\n        const current = get(calculation);\\n        const submitted = get(showCalculation);\\n        const saved = get(showSaved);\\n        const inputError = get(formError);\\n        const report = AsyncResult.value(current).pipe(\\n          Option.filter(\\n            (value) => value.calculator.calculatorId === calculatorId\\n          ),\\n          Option.map((value) => value.report),\\n          Option.orElse(() => get(savedReport)),\\n          Option.filter((value) =>\\n            Match.value(calculatorId).pipe(\\n              Match.when(\\\"au.income-tax.annual\\\", () =>\\n                Schema.is(AnnualTaxReport)(value)\\n              ),\\n              Match.when(\\\"au.pay.take-home\\\", () =>\\n                Schema.is(TakeHomePayReport)(value)\\n              ),\\n              Match.orElse(() => Schema.is(PayWithholdingsLedger)(value))\\n            )\\n          )\\n        );\\n        const message = Option.match(inputError, {\\n          onNone: () => {\\n            if (\\n              submitted &&\\n              !current.waiting &&\\n              (AsyncResult.isFailure(current) ||\\n                (AsyncResult.isSuccess(current) && Option.isNone(report)))\\n            ) {\\n              if (AsyncResult.isFailure(current)) {\\n                return current.cause.pipe(\\n                  Cause.findErrorOption,\\n                  Option.map(calculationFailureMessage)\\n                );\\n              }\\n              return Option.some(\\n                \\\"The calculation could not finish. Please try again.\\\"\\n              );\\n            }\\n            return saved ? get(savedMessage) : Option.none<string>();\\n          },\\n          onSome: Option.some,\\n        });\\n        return {\\n          busy: submitted && current.waiting,\\n          calculatorId,\\n          form: get(group.form),\\n          message,\\n          report,\\n          stale:\\n            Option.isSome(report) &&\\n            !saved &&\\n            (!submitted ||\\n              current.waiting ||\\n              !AsyncResult.isSuccess(current) ||\\n              Option.isSome(inputError)),\\n        };\\n      }).pipe(Atom.keepAlive),\\n    } as const;\\n    return group;\\n  }\\n);\\n\\n// Home uses the same page commands and state owner as the other calculators.\\n// These existing names retain their narrow React/test call sites.\\nconst home = calculatorPageAtoms(AuPayCalculatorId.make(\\\"au.pay.take-home\\\"));\\nexport const calculateAtom: Atom.AtomResultFn<\\n  CalculatorRunServiceRequest,\\n  CalculatorRunResponse,\\n  CalculatorRpcClientError | TaxKitWebConfigError\\n> = home.calculation;\\nexport const takeHomeFormAtom = Atom.writable(\\n  (get) => {\\n    const form = get(home.form);\\n    return Schema.is(TakeHomeForm)(form) ? form : initialTakeHomeForm;\\n  },\\n  (get, form: TakeHomeForm) => get.set(home.form, form)\\n);\\nexport const submitTakeHomeAtom = home.submit;\\nexport const editTakeHomeAtom = Atom.fnSync<TakeHomeForm>()((value, get) =>\\n  get.set(home.edit, value)\\n);\\nimport { Config, Effect, Match, Schema } from \\\"effect\\\";\\n\\nimport { AnalyticsConfigurationError } from \\\"./errors.js\\\";\\nimport type { AnalyticsSettings } from \\\"./schemas.js\\\";\\nimport { AnalyticsDisabled, AnalyticsEnabled } from \\\"./schemas.js\\\";\\n\\n// Off is a deliberate mode. Missing or malformed enabled settings have a\\n// separate failure; no token is acquired by the disabled branch.\\nexport const AnalyticsSettingsConfig: Effect.Effect<\\n  AnalyticsSettings,\\n  AnalyticsConfigurationError\\n> = Config.schema(\\n  Schema.Literals([\\\"off\\\", \\\"production\\\", \\\"controlled-preview\\\"]),\\n  \\\"POSTHOG_COLLECTION_MODE\\\"\\n).pipe(\\n  Config.withDefault(\\\"off\\\"),\\n  Effect.flatMap((mode) =>\\n    Match.value(mode).pipe(\\n      Match.when(\\\"off\\\", () => Effect.succeed(AnalyticsDisabled.make({}))),\\n      Match.orElse((environment) =>\\n        Effect.all({\\n          projectId: Config.schema(\\n            AnalyticsEnabled.fields.projectId,\\n            \\\"POSTHOG_PROJECT_ID\\\"\\n          ),\\n          region: Config.schema(\\n            AnalyticsEnabled.fields.region,\\n            \\\"POSTHOG_REGION\\\"\\n          ),\\n          stage: Config.schema(AnalyticsEnabled.fields.stage, \\\"POSTHOG_STAGE\\\"),\\n          token: Config.schema(\\n            AnalyticsEnabled.fields.token,\\n            \\\"POSTHOG_CAPTURE_TOKEN\\\"\\n          ),\\n        }).pipe(\\n          Effect.flatMap((settings) =>\\n            AnalyticsEnabled.makeEffect({\\n              environment,\\n              ...settings,\\n            })\\n          )\\n        )\\n      )\\n    )\\n  ),\\n  Effect.mapError(\\n    () => new AnalyticsConfigurationError({ operation: \\\"configure\\\" })\\n  )\\n);\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"goal\":{\"threadId\":\"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159\",\"objective\":\"Continue the approved TaxKit clean-slate work in crcorbett/taxkit: finish DEV-73 strict enforcement and host checks, then implement DEV-74–81 in the accepted order through tested commits, pushes and reviewable draft PRs. Preserve retained tax results pending Cooper's Medicare scope decision; do not merge, deploy, publish or apply provider changes.\",\"status\":\"active\",\"tokensUsed\":32060800,\"timeUsedSeconds\":218576,\"createdAt\":1791091582,\"updatedAt\":1791372554},\"remainingTokens\":null,\"completionBudgetReport\":null}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","create_time":1791372554.593658}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
