{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T11:29:51.414Z","ordinal":69409,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-e48aaaaa-c87a-4bd7-8d2d-638307d49605","process_id":"67286","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 - <<'PY'\ns=open('/private/tmp/dev78-handover-qualify.py').read().replace('dev78-handover-freeze-b','dev79-backend-freeze-a').replace('dev78-handover-whole-b','dev79-backend-whole-a').replace('dev78-handover-local-qualification','dev79-backend-local-qualification').replace(\"assert len(checks)==1 and checks[0]['exitCode']==0\",\"assert [c['stage'] for c in checks]==['tests','build','verification'] and all(c['exitCode']==0 for c in checks)\")\ns=s.replace(\"'durationSeconds':checks[0]['durationSeconds']\",\"'durationSeconds':{c['stage']:c['durationSeconds'] for c in checks}\")\nopen('/private/tmp/dev79-backend-qualify.py','w').write(s)\nPY\nsed -n '1,100p' .agents/skills/effect-client-wrapper/references/posthog-browser.md; rg -n 'capture_|disable_|log|metric|queue' /private/tmp/dev79-analytics-package-reference/posthog-js/package/lib/src/config.js; cat packages/analytics/package.json"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 - <<'PY'\ns=open('/private/tmp/dev78-handover-qualify.py').read().replace('dev78-handover-freeze-b','dev79-backend-freeze-a').replace('dev78-handover-whole-b','dev79-backend-whole-a').replace('dev78-handover-local-qualification','dev79-backend-local-qualification').replace(\"assert len(checks)==1 and checks[0]['exitCode']==0\",\"assert [c['stage'] for c in checks]==['tests','build','verification'] and all(c['exitCode']==0 for c in checks)\")\ns=s.replace(\"'durationSeconds':checks[0]['durationSeconds']\",\"'durationSeconds':{c['stage']:c['durationSeconds'] for c in checks}\")\nopen('/private/tmp/dev79-backend-qualify.py','w').write(s)\nPY\nsed -n '1,100p' .agents/skills/effect-client-wrapper/references/posthog-browser.md; rg -n 'capture_|disable_|log|metric|queue' /private/tmp/dev79-analytics-package-reference/posthog-js/package/lib/src/config.js; cat packages/analytics/package.json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"# A PostHog browser client owned by Effect\n\nUse this for a PostHog client in a React/TanStack application with an Effect\nAtom runtime. It complements the\n[app and proxy layout](../../alchemy-iac/references/effect/posthog-analytics.md)\nand [Alchemy provider guide](../../alchemy-iac/references/providers/posthog.md).\nInspect the installed SDK and Effect APIs; this describes a qualified pattern,\nnot a version-independent implementation to paste. Apply the sibling\n[strict Effect policy](../../strict-effect-ts/SKILL.md), including its named\noperations, closed requirements, typed errors and narrow host exceptions.\n\n## Contents\n\n- [Keep the public service semantic](#keep-the-public-service-semantic)\n- [Acquire, initialise and close the SDK in the Layer](#acquire-initialise-and-close-the-sdk-in-the-layer)\n- [Make collection choices explicit](#make-collection-choices-explicit)\n- [Respect the selected privacy controls](#respect-the-selected-privacy-controls)\n- [Check the real client](#check-the-real-client)\n\n## Keep the public service semantic\n\nExpose checked operations such as `recordPageView(PageView)` and\n`recordNavigation(NavigationUse)`, with closed typed errors and no environment\nrequirements escaping callers. Put event Schemas and the service in the shared\nanalytics owner. Keep the SDK instance, wire acknowledgements and browser access\ninside the app's private `browser.adapter.layer.ts`. Never expose a raw client,\ngeneric `capture(string, object)`, `use` callback or arbitrary properties.\n\nExtend the existing React-mounted Atom runtime. Atom is the owner of service\nlifetime and effectful actions, not a second wrapper around every SDK method.\nReact calls the service through the established Atom action boundary. Routes\nchoose event semantics; components can receive action callbacks. Do not create\na second runtime, mutable module singleton or per-click Promise runner.\nKeep browser imports in the framework's matching client environment function.\n\n## Acquire, initialise and close the SDK in the Layer\n\nDecode enabled/disabled settings, stage and Website origin before construction.\nDisabled collection returns a working no-op service and should not load the SDK.\nKeep configured-off, policy-blocked and unavailable distinct. Malformed enabled\nsettings produce a named configuration failure; any safe downgrade belongs to\nan explicit composition policy with a fixed diagnostic. Do not silently turn\nall decode or acquisition errors into an indistinguishable disabled state.\nConstruct the browser SDK once in the scoped Layer and register cleanup before\ninitialisation can partly fail. Adapt synchronous SDK and browser operations\nwith `Effect.try`; confine import/shutdown Promise bridges to this exact adapter\nwith `Effect.tryPromise`. Native Effect operations need no Promise conversion.\nKeep `this` bound when calling instance methods.\n\nApply a total acquisition deadline and bounded cleanup. Supply the Effect\ncancellation signal when the SDK operation supports it. A dynamic import itself\ncannot be aborted; a late module result must not initialise a client after its\nscope closes. Keep construction inside the interruptible Effect continuation,\nnot a detached Promise callback. Cleanup also covers partial initialisation and\nmust not swallow defects or interruption while handling named shutdown failures.\nState the limits of any SDK operation that cannot be cancelled. The cleanup\nbudget must include waiting for a capture permit and acquiring ownership of the\nclient, not only the SDK shutdown call. Test close while a capture is stalled:\nclose must finish within its budget, old handles must stay closed, and a later\ncapture completion must not send or restore the client. Choose and test an\nexplicit cancellation/drop policy if capture work can outlive its Layer scope;\na timeout that leaves a usable instance behind is not bounded cleanup.\n\nUse `Ref<Option<Client>>` for scoped state, `Option.match` for presence and\n`Semaphore` only where acknowledgement/state updates need serial access.\nUse named `Effect.fn` for public operations and `Effect.fnUntraced` for private\nhelpers without a separate span. Do not manually branch on `Option._tag`,\nread `.value`, assert a client exists or use ternaries to unwrap optional settings.\nCoordinate capture, acknowledgement updates and close so competing calls cannot\nuse an instance that has been released. Match the configured mode exhaustively;\ndo not turn a future mode into a silent default.\n\nDecode the SDK's capture acknowledgement with its owning Schema. It reports\nclient acceptance, not provider storage. Mark a page as sent only after the\nclient accepted it. Guard repeated effects, remounts and competing calls without\nsuppressing a later real navigation back to the same page.\n\n## Make collection choices explicit\n\nFor selected events, disable SDK automatic page views and automatic clicks, then\nrecord page views and chosen actions from their semantic owners. A custom event\ncan still be blocked by an analytics-domain rule when autocapture is disabled.\nTurning off autocapture is not the same as disabling the SDK or changing its\ndelivery address.\n\nInspect every enabled SDK feature and its network paths. A minimal profile may\ndisable replay, page-leave/performance/error capture, heatmaps, surveys, tours,\nfeature-flag requests and external dependency loading. These are product choices,\nnot an instruction to disable features a user needs. Qualify actual option names\nand defaults for the pinned SDK. Keep the UI host on the matching PostHog region\neven when the ingestion host becomes a Website path.\n\nAgree identity and persistence. An anonymous visitor ID can support repeat\nvisits without creating person profiles. Keep backend request identities separate\nunless the product explicitly needs and approves linking them. Check an owned\nproperty allowlist: short page/action names, stage, bounded campaign names and\nreferrer host can be useful; complete URLs, queries, bodies, cookies, auth headers,\nemails and raw errors usually are not needed for these measures.\n\nThe SDK's synchronous `before_send` callback must remain synchronous. Confine it\n{\n  \"name\": \"@taxkit/analytics\",\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"exports\": {\n    \"./schemas\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/schemas.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/schemas.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/schemas.js\"\n    },\n    \"./errors\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/errors.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/errors.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/errors.js\"\n    },\n    \"./service\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/service.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/service.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/service.js\"\n    },\n    \"./live\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/live.layer.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/live.layer.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/live.layer.js\"\n    },\n    \"./test\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/test.layer.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/test.layer.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/test.layer.js\"\n    },\n    \"./testing/fixtures\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/__testing__/fixtures.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/__testing__/fixtures.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/__testing__/fixtures.js\"\n    },\n    \"./testing/observations\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/__testing__/observations.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/__testing__/observations.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/__testing__/observations.js\"\n    },\n    \"./config\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/config.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/config.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/config.js\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"publishConfig\": {\n    \"exports\": {\n      \"./schemas\": {\n        \"types\": \"./dist/schemas.d.ts\",\n        \"default\": \"./dist/schemas.js\"\n      },\n      \"./errors\": {\n        \"types\": \"./dist/errors.d.ts\",\n        \"default\": \"./dist/errors.js\"\n      },\n      \"./service\": {\n        \"types\": \"./dist/service.d.ts\",\n        \"default\": \"./dist/service.js\"\n      },\n      \"./live\": {\n        \"types\": \"./dist/live.layer.d.ts\",\n        \"default\": \"./dist/live.layer.js\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"rm -rf dist && tsc -p tsconfig.build.json\",\n    \"check-types\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n    \"test\": \"bun --bun vitest run\",\n    \"clean\": \"rm -rf dist .turbo *.tsbuildinfo\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@taxkit/calculators\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@taxkit/content\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"effect\": \"catalog:\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@effect/vitest\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"typescript\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"vite\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"vitest\": \"catalog:\"\n  }\n}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"# A PostHog browser client owned by Effect\n\nUse this for a PostHog client in a React/TanStack application with an Effect\nAtom runtime. It complements the\n[app and proxy layout](../../alchemy-iac/references/effect/posthog-analytics.md)\nand [Alchemy provider guide](../../alchemy-iac/references/providers/posthog.md).\nInspect the installed SDK and Effect APIs; this describes a qualified pattern,\nnot a version-independent implementation to paste. Apply the sibling\n[strict Effect policy](../../strict-effect-ts/SKILL.md), including its named\noperations, closed requirements, typed errors and narrow host exceptions.\n\n## Contents\n\n- [Keep the public service semantic](#keep-the-public-service-semantic)\n- [Acquire, initialise and close the SDK in the Layer](#acquire-initialise-and-close-the-sdk-in-the-layer)\n- [Make collection choices explicit](#make-collection-choices-explicit)\n- [Respect the selected privacy controls](#respect-the-selected-privacy-controls)\n- [Check the real client](#check-the-real-client)\n\n## Keep the public service semantic\n\nExpose checked operations such as `recordPageView(PageView)` and\n`recordNavigation(NavigationUse)`, with closed typed errors and no environment\nrequirements escaping callers. Put event Schemas and the service in the shared\nanalytics owner. Keep the SDK instance, wire acknowledgements and browser access\ninside the app's private `browser.adapter.layer.ts`. Never expose a raw client,\ngeneric `capture(string, object)`, `use` callback or arbitrary properties.\n\nExtend the existing React-mounted Atom runtime. Atom is the owner of service\nlifetime and effectful actions, not a second wrapper around every SDK method.\nReact calls the service through the established Atom action boundary. Routes\nchoose event semantics; components can receive action callbacks. Do not create\na second runtime, mutable module singleton or per-click Promise runner.\nKeep browser imports in the framework's matching client environment function.\n\n## Acquire, initialise and close the SDK in the Layer\n\nDecode enabled/disabled settings, stage and Website origin before construction.\nDisabled collection returns a working no-op service and should not load the SDK.\nKeep configured-off, policy-blocked and unavailable distinct. Malformed enabled\nsettings produce a named configuration failure; any safe downgrade belongs to\nan explicit composition policy with a fixed diagnostic. Do not silently turn\nall decode or acquisition errors into an indistinguishable disabled state.\nConstruct the browser SDK once in the scoped Layer and register cleanup before\ninitialisation can partly fail. Adapt synchronous SDK and browser operations\nwith `Effect.try`; confine import/shutdown Promise bridges to this exact adapter\nwith `Effect.tryPromise`. Native Effect operations need no Promise conversion.\nKeep `this` bound when calling instance methods.\n\nApply a total acquisition deadline and bounded cleanup. Supply the Effect\ncancellation signal when the SDK operation supports it. A dynamic import itself\ncannot be aborted; a late module result must not initialise a client after its\nscope closes. Keep construction inside the interruptible Effect continuation,\nnot a detached Promise callback. Cleanup also covers partial initialisation and\nmust not swallow defects or interruption while handling named shutdown failures.\nState the limits of any SDK operation that cannot be cancelled. The cleanup\nbudget must include waiting for a capture permit and acquiring ownership of the\nclient, not only the SDK shutdown call. Test close while a capture is stalled:\nclose must finish within its budget, old handles must stay closed, and a later\ncapture completion must not send or restore the client. Choose and test an\nexplicit cancellation/drop policy if capture work can outlive its Layer scope;\na timeout that leaves a usable instance behind is not bounded cleanup.\n\nUse `Ref<Option<Client>>` for scoped state, `Option.match` for presence and\n`Semaphore` only where acknowledgement/state updates need serial access.\nUse named `Effect.fn` for public operations and `Effect.fnUntraced` for private\nhelpers without a separate span. Do not manually branch on `Option._tag`,\nread `.value`, assert a client exists or use ternaries to unwrap optional settings.\nCoordinate capture, acknowledgement updates and close so competing calls cannot\nuse an instance that has been released. Match the configured mode exhaustively;\ndo not turn a future mode into a silent default.\n\nDecode the SDK's capture acknowledgement with its owning Schema. It reports\nclient acceptance, not provider storage. Mark a page as sent only after the\nclient accepted it. Guard repeated effects, remounts and competing calls without\nsuppressing a later real navigation back to the same page.\n\n## Make collection choices explicit\n\nFor selected events, disable SDK automatic page views and automatic clicks, then\nrecord page views and chosen actions from their semantic owners. A custom event\ncan still be blocked by an analytics-domain rule when autocapture is disabled.\nTurning off autocapture is not the same as disabling the SDK or changing its\ndelivery address.\n\nInspect every enabled SDK feature and its network paths. A minimal profile may\ndisable replay, page-leave/performance/error capture, heatmaps, surveys, tours,\nfeature-flag requests and external dependency loading. These are product choices,\nnot an instruction to disable features a user needs. Qualify actual option names\nand defaults for the pinned SDK. Keep the UI host on the matching PostHog region\neven when the ingestion host becomes a Website path.\n\nAgree identity and persistence. An anonymous visitor ID can support repeat\nvisits without creating person profiles. Keep backend request identities separate\nunless the product explicitly needs and approves linking them. Check an owned\nproperty allowlist: short page/action names, stage, bounded campaign names and\nreferrer host can be useful; complete URLs, queries, bodies, cookies, auth headers,\nemails and raw errors usually are not needed for these measures.\n\nThe SDK's synchronous `before_send` callback must remain synchronous. Confine it\n{\n  \"name\": \"@taxkit/analytics\",\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"exports\": {\n    \"./schemas\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/schemas.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/schemas.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/schemas.js\"\n    },\n    \"./errors\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/errors.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/errors.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/errors.js\"\n    },\n    \"./service\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/service.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/service.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/service.js\"\n    },\n    \"./live\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/live.layer.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/live.layer.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/live.layer.js\"\n    },\n    \"./test\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/test.layer.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/test.layer.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/test.layer.js\"\n    },\n    \"./testing/fixtures\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/__testing__/fixtures.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/__testing__/fixtures.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/__testing__/fixtures.js\"\n    },\n    \"./testing/observations\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/__testing__/observations.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/__testing__/observations.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/__testing__/observations.js\"\n    },\n    \"./config\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/config.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/config.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/config.js\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"publishConfig\": {\n    \"exports\": {\n      \"./schemas\": {\n        \"types\": \"./dist/schemas.d.ts\",\n        \"default\": \"./dist/schemas.js\"\n      },\n      \"./errors\": {\n        \"types\": \"./dist/errors.d.ts\",\n        \"default\": \"./dist/errors.js\"\n      },\n      \"./service\": {\n        \"types\": \"./dist/service.d.ts\",\n        \"default\": \"./dist/service.js\"\n      },\n      \"./live\": {\n        \"types\": \"./dist/live.layer.d.ts\",\n        \"default\": \"./dist/live.layer.js\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"rm -rf dist && tsc -p tsconfig.build.json\",\n    \"check-types\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n    \"test\": \"bun --bun vitest run\",\n    \"clean\": \"rm -rf dist .turbo *.tsbuildinfo\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@taxkit/calculators\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@taxkit/content\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"effect\": \"catalog:\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@effect/vitest\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"typescript\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"vite\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"vitest\": \"catalog:\"\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7416},"formatted_output":"# A PostHog browser client owned by Effect\n\nUse this for a PostHog client in a React/TanStack application with an Effect\nAtom runtime. It complements the\n[app and proxy layout](../../alchemy-iac/references/effect/posthog-analytics.md)\nand [Alchemy provider guide](../../alchemy-iac/references/providers/posthog.md).\nInspect the installed SDK and Effect APIs; this describes a qualified pattern,\nnot a version-independent implementation to paste. Apply the sibling\n[strict Effect policy](../../strict-effect-ts/SKILL.md), including its named\noperations, closed requirements, typed errors and narrow host exceptions.\n\n## Contents\n\n- [Keep the public service semantic](#keep-the-public-service-semantic)\n- [Acquire, initialise and close the SDK in the Layer](#acquire-initialise-and-close-the-sdk-in-the-layer)\n- [Make collection choices explicit](#make-collection-choices-explicit)\n- [Respect the selected privacy controls](#respect-the-selected-privacy-controls)\n- [Check the real client](#check-the-real-client)\n\n## Keep the public service semantic\n\nExpose checked operations such as `recordPageView(PageView)` and\n`recordNavigation(NavigationUse)`, with closed typed errors and no environment\nrequirements escaping callers. Put event Schemas and the service in the shared\nanalytics owner. Keep the SDK instance, wire acknowledgements and browser access\ninside the app's private `browser.adapter.layer.ts`. Never expose a raw client,\ngeneric `capture(string, object)`, `use` callback or arbitrary properties.\n\nExtend the existing React-mounted Atom runtime. Atom is the owner of service\nlifetime and effectful actions, not a second wrapper around every SDK method.\nReact calls the service through the established Atom action boundary. Routes\nchoose event semantics; components can receive action callbacks. Do not create\na second runtime, mutable module singleton or per-click Promise runner.\nKeep browser imports in the framework's matching client environment function.\n\n## Acquire, initialise and close the SDK in the Layer\n\nDecode enabled/disabled settings, stage and Website origin before construction.\nDisabled collection returns a working no-op service and should not load the SDK.\nKeep configured-off, policy-blocked and unavailable distinct. Malformed enabled\nsettings produce a named configuration failure; any safe downgrade belongs to\nan explicit composition policy with a fixed diagnostic. Do not silently turn\nall decode or acquisition errors into an indistinguishable disabled state.\nConstruct the browser SDK once in the scoped Layer and register cleanup before\ninitialisation can partly fail. Adapt synchronous SDK and browser operations\nwith `Effect.try`; confine import/shutdown Promise bridges to this exact adapter\nwith `Effect.tryPromise`. Native Effect operations need no Promise conversion.\nKeep `this` bound when calling instance methods.\n\nApply a total acquisition deadline and bounded cleanup. Supply the Effect\ncancellation signal when the SDK operation supports it. A dynamic import itself\ncannot be aborted; a late module result must not initialise a client after its\nscope closes. Keep construction inside the interruptible Effect continuation,\nnot a detached Promise callback. Cleanup also covers partial initialisation and\nmust not swallow defects or interruption while handling named shutdown failures.\nState the limits of any SDK operation that cannot be cancelled. The cleanup\nbudget must include waiting for a capture permit and acquiring ownership of the\nclient, not only the SDK shutdown call. Test close while a capture is stalled:\nclose must finish within its budget, old handles must stay closed, and a later\ncapture completion must not send or restore the client. Choose and test an\nexplicit cancellation/drop policy if capture work can outlive its Layer scope;\na timeout that leaves a usable instance behind is not bounded cleanup.\n\nUse `Ref<Option<Client>>` for scoped state, `Option.match` for presence and\n`Semaphore` only where acknowledgement/state updates need serial access.\nUse named `Effect.fn` for public operations and `Effect.fnUntraced` for private\nhelpers without a separate span. Do not manually branch on `Option._tag`,\nread `.value`, assert a client exists or use ternaries to unwrap optional settings.\nCoordinate capture, acknowledgement updates and close so competing calls cannot\nuse an instance that has been released. Match the configured mode exhaustively;\ndo not turn a future mode into a silent default.\n\nDecode the SDK's capture acknowledgement with its owning Schema. It reports\nclient acceptance, not provider storage. Mark a page as sent only after the\nclient accepted it. Guard repeated effects, remounts and competing calls without\nsuppressing a later real navigation back to the same page.\n\n## Make collection choices explicit\n\nFor selected events, disable SDK automatic page views and automatic clicks, then\nrecord page views and chosen actions from their semantic owners. A custom event\ncan still be blocked by an analytics-domain rule when autocapture is disabled.\nTurning off autocapture is not the same as disabling the SDK or changing its\ndelivery address.\n\nInspect every enabled SDK feature and its network paths. A minimal profile may\ndisable replay, page-leave/performance/error capture, heatmaps, surveys, tours,\nfeature-flag requests and external dependency loading. These are product choices,\nnot an instruction to disable features a user needs. Qualify actual option names\nand defaults for the pinned SDK. Keep the UI host on the matching PostHog region\neven when the ingestion host becomes a Website path.\n\nAgree identity and persistence. An anonymous visitor ID can support repeat\nvisits without creating person profiles. Keep backend request identities separate\nunless the product explicitly needs and approves linking them. Check an owned\nproperty allowlist: short page/action names, stage, bounded campaign names and\nreferrer host can be useful; complete URLs, queries, bodies, cookies, auth headers,\nemails and raw errors usually are not needed for these measures.\n\nThe SDK's synchronous `before_send` callback must remain synchronous. Confine it\n{\n  \"name\": \"@taxkit/analytics\",\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"exports\": {\n    \"./schemas\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/schemas.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/schemas.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/schemas.js\"\n    },\n    \"./errors\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/errors.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/errors.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/errors.js\"\n    },\n    \"./service\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/service.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/service.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/service.js\"\n    },\n    \"./live\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/live.layer.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/live.layer.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/live.layer.js\"\n    },\n    \"./test\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/test.layer.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/test.layer.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/test.layer.js\"\n    },\n    \"./testing/fixtures\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/__testing__/fixtures.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/__testing__/fixtures.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/__testing__/fixtures.js\"\n    },\n    \"./testing/observations\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/__testing__/observations.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/__testing__/observations.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/__testing__/observations.js\"\n    },\n    \"./config\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/config.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./dist/config.d.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/config.js\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"publishConfig\": {\n    \"exports\": {\n      \"./schemas\": {\n        \"types\": \"./dist/schemas.d.ts\",\n        \"default\": \"./dist/schemas.js\"\n      },\n      \"./errors\": {\n        \"types\": \"./dist/errors.d.ts\",\n        \"default\": \"./dist/errors.js\"\n      },\n      \"./service\": {\n        \"types\": \"./dist/service.d.ts\",\n        \"default\": \"./dist/service.js\"\n      },\n      \"./live\": {\n        \"types\": \"./dist/live.layer.d.ts\",\n        \"default\": \"./dist/live.layer.js\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"rm -rf dist && tsc -p tsconfig.build.json\",\n    \"check-types\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n    \"test\": \"bun --bun vitest run\",\n    \"clean\": \"rm -rf dist .turbo *.tsbuildinfo\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@taxkit/calculators\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"@taxkit/content\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"effect\": \"catalog:\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@effect/vitest\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"typescript\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"vite\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"vitest\": \"catalog:\"\n  }\n}\n"},"started_at_ms":1791372591414,"completed_at_ms":1791372591414}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T11:29:51.571Z","ordinal":69410,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a11620-81d2-72e3-9242-22f57e19a7a5","call_id":"call_bd3911d67ced4f649ef7cd3be63b641f","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"de77cb\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007416,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2105,\"output\":\"# A PostHog browser client owned by Effect\\n\\nUse this for a PostHog client in a React/TanStack application with an Effect\\nAtom runtime. It complements the\\n[app and proxy layout](../../alchemy-iac/references/effect/posthog-analytics.md)\\nand [Alchemy provider guide](../../alchemy-iac/references/providers/posthog.md).\\nInspect the installed SDK and Effect APIs; this describes a qualified pattern,\\nnot a version-independent implementation to paste. Apply the sibling\\n[strict Effect policy](../../strict-effect-ts/SKILL.md), including its named\\noperations, closed requirements, typed errors and narrow host exceptions.\\n\\n## Contents\\n\\n- [Keep the public service semantic](#keep-the-public-service-semantic)\\n- [Acquire, initialise and close the SDK in the Layer](#acquire-initialise-and-close-the-sdk-in-the-layer)\\n- [Make collection choices explicit](#make-collection-choices-explicit)\\n- [Respect the selected privacy controls](#respect-the-selected-privacy-controls)\\n- [Check the real client](#check-the-real-client)\\n\\n## Keep the public service semantic\\n\\nExpose checked operations such as `recordPageView(PageView)` and\\n`recordNavigation(NavigationUse)`, with closed typed errors and no environment\\nrequirements escaping callers. Put event Schemas and the service in the shared\\nanalytics owner. Keep the SDK instance, wire acknowledgements and browser access\\ninside the app's private `browser.adapter.layer.ts`. Never expose a raw client,\\ngeneric `capture(string, object)`, `use` callback or arbitrary properties.\\n\\nExtend the existing React-mounted Atom runtime. Atom is the owner of service\\nlifetime and effectful actions, not a second wrapper around every SDK method.\\nReact calls the service through the established Atom action boundary. Routes\\nchoose event semantics; components can receive action callbacks. Do not create\\na second runtime, mutable module singleton or per-click Promise runner.\\nKeep browser imports in the framework's matching client environment function.\\n\\n## Acquire, initialise and close the SDK in the Layer\\n\\nDecode enabled/disabled settings, stage and Website origin before construction.\\nDisabled collection returns a working no-op service and should not load the SDK.\\nKeep configured-off, policy-blocked and unavailable distinct. Malformed enabled\\nsettings produce a named configuration failure; any safe downgrade belongs to\\nan explicit composition policy with a fixed diagnostic. Do not silently turn\\nall decode or acquisition errors into an indistinguishable disabled state.\\nConstruct the browser SDK once in the scoped Layer and register cleanup before\\ninitialisation can partly fail. Adapt synchronous SDK and browser operations\\nwith `Effect.try`; confine import/shutdown Promise bridges to this exact adapter\\nwith `Effect.tryPromise`. Native Effect operations need no Promise conversion.\\nKeep `this` bound when calling instance methods.\\n\\nApply a total acquisition deadline and bounded cleanup. Supply the Effect\\ncancellation signal when the SDK operation supports it. A dynamic import itself\\ncannot be aborted; a late module result must not initialise a client after its\\nscope closes. Keep construction inside the interruptible Effect continuation,\\nnot a detached Promise callback. Cleanup also covers partial initialisation and\\nmust not swallow defects or interruption while handling named shutdown failures.\\nState the limits of any SDK operation that cannot be cancelled. The cleanup\\nbudget must include waiting for a capture permit and acquiring ownership of the\\nclient, not only the SDK shutdown call. Test close while a capture is stalled:\\nclose must finish within its budget, old handles must stay closed, and a later\\ncapture completion must not send or restore the client. Choose and test an\\nexplicit cancellation/drop policy if capture work can outlive its Layer scope;\\na timeout that leaves a usable instance behind is not bounded cleanup.\\n\\nUse `Ref<Option<Client>>` for scoped state, `Option.match` for presence and\\n`Semaphore` only where acknowledgement/state updates need serial access.\\nUse named `Effect.fn` for public operations and `Effect.fnUntraced` for private\\nhelpers without a separate span. Do not manually branch on `Option._tag`,\\nread `.value`, assert a client exists or use ternaries to unwrap optional settings.\\nCoordinate capture, acknowledgement updates and close so competing calls cannot\\nuse an instance that has been released. Match the configured mode exhaustively;\\ndo not turn a future mode into a silent default.\\n\\nDecode the SDK's capture acknowledgement with its owning Schema. It reports\\nclient acceptance, not provider storage. Mark a page as sent only after the\\nclient accepted it. Guard repeated effects, remounts and competing calls without\\nsuppressing a later real navigation back to the same page.\\n\\n## Make collection choices explicit\\n\\nFor selected events, disable SDK automatic page views and automatic clicks, then\\nrecord page views and chosen actions from their semantic owners. A custom event\\ncan still be blocked by an analytics-domain rule when autocapture is disabled.\\nTurning off autocapture is not the same as disabling the SDK or changing its\\ndelivery address.\\n\\nInspect every enabled SDK feature and its network paths. A minimal profile may\\ndisable replay, page-leave/performance/error capture, heatmaps, surveys, tours,\\nfeature-flag requests and external dependency loading. These are product choices,\\nnot an instruction to disable features a user needs. Qualify actual option names\\nand defaults for the pinned SDK. Keep the UI host on the matching PostHog region\\neven when the ingestion host becomes a Website path.\\n\\nAgree identity and persistence. An anonymous visitor ID can support repeat\\nvisits without creating person profiles. Keep backend request identities separate\\nunless the product explicitly needs and approves linking them. Check an owned\\nproperty allowlist: short page/action names, stage, bounded campaign names and\\nreferrer host can be useful; complete URLs, queries, bodies, cookies, auth headers,\\nemails and raw errors usually are not needed for these measures.\\n\\nThe SDK's synchronous `before_send` callback must remain synchronous. Confine it\\n{\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"@taxkit/analytics\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.1.0\\\",\\n  \\\"private\\\": true,\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"module\\\",\\n  \\\"exports\\\": {\\n    \\\"./schemas\\\": {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"./src/schemas.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"types\\\": \\\"./dist/schemas.d.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"default\\\": \\\"./dist/schemas.js\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"./errors\\\": {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"./src/errors.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"types\\\": \\\"./dist/errors.d.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"default\\\": \\\"./dist/errors.js\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"./service\\\": {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"./src/service.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"types\\\": \\\"./dist/service.d.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"default\\\": \\\"./dist/service.js\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"./live\\\": {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"./src/live.layer.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"types\\\": \\\"./dist/live.layer.d.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"default\\\": \\\"./dist/live.layer.js\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"./test\\\": {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"./src/test.layer.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"types\\\": \\\"./dist/test.layer.d.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"default\\\": \\\"./dist/test.layer.js\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"./testing/fixtures\\\": {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"./src/__testing__/fixtures.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"types\\\": \\\"./dist/__testing__/fixtures.d.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"default\\\": \\\"./dist/__testing__/fixtures.js\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"./testing/observations\\\": {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"./src/__testing__/observations.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"types\\\": \\\"./dist/__testing__/observations.d.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"default\\\": \\\"./dist/__testing__/observations.js\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"./config\\\": {\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"./src/config.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"types\\\": \\\"./dist/config.d.ts\\\",\\n      \\\"default\\\": \\\"./dist/config.js\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"publishConfig\\\": {\\n    \\\"exports\\\": {\\n      \\\"./schemas\\\": {\\n        \\\"types\\\": \\\"./dist/schemas.d.ts\\\",\\n        \\\"default\\\": \\\"./dist/schemas.js\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"./errors\\\": {\\n        \\\"types\\\": \\\"./dist/errors.d.ts\\\",\\n        \\\"default\\\": \\\"./dist/errors.js\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"./service\\\": {\\n        \\\"types\\\": \\\"./dist/service.d.ts\\\",\\n        \\\"default\\\": \\\"./dist/service.js\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"./live\\\": {\\n        \\\"types\\\": \\\"./dist/live.layer.d.ts\\\",\\n        \\\"default\\\": \\\"./dist/live.layer.js\\\"\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"rm -rf dist && tsc -p tsconfig.build.json\\\",\\n    \\\"check-types\\\": \\\"tsc --noEmit\\\",\\n    \\\"test\\\": \\\"bun --bun vitest run\\\",\\n    \\\"clean\\\": \\\"rm -rf dist .turbo *.tsbuildinfo\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"dependencies\\\": {\\n    \\\"@taxkit/calculators\\\": \\\"workspace:*\\\",\\n    \\\"@taxkit/content\\\": \\\"workspace:*\\\",\\n    \\\"effect\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"devDependencies\\\": {\\n    \\\"@effect/vitest\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"typescript\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"vite\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\",\\n    \\\"vitest\\\": \\\"catalog:\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-9