{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T11:38:25.949Z","ordinal":69549,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac62f21f3ec87d0af7aefbd02511069","status":"completed","call_id":"call_35245ca90d0d495db53b5bf0add93a72","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat > /private/tmp/dev79-browser-sender-proposal.md <<'EOF'\\n# TaxKit browser pageview sender proposal\\n\\nCooper's accepted plan uses the latest PostHog browser library. The pinned official\\n1.438.2 archive was tested in Chromium with a synthetic token and controlled local\\nresponses. No real PostHog request or provider change took place.\\n\\nThe library sent one waiting pageview after Do Not Track changed to 1. It also\\nretried an earlier failed pageview after that change. Its public configuration\\nsupports cache options but does not declare an abort signal. The runtime-only\\nsignal experiment blocked sends, but that is not a supported public contract.\\nCalling its opt-out API can write a cookie even with ordinary identity persistence\\ndisabled. Its shutdown flushes queues; it is not a public discard operation.\\n\\nProposed change for approval:\\n\\n- Replace only the browser library requirement with a small TaxKit-owned Effect\\n  pageview sender. Keep the existing private BrowserAnalytics service and the\\n  React Atom registry as its lifetime owner.\\n- Encode exactly the approved event fields. No automatic clicks, profiles,\\n  recordings, storage, enrichment, query strings, referrer details or tax figures.\\n- Use random identity held only in the loaded page's memory, with a distinct\\n  immutable event UUID and timestamp for each accepted navigation.\\n- Check Do Not Track before collecting and immediately before sending. Cancel\\n  pending work on withdrawal or scope close. Do not flush after collection stops.\\n- Send through the fixed same-origin relay, with one complete five-second bound,\\n  one attempt and accepted best-effort loss. Do not add a persistent queue or\\n  promise exact counts or delivery on tab close.\\n- Keep the same planned PostHog Production/shared Preview projects and private\\n  Distilled/Alchemy management. Local and ordinary Preview collection stay off.\\n- Update the earliest SPEC/task/plan and privacy/operations owners, then test the\\n  actual browser and built apps. Do not claim a library lifecycle or compression\\n  qualification for the replacement sender.\\n\\nAlternative: keep the accepted library requirement and leave browser activation\\nunfinished until a supported queue-discard contract is available. Backend,\\nprovider planning and independent work can proceed.\\n\\nControlled evidence: /private/tmp/dev79-sdk-policy-probe-e.json\\nSHA-256: 90ad14f945baaee30a77570dbdbffcd1a42373d792fded058288fd14f93dc81f\\nThe earlier signal probe is experimental evidence only, not a shipping approach.\\nEOF\\nchmod 600 /private/tmp/dev79-browser-sender-proposal.md\",\"max_output_tokens\":1000}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","create_time":1791373089.9753866}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T11:38:26.016Z","ordinal":69550,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-04473706-ce59-4eef-91d8-abfd976e5419","process_id":"30746","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat > /private/tmp/dev79-browser-sender-proposal.md <<'EOF'\n# TaxKit browser pageview sender proposal\n\nCooper's accepted plan uses the latest PostHog browser library. The pinned official\n1.438.2 archive was tested in Chromium with a synthetic token and controlled local\nresponses. No real PostHog request or provider change took place.\n\nThe library sent one waiting pageview after Do Not Track changed to 1. It also\nretried an earlier failed pageview after that change. Its public configuration\nsupports cache options but does not declare an abort signal. The runtime-only\nsignal experiment blocked sends, but that is not a supported public contract.\nCalling its opt-out API can write a cookie even with ordinary identity persistence\ndisabled. Its shutdown flushes queues; it is not a public discard operation.\n\nProposed change for approval:\n\n- Replace only the browser library requirement with a small TaxKit-owned Effect\n  pageview sender. Keep the existing private BrowserAnalytics service and the\n  React Atom registry as its lifetime owner.\n- Encode exactly the approved event fields. No automatic clicks, profiles,\n  recordings, storage, enrichment, query strings, referrer details or tax figures.\n- Use random identity held only in the loaded page's memory, with a distinct\n  immutable event UUID and timestamp for each accepted navigation.\n- Check Do Not Track before collecting and immediately before sending. Cancel\n  pending work on withdrawal or scope close. Do not flush after collection stops.\n- Send through the fixed same-origin relay, with one complete five-second bound,\n  one attempt and accepted best-effort loss. Do not add a persistent queue or\n  promise exact counts or delivery on tab close.\n- Keep the same planned PostHog Production/shared Preview projects and private\n  Distilled/Alchemy management. Local and ordinary Preview collection stay off.\n- Update the earliest SPEC/task/plan and privacy/operations owners, then test the\n  actual browser and built apps. Do not claim a library lifecycle or compression\n  qualification for the replacement sender.\n\nAlternative: keep the accepted library requirement and leave browser activation\nunfinished until a supported queue-discard contract is available. Backend,\nprovider planning and independent work can proceed.\n\nControlled evidence: /private/tmp/dev79-sdk-policy-probe-e.json\nSHA-256: 90ad14f945baaee30a77570dbdbffcd1a42373d792fded058288fd14f93dc81f\nThe earlier signal probe is experimental evidence only, not a shipping approach.\nEOF\nchmod 600 /private/tmp/dev79-browser-sender-proposal.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"cat > /private/tmp/dev79-browser-sender-proposal.md <<'EOF'\n# TaxKit browser pageview sender proposal\n\nCooper's accepted plan uses the latest PostHog browser library. The pinned official\n1.438.2 archive was tested in Chromium with a synthetic token and controlled local\nresponses. No real PostHog request or provider change took place.\n\nThe library sent one waiting pageview after Do Not Track changed to 1. It also\nretried an earlier failed pageview after that change. Its public configuration\nsupports cache options but does not declare an abort signal. The runtime-only\nsignal experiment blocked sends, but that is not a supported public contract.\nCalling its opt-out API can write a cookie even with ordinary identity persistence\ndisabled. Its shutdown flushes queues; it is not a public discard operation.\n\nProposed change for approval:\n\n- Replace only the browser library requirement with a small TaxKit-owned Effect\n  pageview sender. Keep the existing private BrowserAnalytics service and the\n  React Atom registry as its lifetime owner.\n- Encode exactly the approved event fields. No automatic clicks, profiles,\n  recordings, storage, enrichment, query strings, referrer details or tax figures.\n- Use random identity held only in the loaded page's memory, with a distinct\n  immutable event UUID and timestamp for each accepted navigation.\n- Check Do Not Track before collecting and immediately before sending. Cancel\n  pending work on withdrawal or scope close. Do not flush after collection stops.\n- Send through the fixed same-origin relay, with one complete five-second bound,\n  one attempt and accepted best-effort loss. Do not add a persistent queue or\n  promise exact counts or delivery on tab close.\n- Keep the same planned PostHog Production/shared Preview projects and private\n  Distilled/Alchemy management. Local and ordinary Preview collection stay off.\n- Update the earliest SPEC/task/plan and privacy/operations owners, then test the\n  actual browser and built apps. Do not claim a library lifecycle or compression\n  qualification for the replacement sender.\n\nAlternative: keep the accepted library requirement and leave browser activation\nunfinished until a supported queue-discard contract is available. Backend,\nprovider planning and independent work can proceed.\n\nControlled evidence: /private/tmp/dev79-sdk-policy-probe-e.json\nSHA-256: 90ad14f945baaee30a77570dbdbffcd1a42373d792fded058288fd14f93dc81f\nThe earlier signal probe is experimental evidence only, not a shipping approach.\nEOF\nchmod 600 /private/tmp/dev79-browser-sender-proposal.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":6750},"formatted_output":""},"started_at_ms":1791373106016,"completed_at_ms":1791373106016}}
