{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T11:54:04.248Z","ordinal":69736,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac632da79f887d0bd5d3b94fa489160","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The approved Production token change is already applied and checked. The calculator event code now passes the local checks; I’m putting it into a draft PR and recording what remains unfinished. Browser collection is waiting on the sender choice, and metrics remain deferred."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1791374042488,"completed_at_ms":1791374044248}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T11:54:04.252Z","ordinal":69737,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac632da79f887d0bd5d3b94fa489160","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The approved Production token change is already applied and checked. The calculator event code now passes the local checks; I’m putting it into a draft PR and recording what remains unfinished. Browser collection is waiting on the sender choice, and metrics remain deferred."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","create_time":1791374042.4791281,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac632da79f887d0bd5d3b94fa489160","turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a11636-ac5b-7e61-8a70-6196bc70b763","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":1465}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T11:54:20.623Z","ordinal":69738,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac632dc3a1c87d09c09020c3418995e","status":"completed","call_id":"call_a8f00efac5b04bd9876a7b817ffe7f9d","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"python3 - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\np=Path('/private/tmp/dev79-draft-pr-body.md')\\np.write_text('''Successful hosted calculations now collect only the calculator’s catalogue ID and name. One shared path handles HTTP, RPC and remote MCP requests, so each allowed calculation produces one event. Tax inputs, results, request details and browser identity are excluded.\\n\\nCollection is off by default. Missing analytics keys work while collection is off; invalid enabled settings fail with a safe, named configuration error. Explicit denial, malformed collection headers and Do Not Track leave the calculation response unchanged. Native background delivery makes one attempt with a five-second limit and a 64 KiB reply limit, without forwarding authentication, cookies, IP or trace headers or following redirects.\\n\\nLocal validation passed: root tests and builds on `73f2bc7d8bcdb49446e02e878a3944e7e263e8c8`, followed by full `bun run verification` on `311288c3b12c768af15e1efe4738286b56b5e506` in 680.92 seconds. All 17 built native cases passed, including both supported MCP protocols changing from deny to allow to deny within the same conversation. An initial reload test failure was traced to its import-dependent fixture and fixed without extending its deadline. The receipt retains that failure and the successful rerun. The final two documentation files passed focused checks; all 1,770 other frozen file identities remained unchanged.\\n\\nDEV-79 remains in progress. The browser sender decision, browser relay, Website opt-out forwarding, retained PostHog project definitions, scoped private credentials, stored-event UUID checks and public privacy/operations documentation remain unfinished. Controlled browser tests show the current PostHog library can send waiting or retried events after Do Not Track turns on; the proposed small TaxKit sender requires Cooper’s design decision. Local development and ordinary Preview stay off. No PostHog project, credential, deployment, merge, publication or new metrics work is included here. This private package does not change the published package closure, so no Changeset is required.\\n\\nStacked on draft #163 (`codex/dev-78-native-operation-handover`). Checks ran locally because GitHub Actions credits are exhausted.\\n\\nEvidence: [local qualification receipt](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/blob/bea4539137e14844dff3732691c856a19353f626/docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-analytics-backend-and-request-policy.json).\\n''')\\np.chmod(0o600)\\nPY\",max_output_tokens:1000}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh pr create --draft --base codex/dev-78-native-operation-handover --head codex/dev-79-analytics-policy-and-capture --title 'DEV-79: Add minimal calculator events and per-request opt-out' --body-file /private/tmp/dev79-draft-pr-body.md\",max_output_tokens:1200,yield_time_ms:10000}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","create_time":1791374044.2322235}}}
