{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T12:09:11.347Z","ordinal":70034,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","session_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","root_turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","response_id":"resp_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac6364c773c87d08783bc04362988f9","usage":{"input_tokens":167664,"cached_input_tokens":161280,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":672,"reasoning_output_tokens":453,"total_tokens":168336},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":74400158,"cached_input_tokens":72884096,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":371442,"reasoning_output_tokens":142233,"total_tokens":74771600},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1310910360,"cached_input_tokens":1283907584,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":6509504,"reasoning_output_tokens":2892070,"total_tokens":1317419864}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-07T12:09:20.567Z","ordinal":70035,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a11571-1a58-7282-903b-860cd96057b2","item":{"type":"McpToolCall","id":"exec-91d47354-925d-444d-bf0e-7f15a397e74b","server":"codex_apps","tool":"posthog.exec","arguments":{"command":"call docs-search {\"query\":\"What exact personal API key scopes are required for GET, POST and PATCH /api/organizations/{organization_id}/projects/ and POST /api/projects/{project_id}/query/? How can I inspect the organisation project limit without changing billing?\"}","context":"Prepare a narrow TaxKit PostHog project-management credential proposal. Read-only documentation research; no key creation, project change or billing operation. Organisation and API region are still to be independently verified.","conversation_id":"01a115c6-eb76-7c60-b844-89c2daa3e68a","llm_model":"gpt-6"},"connectorId":"asdk_app_699caef2d680819188727b0ddbb349dd","linkId":"link_6a2e191ad8c88191b46d4bc2f680d113","appName":"PostHog","actionName":"exec","readOnlyHint":false,"status":"completed","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"content: \"Found 6 relevant documentation page(s):\\n\\n# Organizations API Reference - PostHog\\nURL: https://posthog.com/docs/api/organizations\\n\\n# Organizations\\n\\n> For instructions on how to authenticate to use this endpoint, see [API overview](https://posthog.com/docs/api/overview) .\\n> \\n> \\n\\n ### Endpoints\\n\\n|  |  |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/` |\\n| `POST` | `/api/organizations/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:id/` |\\n| `PATCH` | `/api/organizations/:id/` |\\n| `DELETE` | `/api/organizations/:id/` |\\n| `POST` | `/api/organizations/:id/remove_blocked_members_and_enforce_verified_domains/` |\\n| `POST` | `/api/organizations/:id/request_ai_access/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:id/teams/data_freshness/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/features/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/forecast/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/invoices/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/invoices/:invoice_id/content/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/limits/` |\\n\\n [Next page →](https://posthog.com/docs/api/organizations-2) ##  Retrieve\\n\\n #### Required API key scopes\\n\\n `organization:read` \\n\\n---\\n\\n #### Query parameters\\n\\n * limit integer\\n* offset integer\\n\\n---\\n\\n #### Response\\n\\n Show response body   \\n #### Example request\\n\\n `GET`   `/api  /organizations`  cURL  PostHog AI    \\n```\\nexport POSTHOG_PERSONAL_API_KEY=[your personal api key]    curl \\\\        -H \\\"Authorization: Bearer $POSTHOG_PERSONAL_API_KEY\\\" \\\\        <ph_app_host>/api/organizations/\\n```\\n \\n```\\napi_key = \\\"[your personal api key]\\\"    project_id = \\\"[your project id]\\\"    response = requests.get(        \\\"<ph_app_host>/api/organizations/\\\".format(            project_id=project_id        ),        headers={\\\"Authorization\\\": \\\"Bearer {}\\\".format(api_key)},    ).json()\\n```\\n #### Example response\\n\\n ##### Status 200\\n\\n RESPONSE PostHog AI  \\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Organizations - Docs - PostHog\\nURL: https://posthog.com/docs/settings/organizations\\n\\n\\n Organization admins and owners can view all [personal API keys](https://posthog.com/docs/api/personal-api-keys) that have access to their organization or its projects. This includes organization-scoped keys, project-scoped keys, and fully unscoped keys held by any member.\\n\\n Find this under [**Settings** > **Organization** > **Security** > **Personal API key access**](https://app.posthog.com/settings/organization-security#organization-personal-api-keys). For each key, you can see:\\n\\n * **Owner** – the member who created the key\\n* **Masked value** – a display-safe hint (e.g. `phx_***1234` ) to help identify the key\\n* **Scopes** – the API scopes granted (e.g. `insight:read` , or `*` for full access)\\n* **Access scope** – whether the key applies to the whole organization, specific projects, or all projects (unscoped)\\n* **Last used** and **Created** timestamps\\n\\n You can search the table by owner name, email, or scope. Click any of the **Owner** , **Masked value** , **Last used** , or **Created** column headers to sort the table. The table is paginated at 25 rows per page.\\n\\n The secret key value and key label are never exposed.\\n\\n> **Note:** This feature requires a plan that includes organization security settings. Only admins and owners can access this section.\\n> \\n> \\n\\n ###  Member list visibility\\n\\n Organization admins and owners can restrict members from viewing the full list of org members. This is useful if you invite external collaborators into separate projects, like when you set up [embedded analytics](https://posthog.com/tutorials/embedded-analytics).\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Personal API keys - Docs - PostHog\\nURL: https://posthog.com/docs/api/personal-api-keys\\n\\nhttps://posthog.com/docs/api/personal-api-keys\\n\\nPersonal API keys authenticate requests to PostHog's private `GET` , `POST` , `PATCH` , and `DELETE` endpoints. They're the right choice when you're using PostHog from your own scripts, automations, or any integration tied to your own account.\\n\\n> **Building an app that other PostHog users will install or connect to?** Use [OAuth](https://posthog.com/docs/api/oauth) instead so users can grant your app scoped access without sharing their own keys.\\n> \\n> \\n\\n  Personal API keys can enable full access to your account, like logging in with your email and password. You can create multiple, give them different scopes, and each can be invalidated individually. This improves the security of your PostHog account. Personal API keys need to be kept private and shouldn't be used in the frontend.\\n\\n ####  How to obtain a personal API key\\n\\n 1. Go to the [Personal API keys](https://us.posthog.com/settings/user-api-keys) section in your account settings\\n2. Click **+ Create a personal API Key** .\\n3. Give your key a label - this is just for you, usually to describe the key's purpose.\\n4. Choose the scopes for your key. We recommended selecting only the scopes required for the API endpoints you really need. This is a security best practice. You can always modify the scopes later if you need to.\\n5. At the top of the list, you should see your brand new key. **Immediately** copy its value, as you'll **never** see it again after refreshing the page.\\n\\n You can create up to 10 personal API keys. Personal API keys are deleted when a user is deleted.\\n\\n ![How to create an api key]() \\n\\n ####  Rolling and upgrading legacy keys\\n\\n Personal API keys created before February 2024 use legacy PBKDF2 hashing. These keys still work, but use an older, slower hashing method. They display a **Legacy** status tag in the keys table.\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Billing API Reference - PostHog\\nURL: https://posthog.com/docs/api/billing-3\\n\\n# Billing\\n\\n> For instructions on how to authenticate to use this endpoint, see [API overview](https://posthog.com/docs/api/overview) .\\n> \\n> \\n\\n ### Endpoints\\n\\n|  |  |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `GET` | `/api/billing/usage/export/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/billing/usage/team_options/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/alerts/` |\\n| `POST` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/alerts/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/alerts/:id/` |\\n| `PATCH` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/alerts/:id/` |\\n| `DELETE` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/alerts/:id/` |\\n| `POST` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/alerts/:id/check_now/` |\\n| `POST` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/alerts/:id/destinations/` |\\n\\n [← Previous page](https://posthog.com/docs/api/billing-2) [Next page →](https://posthog.com/docs/api/billing-4) ##  Retrieve billing usage export\\n\\n Download the usage breakdown as CSV, honouring the requested project cap.\\n\\n #### Required API key scopes\\n\\n `billing:read` \\n\\n---\\n\\n #### Query parameters\\n\\n * after string | null\\n* breakdowns string | null\\n* end_date string | null\\n* interval string | null\\n* page_size integer | null\\n* start_date string | null\\n* team_ids string | null\\n* top_projects integer | null\\n* usage_types string | null\\n\\n---\\n\\n #### Example request\\n\\n `GET`   `/api  /billing  /usage  /export`  cURL  PostHog AI    \\n```\\nexport POSTHOG_PERSONAL_API_KEY=[your personal api key]    curl \\\\        -H \\\"Authorization: Bearer $POSTHOG_PERSONAL_API_KEY\\\" \\\\        <ph_app_host>/api/billing/usage/export/\\n```\\n \\n```\\napi_key = \\\"[your personal api key]\\\"    project_id = \\\"[your project id]\\\"    response = requests.get(        \\\"<ph_app_host>/api/billing/usage/export/\\\".format(            project_id=project_id        ),        headers={\\\"Authorization\\\": \\\"Bearer {}\\\".format(api_key)},    ).json()\\n```\\n #### Example response\\n\\n ##### Status 200 No response body\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Billing API Reference - PostHog\\nURL: https://posthog.com/docs/api/billing-4\\n\\n# Billing\\n\\n> For instructions on how to authenticate to use this endpoint, see [API overview](https://posthog.com/docs/api/overview) .\\n> \\n> \\n\\n ### Endpoints\\n\\n|  |  |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `POST` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/alerts/:id/destinations/delete/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/alerts/:id/events/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/features/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/forecast/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/invoices/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/invoices/:invoice_id/content/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/limits/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/products/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/products/:product_key/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/products/summary/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/projects/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/spend/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/spend/export/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/spend/timeseries/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/subscription/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/usage/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/usage/export/` |\\n| `GET` | `/api/organizations/:organization_id/billing/usage/status/` |\\n\\n [← Previous page](https://posthog.com/docs/api/billing-3) [Next page →](https://posthog.com/docs/api/billing-5) ##  Create billing alerts destinations delete\\n\\n Delete a notification destination by deleting its HogFunction group atomically.\\n\\n #### Required API key scopes\\n\\n `organization:write` \\n\\n---\\n\\n #### Path parameters\\n\\n * id string\\n\\n---\\n\\n #### Request parameters\\n\\n * hog_function_ids array\\n\\n---\\n\\n #### Example request\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Metrics API Reference - PostHog\\nURL: https://posthog.com/docs/api/metrics\\n\\n\\n Show response body   \\n #### Example request\\n\\n `POST`   `/api  /projects  /:project_id  /metrics  /samples`  cURL  PostHog AI    \\n```\\nexport POSTHOG_PERSONAL_API_KEY=[your personal api key]    curl         -H 'Content-Type: application/json'\\\\        -H \\\"Authorization: Bearer $POSTHOG_PERSONAL_API_KEY\\\" \\\\        <ph_app_host>/api/projects/:project_id/metrics/samples/\\\\    \\t-d query=undefined\\n```\\n \\n```\\napi_key = \\\"[your personal api key]\\\"    project_id = \\\"[your project id]\\\"    response = requests.post(        \\\"<ph_app_host>/api/projects/{project_id}/metrics/samples/\\\".format(            project_id=project_id        ),        headers={\\\"Authorization\\\": \\\"Bearer {}\\\".format(api_key)},    \\tdata={}    ).json()\\n```\\n #### Example response\\n\\n ##### Status 200\\n\\n RESPONSE PostHog AI  \\n```\\n{      \\\"results\\\": [        {          \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"string\\\",          \\\"metric_name\\\": \\\"string\\\",          \\\"metric_type\\\": \\\"string\\\",          \\\"value\\\": 0.1,          \\\"count\\\": 0,          \\\"unit\\\": \\\"string\\\",          \\\"aggregation_temporality\\\": \\\"string\\\",          \\\"is_monotonic\\\": true,          \\\"service_name\\\": \\\"string\\\",          \\\"trace_id\\\": \\\"string\\\",          \\\"span_id\\\": \\\"string\\\",          \\\"attributes\\\": {            \\\"property1\\\": \\\"string\\\",            \\\"property2\\\": \\\"string\\\"          },          \\\"resource_attributes\\\": {            \\\"property1\\\": \\\"string\\\",            \\\"property2\\\": \\\"string\\\"          }        }      ]    }\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n ##  Create metrics samples\\n\\n Raw individual emissions for a metric (the events model), newest\\nfirst — backs the Samples view and the metric->trace pivot.\\n\\n #### Required API key scopes\\n\\n `metrics:read` \\n\\n---\\n\\n #### Request parameters\\n\\n * query\\n\\n---\\n\\n #### Response\\n\\n Show response body   \""}],"isError":false,"_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"PostHog","version":"1.0.0"}}},"duration":{"secs":9,"nanos":233835125}},"started_at_ms":1791374951333,"completed_at_ms":1791374960567}}
